{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44534": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Position - Exercise Science & Kinesiology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees. Introduction The University of South Florida College of Education serves a community of over 2,200 students and 130 faculty members dedicated to advancing high-quality education through excellence in research, teaching, and learning. Accredited by the Council for the Accreditation of Educator Preparation (CAEP) and fully approved by the Florida Department of Education, the College offers innovative teacher training and collaborative graduate programs aimed at developing educational leaders. In partnership with school districts across the Tampa Bay region, the College is committed to extending proven educational initiatives and exploring new approaches to preparing lifelong learners. Whether pursuing initial teaching certification or advancing professional development through graduate studies, the College provides comprehensive resources and support to help students achieve their educational and career goals. Job Description The University of South Florida (USF), a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), invites applications for an open-rank (Assistant, Associate, and Full Professor) faculty position in Exercise Science & Kinesiology within the College of Education. USF seeks a nationally and internationally recognized or rapidly rising scholar with a strong record of research excellence and demonstrated success securing competitive external funding. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued growth and national prominence of Exercise Science & Kinesiology at USF by developing and sustaining an impactful, externally funded research program. This position represents a significant strategic investment in expanding the research profile, external funding portfolio, and scholarly impact of Exercise Science & Kinesiology. Particular interest will be given to candidates with a demonstrated record of securing substantial competitive external funding and leading impactful research programs. Candidates with experience serving as Principal Investigator on major federal grants are especially encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will build a productive research program while creating opportunities for colleagues and students to develop their scholarship and compete for external funding. Required Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in Exercise Science, Kinesiology, or a related discipline from an accredited institution. Demonstrated record of scholarly productivity and an active research agenda related to Exercise Science & Kinesiology and consistent with appointment at a research-intensive university. Demonstrated success securing competitive external research funding, or strong potential appropriate to career stage. Demonstrated ability to contribute effectively to collaborative and interdisciplinary research environments. Evidence of effective teaching, mentorship, and engagement in academic programs, or demonstrated potential in these areas. Candidates seeking appointment at the Associate Professor or Professor level must demonstrate sustained scholarly productivity, substantive leadership on externally funded research, and national or international recognition commensurate with the proposed rank. Appointment rank and tenure status will be determined in accordance with University policies and the approved position authorization. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate: Sustained success securing significant competitive external research funding as Principal Investigator or equivalent research leader, including federal funding where applicable. Evidence of successfully developing, expanding, or sustaining an externally funded program of research. National or international recognition for research excellence and impact. Demonstrated leadership of interdisciplinary research teams, laboratories, centers, institutes, or collaborative research initiatives. A compelling vision for expanding externally funded research, fostering interdisciplinary collaboration, and enhancing the national prominence of Exercise Science & Kinesiology at USF. Research Opportunity at USF USF’s academic and health enterprise offers opportunities for collaboration across education, artificial intelligence and computing, engineering, medicine, public health, rehabilitation, data science, and technology. The successful candidate will help develop a sustained area of research strength that draws on these complementary capabilities and expands opportunities for faculty and graduate students. This position provides an opportunity to strengthen existing areas of excellence in our program while establishing new directions for research and collaboration. The successful candidate will play an important role in expanding the program's external research portfolio, mentoring the next generation of scholars, building interdisciplinary partnerships, and elevating the national and international visibility of Exercise Science & Kinesiology at USF. Candidates should be positioned to pursue sustained competitive funding from National Institutes of Health (NIH), Department of Defense (DOD), or other federal agencies, foundations, or research partnerships appropriate to their agenda. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin on November 12, 2006 and continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, candidates are encouraged to apply by November 16. Applications should be submitted through Careers@USF - Job ID 44534 and include the following materials: Cover letter with contact information, the rank sought, and a description of the candidate’s fit with this position. Full curriculum vitae. Research statement describing major scholarly contributions, competitive external funding and the candidate’s role in securing it, and a vision for building an interdisciplinary, externally funded research program at USF. Teaching and mentoring statement describing the candidate’s approach to graduate education, mentoring, and student success. Names and contact information for 3 professional references. For additional information about the USF College of Education, visit https://www.usf.edu/education/ Position Overview Exercise Science & Kinesiology encompasses a broad and interdisciplinary scientific landscape focused on understanding human movement, physical activity and health, exercise, and performance across the lifespan. The successful candidate will contribute an innovative research program that complements and expands the existing strengths of the program while creating new opportunities for externally funded research and interdisciplinary collaboration. The area of scholarly expertise is intentionally open. Relevant areas may include, but are not limited to: Exercise physiology Skeletal muscle physiology and biology Sport and human performance Biomechanics and motor control Physical activity and health Exercise and chronic disease prevention or management Metabolism, obesity, and body composition Aging and exercise Cardiovascular or metabolic physiology Nutrition and exercise Behavioral aspects of physical activity and exercise Wearable technology and human performance monitoring Data science, artificial intelligence, and emerging technologies applied to human movement, exercise, or health Other areas relevant to exercise science, kinesiology, human performance, or physical activity Candidates may employ laboratory-based, clinical, translational, community-based, epidemiological, computational, or other rigorous approaches. Responsibilities and Expectations Develop and sustain a nationally and internationally prominent research program. Secure substantial competitive external funding from federal agencies, foundations, industry, and/or other sponsors. Serve as Principal Investigator and provide leadership for externally funded research initiatives. Pursue interdisciplinary and collaborative research opportunities within USF and with external partners. Publish influential scholarship in leading peer-reviewed journals and other high-impact scholarly outlets. Mentor graduate and undergraduate students and contribute to the development of the next generation of researchers and scholars. Contribute to the academic mission of the Exercise Science & Kinesiology program through teaching and service appropriate to rank. Build productive collaborations across departments, colleges, research centers, healthcare systems, community organizations, industry, and other external partners. Enhance the national and international visibility of Exercise Science & Kinesiology at USF. Engage in the Exercise Science and Kinesiology program. Assistant, Associate Professors, and Professors in the Department of Educational & Psychological Studies at the USF College of Education are responsible to a Chair or to other appropriate administrators of a state university. Assistant, Associate Professors, and Professors are responsible for teaching, research, service and related administrative activities and for academic advising. Assistant, Associate Professors, and Professors may represent the University, College, or Department on university and/or statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44541": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Position in Special Education and Emerging Technologies",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees. The University of South Florida (USF), a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), invites applications for an open-rank (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor) faculty position to lead and expand a strategic research area focused on Special Education and Emerging Technologies. USF seeks a nationally and internationally recognized or rising scholar who will sustain a nationally recognized, externally funded research program, lead interdisciplinary collaborations, and mentor faculty and graduate students. This position represents a significant institutional investment to establish a nationally visible, externally funded research enterprise focused on the development and implementation of approaches designed to improve educational access and meaningful outcomes for individuals with disabilities. Candidates with experience serving as Principal Investigators on federal grants are especially encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will build a productive research program while creating opportunities for colleagues and students to develop their scholarship and compete for external funding. Job Description The University of South Florida College of Education serves a community of over 2,200 students and 130 faculty members dedicated to advancing high-quality education through excellence in research, teaching, and learning. Accredited by the Council for the Accreditation of Educator Preparation (CAEP) and fully approved by the Florida Department of Education, the College offers innovative teacher training and collaborative graduate programs aimed at developing educational leaders. In partnership with school districts across the Tampa Bay region, the College is committed to extending proven educational initiatives and exploring new approaches to preparing lifelong learners. Whether pursuing initial teaching certification or advancing professional development through graduate studies, the College provides comprehensive resources and support to help students achieve their educational and career goals. Required Qualifications An earned doctorate in Special Education or a closely related discipline. A record of peer-reviewed scholarship and research achievement appropriate to the rank at a research-intensive university. An active research agenda focused on special education or disability that aligns with accessibility and emerging technologies. Evidence of success in securing competitive external research funding, or strong potential appropriate to career stage. Evidence of effective graduate mentorship or the capacity to mentor graduate students. Evidence of successful interdisciplinary collaboration or the capacity to contribute substantively to collaborative research teams. Candidates seeking appointment at the Associate Professor or Professor level must demonstrate sustained scholarly productivity, substantive leadership on externally funded research, and national or international recognition commensurate with the proposed rank. Appointment rank and tenure status will be determined in accordance with University policies and the approved position authorization. Preferred Qualifications A sustained record of competitive external funding as Principal Investigator, Co-Principal Investigator, or another role demonstrating substantial intellectual leadership. Experience securing federal research awards and developing a coherent program of research across successive projects. Evidence of successful faculty mentorship, such as collaborative publications, funded proposals, or colleagues’ development as research leaders. Experience building interdisciplinary teams, research programs, laboratories, centers, or multi-institutional partnerships. Research integrating accessible or emerging technologies with rigorous evaluation of interventions, implementation, or educational outcomes. Research expertise in literacy or other critical areas of special education, particularly where such expertise supports the development of externally funded research programs. Experience conducting research in authentic educational or community settings and translating findings into usable practices, tools, or policy. Research Opportunity at USF USF’s academic and health enterprise offers opportunities for collaboration across education, artificial intelligence and computing, engineering, psychology, communication sciences and disorders, behavioral and community sciences, and health-related disciplines. The successful candidate will help develop a sustained area of research strength that draws on these complementary capabilities and expands opportunities for faculty and graduate students. Candidates should be positioned to pursue sustained competitive funding from IES/NCSER, NSF, NIH, other federal programs, foundations, or research partnerships appropriate to their agenda. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin on November 16, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, candidates are encouraged to apply by November 16, 2026. Applications should be submitted through Careers@USF - Job ID 44541 and include the following materials: Cover letter with contact information, the rank sought, and a description of the candidate’s fit with this position. Full curriculum vitae. Research statement describing major scholarly contributions, competitive external funding and the candidate’s role in securing it, and a vision for building an interdisciplinary, externally funded research program at USF. Teaching and mentoring statement describing the candidate’s approach to graduate education, mentoring, and student success. Names and contact information for 3 professional references. For additional information about the USF College of Education, visit https://www.usf.edu/education/ Responsibilities Assistant/Associate/Professors in the Department of Language, Literacy, Ed.D., Exceptional Education, and Physical Education (LLEEP) at the USF College of Education are responsible to a Chair or to other appropriate administrators of a state university. Assistant/Associate/Professors are responsible for teaching, research, service and related administrative activities and for academic advising. Assistant/Associate/Professors may represent the University, College, or Department on university and/or statewide committees. Research Focus We welcome scholars whose research connects special education, accessibility, and emerging technologies with rigorous intervention, assessment, implementation, or systems research. Artificial intelligence, assistive technologies, adaptive systems, and other emerging technologies are particularly relevant areas of interest. Candidates may bring an established technology-focused research program or a compelling agenda for integrating emerging technologies through substantive interdisciplinary collaboration. We are particularly interested in research that examines whether, how, for whom, and under what conditions interventions and innovations improve outcomes. Relevant areas may include one or more of the following: Academic, behavioral, and communication interventions, including intensive literacy and mathematics intervention. Accessible and assistive technologies, including AI-enabled tools, adaptive learning, augmentative and alternative communication, and Universal Design for Learning. Immersive and interactive learning environments, including virtual, augmented, and mixed reality, simulations, and other emerging technologies. Assessment, progress monitoring, data-based individualization, and decision-making. Special education workforce preparation, professional learning, and development. Implementation, adaptation, and scaling of effective practices. These examples are illustrative. Candidates should demonstrate a coherent research program with a clear focus on individuals with disabilities and a credible contribution to the position’s emphasis on educational access and emerging technologies. Expectations The successful candidate will be expected to: Develop and sustain a nationally visible research program that produces influential scholarship and meaningful improvements in outcomes for individuals with disabilities. Secure competitive external research funding and provide substantive intellectual leadership on funded projects. Conduct rigorous research appropriate to the questions under study, including development, intervention, efficacy, effectiveness, measurement, implementation, or systems research. Build interdisciplinary research teams and collaborative funding initiatives across the College and University. Mentor faculty and emerging researchers in developing research programs, preparing competitive grant proposals, and leading collaborative projects. Mentor doctoral students, postdoctoral fellows, and other and early career scholars and contribute to the preparation of future researchers and teacher educators. Develop sustained partnerships with schools, districts, agencies, disability organizations, individuals with disabilities and their families, technology developers, and other relevant stakeholders. Translate findings into practices, interventions, accessible tools, resources, or policy that can be used in educational and community settings. Contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching and University service in a manner appropriate to rank and the responsibilities of the appointment."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44546": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty Position Future of Work and Emerging Technologies",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees. The University of South Florida (USF), a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), invites applications for an open-rank (Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor) faculty position to lead and expand a strategic research area focused on the Future of Work and Emerging Technologies. USF seeks a nationally and internationally recognized or rising scholar whose work is reshaping how individuals, organizations, educational institutions, and communities prepare for and thrive in a workforce transformed by artificial intelligence and technological innovation. This position represents a significant institutional investment intended to establish a nationally and internationally visible, externally funded research enterprise focused on the future of learning, work, emerging technologies, economic opportunity, and workforce development. Particular interest will be given to candidates with a demonstrated record of securing competitive external funding and leading impactful research programs. Candidates with experience serving as Principal Investigator on federal grants are especially encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will build a productive research program while creating opportunities for colleagues and students to develop their scholarship and compete for external funding. Required Qualifications Earned doctoral degree in appropriate discipline. Demonstrated record of strong publication in high-quality scholarly venues related to work and learning, workforce development, emerging technologies, economic opportunity, or area relevant to the future of work and emerging technologies that is consistent with appointment at a research-intensive university. Documented record of successfully securing competitive external funding or strong potential, appropriate to career stage. Demonstrated capacity to work effectively in interdisciplinary environments. Candidates seeking appointment at the Associate Professor or Professor level must demonstrate sustained scholarly productivity, substantive leadership on externally funded research, and national or international recognition commensurate with the proposed rank. Appointment rank and tenure status will be determined in accordance with University policies and the approved position authorization. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate: Sustained success obtaining significant competitive external funding as Principal Investigator or equivalent research leader. National or international recognition for research excellence. Experience leading interdisciplinary research centers, laboratories, institutes, or large collaborative projects. Success building partnerships with industry, government agencies, educational systems, workforce organizations, or community partners. Experience translating research into policy, practice, products, or measurable societal impact. Evidence of, or commitment to effective teaching and mentoring of graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and/or early career scholars. A compelling vision for building a high-impact Future of Work and Emerging Technologies research enterprise at USF. Strategic Opportunity USF is seeking more than a faculty member. We seek an entrepreneurial research leader who can shape a signature area of excellence at a major AAU institution. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to build collaborative initiatives across education, business, engineering, computer science, public policy, health, and other disciplines while developing a nationally recognized center of scholarship focused on the future of learning, work, emerging technologies, and economic mobility. Application Instructions Review of applications will begin on November 12, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. To ensure full consideration, candidates are encouraged to apply by November 12, 2026. Applications should be submitted through https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/ . Please specify Position # 330147242 on all submitted documents and include the following materials: 1. Cover letter that describes candidate’s interest in the position and specifically addresses how the candidate’s background, accomplishments, and future plans align with the required qualifications and preferred qualifications. 2. Full curriculum vitae. 3. Research statement describing major scholarly contributions, competitive external funding and the candidate’s role in securing it, and a vision for building an interdisciplinary, externally funded Future of Work and Emerging Technologies research program at USF. 4. Names and contact information for 3 professional references. For additional information about the USF College of Education, visit https://www.usf.edu/education/ Position Overview Artificial intelligence, automation, digital transformation, and emerging technologies are rapidly changing the nature of work and learning. The successful candidate will play a leadership role in building an innovative and forward-looking research agenda that examines how educational systems, workforce development organizations, employers, and policymakers can prepare individuals for evolving careers while promoting economic mobility and expanding access to opportunity. Relevant areas of scholarship may include, but are not limited to: Future of work Artificial intelligence and workforce transformation Human-AI collaboration Workforce development and workforce policy Career pathways and talent development Credentials, microcredentials, and alternative pathways Skills acquisition, reskilling, and upskilling Adult learning and lifelong learning Experiential and work-based learning Community college and workforce partnerships Industry-education collaborations Labor market analytics and workforce alignment Technology-enabled learning and training systems Economic mobility and workforce success Emerging technologies and human capital development Candidates may come from a wide range of disciplines, including education, workforce development, labor economics, information science, learning sciences, human resource development, human-computer interaction, computer science, engineering, or related fields. Expectations The successful candidate will: Develop and sustain a nationally and internationally prominent research program. Secure substantial competitive external funding from federal agencies, foundations, industry, and other sponsors. Serve as Principal Investigator and provide leadership for externally funded research initiatives. Pursue large-scale interdisciplinary and collaborative research initiatives within USF and with external partners. Publish influential scholarship in leading peer-reviewed journals and other high-impact scholarly outlets. Teach graduate level courses. Mentor graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, and/or early-career scholars and contribute to the development of the next generation of researchers and scholars. Build productive partnerships with workforce organizations, employers, educational institutions, policymakers, and other external partners. Collaborate broadly across the University and with external partners. Help establish USF as a national and international leader in workforce innovation, technology, and economic mobility research. Particular emphasis will be placed on a candidate's ability and potential to attract major investments through programs supported by agencies and organizations such as: National Science Foundation (NSF) Institute of Education Sciences (IES) U.S. Department of Labor Department of Commerce Department of Defense National Institutes of Health Major national and regional foundations Industry-sponsored research partnerships"
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44526": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction/Assistant Instructor & Field Coordinator",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/01/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States Established in 2008, the College of Behavioral & Community Sciences is breaking new ground by combining knowledge gained through the behavioral sciences with knowledge gained from the community. The College serves approximately 3,100 students with seven undergraduate, 14 master's, and seven doctoral programs housed in six academic departments/schools. The University of South Florida, School of Social Work invites applications for a Field Coordinator & Assistant Professor of Instruction/Assistant Instructor position. This is a 12-month continual appointment, subject to annual evaluations. Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience. Promotional opportunities are provided in accordance with the University of South Florida – Tampa, Career Path for Instructors: Promotion Guidelines. Social work faculty members contribute to the mission of the College by preparing professional social workers for evidence based social work practice and a lifelong engagement in social justice advocacy. Candidates should demonstrate strong cultural competence. Leadership, communication, initiative, and organizational and interpersonal skills necessary for effective collaboration with a diverse community of students, faculty, staff, and external constituents. Please see the following website for additional information about the University of South Florida and the School of Social Work: http://socialwork.cbcs.usf.edu/ As part of the College of Behavioral and Community Sciences, members of our faculty engage in innovative interdisciplinary, translational, and implementation research focusing on finding solutions to promote the quality of life, health and the safety of diverse populations and communities. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . Minimum Qualifications: MSW from a CSWE-accredited social work program. Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience in social work higher education. Administrative experience in social work, education and/or leadership in a human service agency. Two years of full-time or the equivalent of part-time post-graduate social work practice experience. Experience in field education for example, creating and developing community partnerships, coordinating student placements, and providing oversight of students throughout the field placement process. Face-to-Face and Online teaching experience in social work education. Demonstrate an ability to problem-solve and prioritize tasks. Experience with competency-based standards. Supervisory experience with students or staff. Social work state licensure in any state, State of Florida preferred. Criteria for the evaluation of candidates To ensure the fair and equitable evaluation of all candidates, the following criteria will be used in reviewing the applicants’ qualifications. Ranges for rating the criteria are weighted in terms of importance to the position. Applicants are required to submit the following in support of their application: Cover Letter CV 2 Letters of Recommendation (these can be collected as part of the application process or at a later date by the HR Coordinator, but before any verbal/soft offer is made) The position will be responsible for the recruitment of new community partners, continued engagement with current community partners, and the student field placement process in coordination with the Director of Field Education. The position is dedicated to providing instruction in both the BSW and MSW programs and contributing to the service needs in the School, including the admissions process, advising and other duties."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44493": {
      "title": "Neonatal NP - Per Diem - Pediatrics",
      "description": "Closing Date: 06/04/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Health Care JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. Learn more at www.usf.edu . The APRN will act following Florida Statutes for the Nurse Practitioners Act. The care and management of critically ill infants requiring hospitalization in a level IV neonatal intensive care unit. This NICU Nurse Practitioner will cover night and/or day shifts as assigned including weekend coverage. The Neonatal Intensive Care Unit is based at Tampa General Hospital (TGH) in Tampa, FL. TGH is a 1,018-bed teaching hospital affiliated with the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine. It is a private not-for-profit hospital and one of the most comprehensive medical facilities in west central Florida, serving a dozen counties with a population of over 4 million. In addition to being a level one trauma center, it has a level 3 NICU. The 82-bed Jennifer Leigh Muma NICU is a designated Regional Perinatal Intensive Care Center designated by the State of Florida to deliver the highest level of medical care to premature and sick infants, and to women with high-risk pregnancies. USF/TGH Neonatology also participates in the Florida Perinatal Quality Collaborative, a statewide initiative to improve maternal and infant health outcomes in Florida. Master's or Medical degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor Master's Degree in Nursing: ARNP training; Florida License. BLS/AED certification is required and must be maintained. Any equivalent combination of experience and education. This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Clinical - Ongoing evaluation and management of neonates and infants requiring care in the neonatal intensive care unit, participation in multidisciplinary rounds, and coordination of care with ancillary staff and family. Attendance at high-risk deliveries and immediate stabilization of critically ill neonates under the supervision of the attending Neonatologist. Documentation of all orders, procedures, and progress notes on the patient's medical record. Perform procedures necessary for the care of neonates and infants in the intensive care unit including endotracheal intubation, umbilical line placement, PICC line placement, lumbar punctures, and peripheral arterial lines. Teaching - Supervision of pediatric residents and participation in the teaching of pediatric residents and medical students. Other - Participation in Quality Assurance / Improvement. Performs other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44502": {
      "title": "APRN/PA - Byrd Institute- Instructor I",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/04/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. Learn more at www.usf.edu . The department of Psychiatry is seeking an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) to join its clinical team at the Byrd Alzheimer's Institute and Memory Disorder Clinics. This position will provide outpatient clinical care to patients to include the diagnosis, treatment and management of adult patients with mental and/or behavioral health conditions. Completes clinical documentation, responds to messages and telephone calls, performs other clinical administrative tasks. This position will also support the clinical research mission through various clinical trial work. Master's or Medical degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Clinical - Provides outpatient medication management to include the diagnosis, treatment and management of adult patients with mental and/or behavioral health conditions. Completes clinical documentation, responds to messages and telephone calls, performs other clinical administrative tasks. Research - Supports the clinical trials mission of the division; Prepares data for collection and reporting; Performs study interventions according to protocol; Completes study training and related reporting. Performs other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, service, and related activities. May be responsible for research and/or academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44508": {
      "title": "Physician Asst/Instructor. I - Plastic Surgery",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/04/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . The Advanced Practice Provider (APP) in the Department of Plastic Surgery is responsible for delivering high-quality, patient-centered care across the continuum of reconstructive and aesthetic plastic surgery services. Working collaboratively with plastic surgeons, residents, nurses, and multidisciplinary teams, the APP provides comprehensive outpatient and inpatient clinical management, perioperative care, first-assist support in the operating room, and patient education. This position plays a critical role in improving patient access, enhancing surgical efficiency, optimizing clinical outcomes, and supporting the academic, research, and educational missions of USF Health while maintaining the highest standards of quality, safety, and compassionate care. Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Degree Equivalency Clause: Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree. • Senate Bill 1310- The Florida Senate (https://www.flsenate.gov/Session/Bill/2023/1310) is conditional upon meeting all employment eligibility requirements in the U.S. • SB 1310: Substitution of Work Experience for Postsecondary Education Requirements • A public employer may include a postsecondary degree as a baseline requirement only as an alternative to the number of years of direct experience required, not to exceed: • (a) Two years of direct experience for an associate degree; • (b) Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree; • (c) Six years of direct experience for a master’s degree; • (d) Seven years of direct experience for a professional degree; or • (e) Nine years of direct experience for a doctoral degree • Related work experience may not substitute for any required licensure, certification, or registration required for the position of employment as established by the public employer and indicated in the advertised description of the position of employment. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . Clinical - Perform comprehensive patient assessments, including medical history, physical examinations, and documentation for reconstructive and aesthetic plastic surgery patients. Evaluate new and established patients in both outpatient clinic and inpatient settings. Develop, implement, and modify treatment plans in collaboration with supervising plastic surgeons. Order, interpret, and communicate laboratory, radiographic, and diagnostic test results. Perform preoperative evaluations and surgical clearances within scope of practice. Provide postoperative care, including wound assessments, drain management, dressing changes, splinting, and suture/staple removal. Diagnose and manage common postoperative complications, escalating care to the attending surgeon as appropriate. Assist in the operating room as First Assist, including tissue handling, exposure, retraction, hemostasis, suturing, and wound closure. Performs other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, service, and related activities. May be responsible for research and/or academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44497": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The University of South Florida’s (USF) Muma College of Business invites applications for the tenure-track position of Assistant Professor in the Vinik Sport & Entertainment Management Program within the School of Hospitality and Sport Management. Position will remain open until filled and review of applications will begin October 19, 2026. The University of South Florida’s (USF) Muma College of Business invites applications for the tenure-track position of Assistant Professor in the Vinik Sport and Entertainment Management Program within the School of Hospitality and Sport Management. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Sport Management or another related business discipline from an accredited university or expect to complete such a Ph.D. by Summer 2027. Professional work experience in a sport or entertainment business environment is also highly recommended. Applications are welcomed from all sport and entertainment business areas. Ideal candidates will target and publish in the most prestigious sport and/or business journals and demonstrate excellence in teaching. Candidates with experience and interest in teaching using innovative technology are encouraged to apply. This is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track position. The Vinik Sport & Entertainment Management Program (VSEM) ranks #2 in the world and #1 in Florida among sport and entertainment management programs. Students in this two-year Tampa-based graduate program earn both an MBA in Sport Business and an M.S. in Sport & Entertainment Management, while achieving nearly a 100% placement rate post-graduation. Undergraduate students may pursue a minor in sport business. VSEM enjoys strong partnerships with major sports and entertainment properties in the region, e.g., Tampa Bay Lightning, Tampa Bay Buccaneers, Tampa Bay Rays, Fanatics, and Seminole Hard Rock Casino. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Sport Business/Management/Administration from an AACSB (or international equivalent) accredited institution or a Ph.D. in other related disciplines before the start of employment. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Primary Considerations: Evidence of ability or potential to publish in top-level journals in sport and/or business. Evidence of superior teaching ability. Overall quality of the candidate as indicated by letters of reference and personal contacts. Other Considerations: Professional work experience in a Sport and/or Entertainment business environment. Evidence of ability to teach Sport and/or Entertainment Management related courses at the graduate and undergraduate levels. Evidence of teaching using innovative technology. Evidence of ability to make service contributions to the university and the profession. Evidence of partnering with sport and entertainment properties to provide students experiential-learning opportunities. Expectation that the candidate will be collegial. Reputation of program granting the candidate’s degree. Reputation of program(s) where candidate might have been employed previously. Interest in applying for externally funded research. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44503": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction/Assistant Instructor",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States Established in 2008, the College of Behavioral & Community Sciences is breaking new ground by combining knowledge gained through the behavioral sciences with knowledge gained from the community. The College serves approximately 3,100 students with seven undergraduate, 14 master's, and seven doctoral programs housed in six academic departments/schools. Position Description: The University of South Florida, School of Social Work invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Instruction/Assistant Instructor. This position is based on the Tampa campus. Term of appointment shall be 12 months continual appointment subject to annual evaluations. Salary is commensurate with experience. Promotional opportunities are provided in accordance with University of South Florida Career Path for Instructors: Promotion Guidelines. Social work faculty members contribute to the mission of the College by preparing professional social workers for social work practice, evidence based social work practice and social justice. Candidates should demonstrate strong cultural humility, verbal communication and interpersonal skills necessary for effective collaboration with a diverse community of students, faculty, staff, and external constituents. https://www.usf.edu/cbcs/social-work/ The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . Minimum Qualifications: MSW from a CSWE-accredited social work program. Preferred Qualifications: Two years of post-MSW professional social work practice experience or equivalent relevant professional experience. Doctorate in Social Work (PhD or DSW) or a related field and/or current LCSW or equivalent clinical licensure. Demonstrated ability to teach across multiple areas of the social work curriculum, with particular interest in candidates capable of teaching both practice and research/data-informed courses. Experience developing, implementing, or evaluating simulation-based education, including standardized clients/patients, role-play, virtual simulation, immersive learning, or other experiential learning approaches. Experience using artificial intelligence or emerging technologies in social work education, practice, research, or evaluation, including attention to ethical, responsible, and critically informed use. Experience integrating AI literacy, data literacy, or digital practice competencies into teaching and learning. Experience with innovative pedagogy, such as competency-based education, experiential learning, flipped classrooms, case-based learning, team-based learning, or authentic assessment. Experience designing or evaluating educational innovations, including scholarship of teaching and learning, implementation research, simulation research, or educational evaluation. Demonstrated ability to translate social work research and evidence into applied practice instruction. Experience teaching across face-to-face, online, hybrid, and/or technology-enhanced modalities. Experience collaborating across disciplines or professions, interprofessional Criteria for the evaluation of candidates To ensure the fair and equitable evaluation of all candidates, the following criteria will be used in reviewing the applicants’ qualifications. Ranges for rating the criteria are weighted in terms of importance to the position. Applicants are required to submit the following in support of their application: Cover Letter CV Teaching Philosophy and Innovation Statement (2-3 pages) Candidates should describe their overall approach to teaching and preparing students for contemporary social work practice. The statement should address: Approaches to engaging students and supporting competency development Ability and interest in teaching across multiple areas of the BSW and/or MSW curriculum Use of experiential, simulation-based, or other innovative teaching strategies Experience with or perspectives on the ethical and responsible integration of artificial intelligence, emerging technologies, and/or data-informed approaches in social work education and practice How the candidate connects classroom learning with real-world social work practice and evolving workforce needs. practice, and evolving workforce needs. This position is dedicated to providing instruction in the BSW and MSW programs and contributing to the service needs in the School."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44494": {
      "title": "Research Associate Dr. Wang Lab",
      "description": "Closing Date: 03/01/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Faculty - Other JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. Minimum: Ph.D., M.D./Ph.D., or equivalent doctoral degree from an accredited institution in physiology, molecular biology, cell biology, biomedical sciences, or a related field. Appropriate research experience and training in molecular, cellular, or animal physiology. .Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Research Associate. Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English. Strong organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills. Ability to work both independently and effectively as part of a multidisciplinary research team. Preferred: Experience with Rodent microsurgery, kidney injury models, or organ transplantation models is highly desirable. Experience with one or more of the following is preferred. Western Blotting. immunoprecipitation Primary cell culture, Confocal microscopy, Single cell RNA sequencing, Proteomics, bioinformatics, or neonatology. Experience with renal physiology, Ischemia-reperfusion injury, regulated cell death, transplantation or related area is a plus. Strong record of scientific productivity and demonstrated the ability to conduct research independently and. collaboratively ​‌ "
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42451": {
      "title": "CRNA Assistant /Associate Professor Non-Tenure Track",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physicians’ Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The USF Health College of Nursing is one of 14 colleges at the University of South Florida and one of four that make up USF Health. As a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities, USF is designated by the Carnegie Foundation as both a Research 1 and a Community-Engaged institution, reflecting its commitment to excellence in education, research, and service. Nationally recognized as a leader in nursing education and research, the College of Nursing serves more than 2,000 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students each year. For the fourth consecutive year, our Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) program has been ranked No. 1 among Florida’s public universities by U.S. News & World Report—rising to No. 23 in the nation in 2025. As an integral part of USF Health, the College of Nursing is guided by a mission grounded in excellence, innovation, and respect. We are dedicated to educating future nurses, advancing nursing science, and applying evidence-based practice to improve health outcomes and community well-being. SUMMARY: This non-tenure-earning faculty position will teach in the CRNA Program, engage in scholarly activity, mentor graduate nursing students, and contribute to college, university, community, and professional service in alignment with the university’s criteria for appointment at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank. Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization. Must meet university criteria for appointment at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor (non-tenure earning). Additional Minimum Qualifications: Must hold, or be eligible for, licensure as an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) in the state of Florida by the start date. Must hold national certification as a Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist (CRNA). Current clinical practice as a CRNA/APRN in the state of Florida. Preferred Qualifications: Minimum of one year of post-secondary teaching experience in a college or school of nursing. Demonstrated expertise in teaching and developing curriculum in pharmacology, physiology, pathophysiology, and nurse anesthesia–related courses. Experience with technology-supported educational methods, including online and blended formats •Demonstrated ability to work effectively with community partners. Established record of scholarly work and/or external funding. Experience with simulation-based learning. Evidence of independent and collaborative scholarship or creative work, supported by publications, presentations, and/or equivalent contributions. The faculty member will be responsible for teaching didactic, lab, and clinical residency courses within the CRNA Program, utilizing a variety of instructional methods. Additional responsibilities include participating in program and curriculum review and conducting student and clinical site evaluations, as appropriate. The faculty member will also serve on college and university committees, contribute to community and professional service activities, and engage in scholarly work through publications and presentations consistent with university expectations for the assistant professor rank. In-person presence during standard business hours is required; remote work is not available for this position"
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42755": {
      "title": "Assistant/Assoc. Professor, Non-Tenure Track",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physicians’ Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The USF Health College of Nursing is one of 14 colleges at the University of South Florida and one of four that make up USF Health. As a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities, USF is designated by the Carnegie Foundation as both a Research 1 and a Community-Engaged institution, reflecting its commitment to excellence in education, research, and service. Nationally recognized as a leader in nursing education and research, the College of Nursing serves more than 2,000 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students each year. For the fourth consecutive year, our Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) program has been ranked No. 1 among Florida’s public universities by U.S. News & World Report—rising to No. 23 in the nation in 2025. As an integral part of USF Health, the College of Nursing is guided by a mission grounded in excellence, innovation, and respect. We are dedicated to educating future nurses, advancing nursing science, and applying evidence-based practice to improve health outcomes and community well-being. Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor (non-tenure earning). Additional Minimum Qualifications: Must hold, or be eligible for, licensure as a Registered Nurse (RN) or Advanced Practice Registered Nursing (APRN) in the state of Florida by the start date. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with curriculum development and accreditation processes. Strong leadership, communication, and organizational skills. Demonstrated record of grant writing and/or research in nursing healthcare leadership. This full-time, onsite faculty position at the USF College of Nursing involves teaching in undergraduate and/or graduate programs, mentoring students, and participating in service activities. The role may include travel to clinical sites and teaching across the Tampa, St. Petersburg, or Sarasota-Manatee campuses. Responsibilities include delivering didactic, clinical, lab, and online instruction; engaging in curriculum and clinical site evaluation; conducting scholarly work; and contributing to college, university, and professional service consistent with the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. In-person presence during standard business hours is required. Remote work option is not available for this position."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42979": {
      "title": "Open Rank Vascular",
      "description": "Closing Date: 31/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of Surgery at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking a Open Rank to Perform all aspects of Vascular surgery. Applicants that have completed Vascular surgery residency and demonstrated experience in surgical education, research, and patient care. Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. Candidates must be Board Certified/Board Eligible. PREFERRED: Certified (or eligible for certification according to current requirements) by the American Board of Surgery or American Osteopathic Board of Surgery in Surgery, with Added Qualifications in Vascular Surgery. Demonstrated proficiency in the field of Vascular Surgery. Demonstrated commitment to teaching health care professional students, residents, and practicing clinicians Successfully complete program requirements of ACGME institutional and residency/fellowship. Direct supervision of residents. Responsible (with authority) for all aspects of the Vascular Program to include call panel privileges, treatment protocols and guidelines, service policies, education, community outreach, hospital executive interface, and performance improvement; promotes multidisciplinary approach to care. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State University. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43082": {
      "title": "Instructor 1",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physicians’ Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The USF Health College of Nursing is one of 14 colleges at the University of South Florida and one of four that make up USF Health. As a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities, USF is designated by the Carnegie Foundation as both a Research 1 and a Community-Engaged institution, reflecting its commitment to excellence in education, research, and service. Nationally recognized as a leader in nursing education and research, the College of Nursing serves more than 2,000 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students each year. For the fourth consecutive year, our Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) program has been ranked No. 1 among Florida’s public universities by U.S. News & World Report—rising to No. 23 in the nation in 2025. As an integral part of USF Health, the College of Nursing is guided by a mission grounded in excellence, innovation, and respect. We are dedicated to educating future nurses, advancing nursing science, and applying evidence-based practice to improve health outcomes and community well-being. The USF College of Nursing is seeking a full-time, non-tenure-track Instructor I to join its clinical/teaching faculty. The primary focus is undergraduate instruction, with responsibilities that may include graduate-level teaching, mentoring students, serving on committees, participating in community engagement, and acting as a liaison with clinical sites (which may require travel). Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. Degree Equivalency Clause: Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree. • Senate Bill 1310- The Florida Senate (https://www.flsenate.gov/Session/Bill/2023/1310) is conditional upon meeting all employment eligibility requirements in the U.S. • SB 1310: Substitution of Work Experience for Postsecondary Education Requirements • A public employer may include a postsecondary degree as a baseline requirement only as an alternative to the number of years of direct experience required, not to exceed: • (a) Two years of direct experience for an associate degree; • (b) Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree; • (c) Six years of direct experience for a master’s degree; • (d) Seven years of direct experience for a professional degree; or • (e) Nine years of direct experience for a doctoral degree • Related work experience may not substitute for any required licensure, certification, or registration required for the position of employment as established by the public employer and indicated in the advertised description of the position of employment. • Minimum Qualifications that require a high school diploma are exempt from SB 1310. Additional Minimum Qualifications: Must hold, or be eligible for, licensure as a Registered Nurse (RN) or Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) in the state of Florida by the start date. Must meet university criteria for appointment at the rank of Instructor I (non-tenure earning). Minimum of two years of direct patient care clinical experience. Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Nursing (DNP or PhD). Minimum of three years of classroom and clinical teaching experience. A broad range of clinical knowledge and expertise in various settings or specialty areas. Local, state, or national leadership in a nursing professional organization. Strong communication and technology skills, and experience in curriculum design and evaluation of program outcomes. Teaching may occur across USF’s three campuses: Tampa, St. Petersburg, and Sarasota-Manatee. Faculty are also expected to contribute to curriculum development, service, and scholarly activities appropriate to the rank of Instructor I. In-person presence during standard business hours is required. Remote work option is not available for this position."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44075": {
      "title": "Open Rank Non Tenure Track (Assoc Director of Workforce Research, Florida Center for Nursing",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physicians’ Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The USF Health College of Nursing is one of 14 colleges at the University of South Florida and one of four that make up USF Health. As a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities, USF is designated by the Carnegie Foundation as both a Research 1 and a Community-Engaged institution, reflecting its commitment to excellence in education, research, and service. Nationally recognized as a leader in nursing education and research, the College of Nursing serves more than 2,000 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students each year. For the fourth consecutive year, our Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) program has been ranked No. 1 among Florida’s public universities by U.S. News & World Report—rising to No. 23 in the nation in 2025. As an integral part of USF Health, the College of Nursing is guided by a mission grounded in excellence, innovation, and respect. We are dedicated to educating future nurses, advancing nursing science, and applying evidence based practice to improve health outcomes and community well-being. Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. Additional Minimum Qualifications: Knowledge of research methods, statistics, and health workforce issues. Demonstrated ability to design and implement research including the analysis and interpretations of primary and secondary data. Survey research, health services research, and evaluation research experience. Experience in translating research into visual and written briefs. Strong communication, leadership, and collaboration skills. Proficient in technology and data systems relevant to workforce analysis. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with administrators, partners, and staff. Demonstrated ability to plan and organize assigned activities, including staff when appropriate. Demonstrated leadership skills. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in grant writing and program funding. Experience in advancing workforce initiatives. Experience working with state agencies, boards, or legislative stakeholders. Summary: The Associate Director of Workforce Research at the Florida Center for Nursing (FCN), headquartered within the University of South Florida College of Nursing (USF-CON), supports the Executive Director in advancing the mission of the FCN to address nursing workforce challenges through data-driven policy, education, and innovation. This faculty member plays a critical role in providing statewide workforce planning, developing initiatives and research on best practices, and evaluates and disseminates strategies that will lead to improved retention among nurses and recruitment of a qualified nursing workforce. This role exceeds traditional academic responsibilities and requires a dynamic scientist with a strong background in academia, workforce research, grant writing, and scholarly dissemination. The role includes significant travel (~50%, primarily in-state) to represent FCN at conferences, community meetings, and events. Renewal of appointment is dependent on performance, program needs, and/or availability of funds. Responsibilities: Responsible for the design, implementation, analysis, and reporting of nursing workforce research including but not limited to surveys of the nursing and health care workforce, nursing employers and nursing education programs. Monitor trends and best practices among the nursing workforce and briefs the Executive Director accordingly. Evaluate and apply selected available models for nurse supply or demand forecasting and generating projections. Assist with identification of workforce projects. Prepare grant proposals and budgets for submission to funding sources. Identify and secure resources for projects to be addressed by the FCN. Develop and design instruments for data collection. Collect and analyze data. Maintain databases of workforce supply, demand, and nursing programs. Generate written briefs, reports, infographics, visuals, and other materials to distribute nursing workforce data and trends to a wide audience. Present FCN findings to local, statewide, and national stakeholders. Collaborate with the marketing team to prepare media releases. Prepare manuscripts for publication related to activities of the FCN. Supervise staff and/or work with vendors assisting with projects for which the position is responsible. Maintain a network of state and national relationships that facilitates FCN’s efforts. Represent the FCN at selected meetings, conferences, and committees. Plan and implement evaluation of nursing workforce research activities. Perform other duties as assigned."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44232": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Dean for Simulation and Experiential Learning",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physicians’ Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The USF Health College of Nursing is one of 14 colleges at the University of South Florida and one of four that make up USF Health. As a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities, USF is designated by the Carnegie Foundation as both a Research 1 and a Community-Engaged institution, reflecting its commitment to excellence in education, research, and service. Nationally recognized as a leader in nursing education and research, the College of Nursing serves more than 2,000 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students each year. For the fourth consecutive year, our Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) program has been ranked No. 1 among Florida’s public universities by U.S. News & World Report—rising to No. 22 in the nation in 2026. As an integral part of USF Health, the College of Nursing is guided by a mission grounded in excellence, innovation, and respect. We are dedicated to educating future nurses, advancing nursing science, and applying evidence-based practice to improve health outcomes and community well-being. The University of South Florida College of Nursing invites applications for the position of Assistant Dean or Associate Dean for Simulation and Experiential Learning. The successful candidate will provide strategic and operational leadership for the College’s Simulation and Experiential Learning Center, advancing innovative, evidence-based learning experiences across undergraduate and graduate nursing programs. This leader will oversee simulation operations, faculty and staff development, accreditation, budget management, and partnerships that support student success and clinical competency. The position offers an opportunity to shape the future of simulation and experiential learning within one of the region’s largest nursing programs. Candidates from nursing are strongly encouraged to apply. Exceptional candidates from other health professions with significant simulation leadership are also encouraged to apply. Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in referred and other professional journals. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Associate or Professor. Additional Minimum Qualifications: Minimum of five (5) years of leadership experience in simulation, experiential learning, nursing education, or healthcare education. Experience supervising and developing faculty and/or staff. Demonstrated expertise in simulation-based education, curriculum integration, assessment, and accreditation. Ability to lead organizational change, build partnerships, and foster high-performing teams. Preferred Qualifications: Leadership experience within a college of nursing, academic health center, or health professions education program. Experience directing a comprehensive simulation center. Experience managing personnel, budgets, educational technologies, and accreditation activities. Success implementing innovative simulation methodologies and evidence-based educational practices. Record of scholarship and professional engagement in simulation, nursing education, or health professions education. CHSE (Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator) preferred certification. Candidates from nursing are strongly encouraged to apply. Exceptional candidates from other health professions with significant simulation leadership are also encouraged to apply. Responsibilities: Lead the strategic vision and daily operations of the Simulation and Experiential Learning Center. Integrate simulation and experiential learning across the undergraduate and graduate nursing curricula. Collaborate with faculty to design, implement, and evaluate evidence-based simulation experiences. Ensure compliance with accreditation requirements, regulatory standards, and simulation best practices. Support faculty development in simulation pedagogy, debriefing, and curriculum integration. Develop partnerships with clinical, community, and interprofessional education partners. Recruit, mentor, supervise, and evaluate simulation faculty and professional staff. Manage budgets, facilities, simulation technologies, and educational resources. Represent the College through professional organizations and simulation initiatives. Promote a culture of excellence, innovation, accountability, inclusion, and professionalism."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44475": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Quantum Information Science, Machine Learning - Physics",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Physics at the University of South Florida, Tampa, invites applications for a 9-month, full-time, tenure-earning faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor. We seek a theorist or computational physicist developing innovative methods and applications in quantum information science, artificial intelligence and machine learning for physics, data-driven physics, or closely related areas. The anticipated starting date is August 7, 2027. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. Candidates working in one or more areas—including quantum computation and algorithms, quantum simulations, quantum many-body theory, quantum machine learning, physics-informed machine learning, computational quantum science, and data-intensive approaches to physical systems—are encouraged to apply. Candidates whose research is at the intersection of these approaches or develop their applications to important problems in physics are welcome. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must hold a doctoral degree in physics or a closely related field from an accredited institution by the time of appointment. Postdoctoral or equivalent research experience in academia, a national laboratory, or industry is required. Applicants must demonstrate a strong record of research accomplishments and the potential to establish an independent, externally funded, and nationally recognized research program. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Information for Applicants: Applicants should submit the following documents with their application: Cover Letter CV Teaching Philosophy Evidence of successful research Names and contact information for three (3) professional references Shortlisted candidates will be contacted for letters of recommendation at a later date. Position is open until it is filled, with initial review of applications beginning on December 1, 2026. Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access institution. For disability accommodations, contact Edwin Perez Jr. at edwinperez@usf.edu , a minimum of five working days in advance. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu. The successful candidate will have opportunities to collaborate with research groups and interdisciplinary initiatives within the Department of Physics and across USF. Areas of potential synergy include quantum materials, nanomagnetism and spintronics, ultrafast dynamics, quantum optics, quantum sensing, biomedical physics, computational and data-driven materials physics. Research connecting fundamental advances in quantum information science or AI/ML with applications in healthcare, environmental sensing, secure communications, and information science is also of interest. The successful candidate will be expected to conduct high-impact research, pursue extramural funding, teach effectively at the undergraduate and graduate levels, and mentor students in research at all levels."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/38229": {
      "title": "Glaucoma Specialist (Open Rank Faculty)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Ophthalmology is seeking a Glaucoma specialist (Assistant Professor) to join its clinical care team and faculty. This position will provide comprehensive specialty Glaucoma care at the USF Health Eye Institute and inpatient services at Tampa General Hospital. This position will also supervise residents and be involved with training Glaucoma fellows. ORGANIZATIONAL SUMMARY: USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician?s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html POSITION SUMMARY: The Department of Ophthalmology is seeking a Glaucoma specialist (Assistant Professor) to join its clinical care team and faculty. This position will provide comprehensive specialty Glaucoma care at the USF Health Eye Institute and inpatient services at Tampa General Hospital. This position will also supervise residents and be involved with training Glaucoma fellows. MINIMUM: Medical degree from an accredited institution. Completion of an accredited Ophthalmology residency training program. Must meet university criteria for faculty appointment to the rank of assistant professor, associate or professor. Candidates must have or be eligible for an unrestricted Florida medical license. This candidate must obtain credentialing with USF Health and Tampa General Hospital. PREFERRED: Glaucoma clinical experience Provides outpatient Glaucoma and inpatient surgical care to patients at the USF Health Eye Institute and Tampa General Hospital. Supervision and teaching of residents, fellows and medical students. Lectures or provides Grand Rounds on various specialty topics. Provides TGH call coverage and performs other duties as assigned by Department Chair."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44466": {
      "title": "Open Rank Vice Chair of Research Anesthesiology.",
      "description": "Closing Date: 29/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Vice Chair of Research is a leadership position within the USF Health Department of Anesthesiology and Perioperative Medicine, reporting directly to the Chair of the Department. In addition to providing clinical care, the Vice Chair will lead and advance the department’s research mission. This role is responsible for establishing the vision, strategic direction, and infrastructure to expand and sustain a vibrant, multidisciplinary research enterprise. The Vice Chair of Research contributes to the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine’s overarching mission of excellence in patient care, research, education, and innovation. • Medical Degree or equivalent • Board Certification in Anesthesiology • Eligible for recommendation to the appropriate academic rank and appointment • Minimum of five years of active research experience with a proven track record of extramural funding as a Principal Investigator leading a team or laboratory. • Current external funding to support dedicated research effort. May include NIH, clinical trial, or other sponsored research funding. • Established record of peer-reviewed publications with the capability to serve as a principal investigator or co-investigator on research projects • Proven record of accomplishments that document excellence in research, teaching and service consistent with appointment as associate or full professor in the tenure-track. • National recognition for research excellence in a field related to anesthesiology • Prior management and/or leadership experience Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Clinical Duties: Provide Anesthesia Clinical Services through TeamHealth at Tampa General Hospital, Participate in teaching of house staff, fellows and students. Participate in evaluation of the performance of clinical fellows, residents, medical students, and research fellows. Under the leadership of the Department Chair of Anesthesiology and Perioperative Medicine, the Vice Chair of Research will: • Develop and implement a strategic research plan aligned with departmental and institutional priorities. • Elevate the department’s national reputation through growth in extramural funding, clinical trial activity, scholarly publications, and visibility at national and international meetings. • Cultivate an environment where research, teaching, and academic scholarship thrive. • Oversee and expand extramurally funded research programs, ensuring sustainability and alignment with the Morsani College of Medicine’s strategic goals. • Oversee and ensure effective administration of extramural funding, including compliance with all regulatory, financial, and reporting requirements for sponsored research. • Build collaborative research networks with other anesthesiology departments and interdisciplinary teams to secure large, multi-institutional awards. • Grow a robust, active research portfolio and laboratory or research team as an independently funded Principal Investigator. Lead the development of a collaborative research infrastructure, including mentorship programs, core resources, and shared facilities. • Recruit and mentor physicians and research staff with demonstrated or emerging success in securing extramural funding. • Champion the education and mentorship of the next generation of physician-scientists, integrating research opportunities into residency, fellowship, and student training. • Monitor and report on key research performance metrics (e.g., grant portfolio, publications, collaborations). • Foster accountability by reviewing physicians productivity, scholarly impact, and funding progress. • Evaluate, pilot, and scale emerging technologies relevant to anesthesiology (e.g., AI decision-support, perioperative monitoring, precision analgesia, remote patient management) • Participate in and strengthen interdisciplinary research and training programs across the institution. Administrative Duties: Represent the department by serving on boards and committees, attending meetings, presenting and participating in other activities as required. • Lead departmental and institutional committees in research. • Offer consultation regarding recruitment, engagement, and employment of program staff as needed. • Address or mediate interpersonal and professional conflicts within the research domain. • Support other leadership roles within the department. • Participates in departmental and institutional committees in training, research and clinical process activities."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44469": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Advertising",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Zimmerman School of Advertising & Mass Communications at the University of South Florida invites applications for two (2) tenure-track Assistant Professors in Advertising, nine-month, full-time positions with a start date of August 7, 2027. Salary is negotiable. We seek an outstanding scholar and instructor with a distinctive and innovative research agenda in advertising and teaching specialization in one or more of the following areas: advertising analytics, interactive advertising, advertising planning and management, or data-driven content creation. Experience with quantitative research methods, emerging technologies (e.g., artificial intelligence, social media targeting, and social listening tools such as Brandwatch), or relevant professional or industry experience is a plus. The ideal candidate will have an established record of, or strong potential for, securing external research funding, and will help build the research culture of The Zimmerman School, whether through their own research activity or by drawing on industry experience to strengthen the School’s professional connections. The Zimmerman School, located in Florida’s #1 media market, offers students transformational learning experiences in media and communication through distinctive curricula and hands-on training with award-winning scholars and professionals. Located in the dynamic Tampa Bay region, the Zimmerman School benefits from strong connections across a range of industries, including sports and entertainment, health care, tourism and hospitality, technology, and nonprofit and community organizations. These connections provide opportunities not only for student internships, client-based projects, and professional networking, but also for faculty to develop industry partnerships, pursue applied research and creative projects, engage community partners, and bring current professional perspectives into the classroom. Students train in a state-of-the-art virtual production studio, produce award-winning broadcast news shows that air on the local PBS affiliate, direct a student-run advertising and public relations agency that represents local and global clients, partner with local and national organizations to advance community initiatives, travel abroad to gain international experience through classes and internships and train to become certified drone pilots. Our graduate students conduct research and develop professional projects to enhance expertise in their fields and prepare for continued graduate study and success in professional practice. Minimum qualifications: A Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in a relevant field from an accredited institution is required. ABD candidates will be considered if the degree is completed before the August 7, 2027 start date. Candidates must have a record of research in advertising (and/or a closely related discipline). Candidates must have prior teaching experience in advertising (and/or a closely related field). Candidates should be qualified to teach in the undergraduate Integrated Public Relations and Advertising (IPRA) program and in the graduate program in Advertising (M.S.). Candidates must also meet university criteria for appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor. Preferred Qualifications: Relevant professional experience and work with advertising analytics, social media, data-driven content creation, or emerging technologies (e.g., social listening tools such as Brandwatch, artificial intelligence, etc.). Relevant advertising industry experience (e.g., agency, in-house, consulting, or freelance work in areas such as advertising strategy, creative development, branding, campaign development, media, or client services). When applying, please submit the following: Cover letter CV Research Statement Teaching Philosophy Provide names and contact information for three (3) professional references The positions are open until filled, and a review of applications begins on October 16, 2026. Questions may be directed to Search Committee Chair Christine McCarty at ccomple@usf.edu . Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access institution. For disability accommodations, contact Gina Lombardo at glombardo@usf.edu , a minimum of five working days in advance. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu. "
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42751": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Epilepsy",
      "description": "Closing Date: 31/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. This position will serve as a Epileptologist in the Department of Neurology at the University of South. The successful candidate will be academically oriented and responsible for providing comprehensive medical care and health counseling to patients. Additional responsibilities include conducting health seminars, offering consultative health services, and participating in educational activities. This role provides opportunities to teach medical students, residents, and fellows. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. ADDITIONAL QUALIFICATIONS: Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Must be Board Certified/Eligible in Epilepsy CLINICAL (90%): Responsible for providing medical care, including outpatient and in hospital examinations/diagnosis and treatment/therapy. Prepares medical records and correspondence related to patient care. Conducts health counseling in preventative medicine for patients. TEACHING (5%): Conducts teaching to Fellow, residents and medical students in the Department of Neurology. OTHER (5%): Other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44448": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Cognitive Science & Philosophy of Mind",
      "description": "Closing Date: 31/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Philosophy at the University of South Florida invites applications for a 9 month, full-time and tenure-earning, Assistant Professor position, with a start date of August 07, 2027. Salary is negotiable. The minimum requirement for this position is a PhD in Philosophy, Cognitive Science, or a cognate field from an accredited institution in hand by time of appointment. When applying, please upload the following documents as 1 combined PDF: Cover letter CV Evidence of teaching excellence (sample syllabi and teaching statement) Writing sample (roughly 25 pages) representative of the direction of research Three (3) letters of recommendation should be submitted directly to CAS-Philosophy@usf.edu. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications must be received by October 30, 2026. Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Institution. For disability accommodations, contact CAS-Philosophy@usf.edu a minimum of five working days in advance. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . AOS: Cognitive Science and Philosophy of Mind. AOC: Open. We expect the new assistant professor to demonstrate strong research potential and to contribute to the development of our new undergraduate degree program in Cognitive Science. In addition, we expect the individual to be a versatile teacher with a clear commitment to teaching courses that promote student success and contribute to improved four-year graduation rates. The department of Philosophy has particular strengths in the history of philosophy and philosophy of science, and several recent hires have added to the vibrant intellectual community in the department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44449": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Modern US History",
      "description": "Closing Date: 02/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of History at the University of South Florida seeks to fill a full-time, tenure-earning Assistant Professor position in Modern U.S. History. We welcome applications from those with specializations in transnational migration, diasporic communities or ethnic studies. The position is on a 9-month contract with a start date of August 7, 2027. Salary is negotiable. PhD in History from an accredited institution is required and must be conferred by the start date. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Preferred candidates will have university-level teaching experience and scholarly publications. When applying, please upload the following: Cover letter CV Writing sample Names and contact information for three (3) references Review of applications begins on December 1, 2026. The University of South Florida is an R1 research university and member of the American Association of Universities that serves 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa and St. Petersburg, Florida. For information regarding USF, please visit our website at www.usf.edu. Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Institution. For disability accommodations, contact Callie Hallett at 813-974-2809 or callieh@usf.edu a minimum of five working days in advance. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . The successful applicant will teach two courses a semester, including a U.S. general education survey (U.S. History since 1877), upper-level courses in their specialization, and seminars at both the undergraduate and graduate level."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44450": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Health & Well-Being",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Sociology and Interdisciplinary Social Sciences at the University of South Florida seeks candidates who specialize in sociology of health to fill a nine-month, full-time, tenure-earning position as Assistant Professor to begin August 7, 2027. Salary is negotiable. This position aligns with our department's strategic focus on health and well-being of communities, families and individuals and the university’s strength in health. A variety of methodological approaches will be considered. Qualified individuals with diverse experience and backgrounds are encouraged to apply. Our department is a multi-campus, multi-program unit with Tampa being the home campus for this position. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Sociology from an accredited institution is required. Applications from individuals who are ABD accepted, but the degree must be conferred by appointment start date. Must meet university criteria for the rank of Assistant Professor. Preferred Qualifications: Research and teaching records in health and medicine; demonstrated ability to work and collaborate across sub-disciplinary and cross-disciplinary areas; evidence of success in publication and teaching; and potential for funding. When applying, please upload a single PDF containing the following materials in this order: Cover letter (addressed to, Dr. Byron Miller, Search Committee Chair) CV, including the names and contact information for three (3) references Statement of research achievements and agenda Teaching portfolio, including teaching philosophy and experience with or commitment to teaching diverse student populations Writing sample for ABDs, a letter from the dissertation advisor stating that the degree will be conferred by August 7, 2027 Review of complete applications will begin promptly on October 30 and continue until the position is filled. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access institution. For disability accommodations, contact Fransheska Andaluz at fandaluz@usf.edu , a minimum of five working days in advance. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . Teaching load for research productive tenured faculty in our doctoral granting department is typically 2/2, and we provide a one course per year reduction during the first three-years of the tenure-earning period."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44455": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Public Relations",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Zimmerman School of Advertising & Mass Communications at the University of South Florida invites applications for two (2) Assistant Professors in Public Relations, a nine-month, full-time, tenure-earning position with a start date of August 7, 2027. Salary is negotiable. Minimum Qualifications: Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Mass Communications or a related field from an accredited institution. ABD candidates will be considered, but the degree must be completed prior to the appointment start date of August 7, 2027. Candidates must be qualified to teach public relations courses in the undergraduate Integrated Public Relations and Advertising (IPRA) program and in the Strategic Communication Management track of the Mass Communications master’s program. The successful candidate must have a commitment to excellence in the classroom, a defined research agenda focused on any area of public relations, and prior experience teaching public relations courses. The successful candidate must also meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Preferred Qualifications: The ideal candidate will have experience teaching one or more of the following courses: public relations ethics and social responsibility, public relations data analytics, and/or social media strategy for public relations. In addition, the ideal candidate will have professional experience in the public relations industry to inform their teaching and scholarship. When applying, please attach the following: Cover letter CV Teaching philosophy Research statement Provide names and contact information for three (3) professional references The positions are open until filled, with initial review of applications beginning on October 23, 2026. Questions may be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Kelli Burns, at kburns@usf.edu . The Zimmerman School, located in Florida's #1 media market, offers students transformational learning experiences in media and communication through distinctive curricula and hands-on training with award-winning scholars and professionals. Students direct a student-run advertising and public relations agency that represents local and global clients, partner with local and national organizations to advance community initiatives, train in a state-of-the-art virtual production studio, produce award-winning broadcast news shows that air on the local PBS affiliate, and travel abroad to gain international experience through classes and internships. Our graduate students conduct research and develop professional projects to enhance expertise in their fields and prepare for continued graduate study and success in professional practice. Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access institution. For disability accommodations, contact Gina Lombardo at glombardo@usf.edu , a minimum of five working days in advance. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . "
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44461": {
      "title": "Open Rank Neuromuscular",
      "description": "Closing Date: 28/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. Florida Medical License. This position requires licensure to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Responsible for providing medical care, including outpatient and in hospital examinations/diagnosis and treatment/therapy. Prepares medical records and correspondence related to patient care. Conducts health counseling in preventative medicine for patients with the guidance of the attending doctor. Conducts teaching, residents, and medical students in the Department of Neurology."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44430": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Spanish Linguistics",
      "description": "Closing Date: 21/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of World Languages at the University of South Florida invites applications for a nine-month, full-time, tenure-track position in Spanish Linguistics at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin August 7, 2027. Salary is negotiable. Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree from an accredited institution in Spanish Linguistics, Applied Linguistics (Spanish-language focus) or a closely related field by August 7, 2027. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Native or near-native command of Spanish. Excellent communication skills in English. Active research agenda. Experience teaching at the university level. Preferred Qualifications: A record of publication. Research focus on the Caribbean and/or the Spanish-speaking world in the Western Hemisphere. Demonstrated success in teaching graduate and undergraduate courses. When applying, please upload the following: a current CV cover letter evidence of teaching effectiveness (one full set of course evaluations, one representative syllabus) a writing sample, published, if possible, written in Spanish or English *Three (3) letters of recommendation (to be sent by the recommenders or through online platforms such as Interfolio to the Department Operations Manager, Ms. Alana Harris, alana18@usf.edu ). Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Institution. For disability accommodations, contact Ms. Alana Harris at alana18@usf.edu , a minimum of five working days in advance. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . Conduct, present, and publish research and engage in other professional activities. Teach courses primarily in Spanish for the Spanish program at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Collaborate, when appropriate, with the graduate programs in Applied Linguistics. Participate actively in department, college, and university governance."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44431": {
      "title": "Chair, Professor, Community Health Sciences",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/01/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. Learn more at www.usf.edu . The Department of Community Health Sciences (CHS) is the largest department within the University of South Florida's College of Public Health (COPH) and is a dynamic academic community dedicating to improving the health and well-being of individuals, families, and communities through excellence in education, research, practice, and service. The Department of Community Health Sciences offers a diverse portfolio of graduate programs, including MPH concentrations in Maternal & Child Health, Nutrition & Dietetics, Community Nutrition, and Health Promotion & Behavior; an MSPH in Genetic Counseling; and a PhD in Public Health with a concentration in Community & Family Health. The department also offers graduate certificates in Applied Lifestyle Medicine Coaching and Maternal and Child Health. Through these programs, CHS prepares public health professionals, researchers, and practitioners to address complex health challenges. CHS also contributes to undergraduate education and interdisciplinary public health training across the university. The department's faculty conduct innovative, community-engaged and translational research addressing critical public health challenges. Areas of research and practice include maternal and child health; health promotion and behavioral health; nutrition, dietetics and community nutrition; genetic counseling and genomics; lifestyle medicine; injury and violence prevention; health disparities; chronic disease prevention; and community-based interventions. CHS faculty and students engage with nationally recognized research and practice centers, including the Lawton and Rhea Chiles Center, USF Center of Excellence in Maternal and Child Health Education, Science and Practice, Sunshine Education and Research Center, James and Jennifer Harrell Center for the Study of Family Violence, and Center for Applied Lifestyle Medicine. These centers provide opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration, research, experiential learning, and community engagement. The department is committed to preparing the next generation of public health scientists, practitioners, educators, and leaders. CHS provides an environment that connects innovative research, evidence-based practice, interdisciplinary education, and meaningful community partnerships to address complex and evolving public health challenges locally, nationally, and globally. Learn more at https://health.usf.edu/publichealth/departments/chs/ Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree in Community Health Sciences or Equivalent with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in referred and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Professor. Additional Minimum Qualifications: A minimum of two years of sustained accomplishment as an Associate Professor in a university or equivalent setting, including evidence of scholarly productivity, leadership, teaching effectiveness, and service. A record of excellence in teaching in Community Health Sciences, including a clearly defined teaching philosophy and a record of participation on and as major professor for thesis and/or dissertation committees for master's and doctoral candidates where applicable. A national and/or international record of excellence in independent and/or collaborative research and/or creative scholarly work in Community Health Sciences supported by substantial and sustained publications or their equivalent. A record of substantive contribution of service to the University and to the field, profession, and community. Compelling evidence of significant achievement among peers in one's discipline or professional field at the national or international level. A record of collegiality and participation as a citizen of a University or other equivalent institution. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated expertise in Community Health Sciences or equivalent. Administrative experience leading multi-disciplinary teams. Commitment to and experience in mentoring of junior faculty. Commitment to and experience in attracting, retaining and graduating doctoral students. Ability to create and support a collaborative research and learning community. Extensive publication record in peer-reviewed journals relevant to the field of Community Health Sciences. Demonstrated commitment to faculty development, mentorship, retention, and advancement across career stages. Demonstrated success obtaining competitive extramural funding, including evidence of leadership on externally funded methodological, collaborative, or data science initiatives. Commitment to faculty governance and collegiality. Experience developing and sustaining community-engaged research, practice, and partnership initiatives. Excellent oral and written communication skills. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu. The incumbent of this position serves as a senior-level faculty member in Community Health Sciences. In addition, the incumbent serves as Chair of the Department. As a ranked professorial faculty position at USF, the incumbent will have teaching, research, scholarship and service responsibilities. As Chair of the Department, the incumbent will have the overall responsibility to lead the Department to a position of academic and professional prominence, while fostering a collaborative, inclusive, and forward-looking academic environment that supports faculty success, student achievement, interdisciplinary partnership, and research growth furthering the goals and mission of the College of Public Health. The Chair must effectively lead a diverse department spanning multiple disciplinary perspectives, fostering collaboration, transparency, faculty engagement, and community partnership. This position reports directly to the Dean who will meet with the incumbent annually to discuss the specific assignment for the upcoming academic year and evaluate performance for the previous year. Instructional Duties: Teach graduate level public health and Community Health Sciences related courses where interests and needs align. Collaborate in teaching with other faculty within the College and participate in college-wide teaching initiatives. Advise graduate students at both masters and doctoral levels, including serving on thesis and dissertation committees as needed. Research Duties: Collaborate with faculty within the Department and across the College, USF Health and USF to create new knowledge through research in the area of Community Health Sciences and to translate that knowledge to practice. Apply for and obtain competitive extramural funding for research grants. Disseminate scholarly achievements through peer-reviewed publications, presentations and active translation to the field. Service Duties: Participate in service activities at the university, professional and community levels, including serving on special work groups and other university service roles. Participate at the local, state and national level in professional organizations and activities. Serve on Department, College and University committees; actively participate in local, state, and national public health organizations and professional associations; and contribute actively to community engagement. Administrative Duties: Specific responsibilities of the Department Chair include: Exercising leadership by developing and implementing effective goals and plans for the department, representing the faculty and serving as a role model for faculty, staff and students. Managing Department staff and student employees, finances and resources effectively and efficiently, in accordance with College and University policies. Practicing fair, balanced and transparent leadership in managing the various constituencies within the Department and facilitating the work of faculty. Fostering excellence in the education, research and service programs of the Department, including collaboration with other department chairs, center directors, and designated mission leads. Facilitating the recruitment and retention of a diverse and talented faculty, staff and student body to fulfill the needs and missions of the Department and College. Advocating for equitable salary and academic work conditions for Department faculty, staff and student employees, facilitating their continuing academic and professional development. Encouraging the development of research and teaching programs and fostering interdisciplinary activities. Responsible for ensuring timely, fair and equitable completion of the annual faculty assignment and evaluation processes. Responsible for ensuring completion of the staff evaluation process and that their students are evaluated consistent with the expectations of the Graduate Assistant Collective Bargaining Agreement. Responsible for ensuring all University and College training requirements are completed on time and are up to date. Actively participating as a member of the College Leadership team, providing overall direction for the continued growth and improvement in quality of all College mission areas. Contributing to the reputation and overall welfare of the College and University. Collaborating with other Department Chairs regarding the assignment and evaluation of faculty who have joint (secondary) appointments in their respective departments, as well as, College-wide program directors for shared teaching responsibilities necessary to meet the academic mission of the College. The Chair is also expected to maintain a record of personal success in his/her field and participate in the teaching, research, and service programs of the Department. The Chair serves as an advisor to the Dean of the College of Public Health and as a member of the Executive Committee of the College. Promote a culture of transparency, collegiality, shared governance, and constructive conflict resolution within the department. Develop and implement strategic plans for faculty recruitment, retention, succession planning, and workforce growth aligned with departmental and college priorities Essential Functions of the Position: The creation, dissemination and translation of knowledge through collaborative research. Teaching on-line and in the classroom and advising students. Active engagement in professional and community service. Actively oversee and lead the academic, financial and human resource activities of the department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44420": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction - Civic Literacy",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The School of Interdisciplinary Global Studies (SIGS) at the University of South Florida invites applications for a 9-month, full-time, non-tenure earning Assistant Professor of Instruction position in Civic Literacy beginning on August 7, 2027. This position is non-tenure stream but is continuing and eligible for promotion to Associate Professor of Instruction and Professor of Instruction. The salary is $55,000 per year. The minimum requirement for this position is a Ph.D. in Political Science, Politics, or Government with a specialization in American Politics from an accredited institution. Applications from individuals who are ABD will be accepted, but the degree must be conferred by appointment start date. Preference will be given to applicants who have experience teaching American government classes as instructor of record. How to apply - Applicants should attach the following supplemental items to their application: cover letter curriculum vitae graduate transcripts teaching philosophy statement sample syllabus evidence of teaching effectiveness All documents must be combined and uploaded as one PDF file. Applicants selected for interviews will be asked to provide names and contact information for three (3) academic references, who will be asked to submit confidential letters of recommendation. A review of applications will begin on October 20, 2026. Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Institution. For disability accommodations, contact Megan Eaton at (813) 974-2384, a minimum of five working days in advance. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu. The incumbent will teach 8 undergraduate political science courses each year. Most semesters they will teach three sections of American National Government and a class in their area of expertise. This position is being established in support of the state of Florida's Postsecondary Civic Literacy Requirement, which has increased demand for our introductory American National Government course. Summer teaching opportunities for additional compensation are likely to become available."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/41978": {
      "title": "Open Rank Movement Disorder Neurology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 31/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. This position will be working in the Department of Neurology Huntington’s Disease as an academically oriented Assistant Professor Neurologist. Will be responsible for providing medical care and health counseling. This position will also conduct health seminars, providing health consultative services. This position will include opportunities for medical student, resident and Fellow teaching. Minimums: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in referred and other professional journals and be recognized authority in the field of specialization. MUST BE BOARD CERTIFIED/ELIGIBLE IN: Movement Disorder Preferred: Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full unrestricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Clinical Responsible for providing medical care, including outpatient and hospital examinations/diagnosis and treatment/therapy. Prepares medical records and correspondence related to patient care. Conducts health counseling in preventative medicine for patients Teaching Conduct teaching to Fellows, residents and medical students in the Department of Neurology Other duties as assigned Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a state university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43026": {
      "title": "Non-Invasive Cardiologist",
      "description": "Closing Date: 24/03/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences, and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. In partnership with Tampa General Hospital (TGH) Heart & Vascular Institute (HVI), the Division of Cardiovascular Sciences, Section of General & Preventive Cardiology, is seeking an academic non-invasive general cardiologist for a full-time position at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor rank. Preference is placed for candidates with expertise in hypertension management or vascular disease to lead a resistant hypertension program or a medical vascular program. Candidates with expertise in sports cardiology are also encouraged to apply. This is a full-time, 12-month salaried faculty appointment and includes attending staff privileges at Tampa General Hospital (TGH) and affiliated hospitals. There is a desire for candidates with a strong interest in and commitment to teaching. Appointment at the rank of Associate Professor requires a minimum of five years of continuing and productive service as an Assistant Professor, or the equivalent. Appointment at the rank of Full Professor involves a minimum of five years of ongoing and productive service as an Associate Professor, or the equivalent. Minimum: Doctoral/Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate or Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in referred and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. The candidate would need to have an expertise in hypertension management or vascular disease, to lead a resistant hypertension program or a medical vascular program. Candidates with expertise in sport cardiology are encouraged to apply Additional Minimum; Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full unrestricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Preferred: Applicants with teaching experience with students/residents, experience with administrative organization/leadership of outpatient practices, and/or clinical research/scholarship experience will be most competitive. Level II certification in Echocardiography is preferred. Desire expertise in adult non-invasive assessment of heart disease, including surface echo and trans-esophageal echocardiography, stress echo and adult congenital heart disease. Desire experience with exercise testing, ECG interpretation, consulting and attending in a coronary intensive care unit or similar environment. Two years’ experience in Non-Invasive Cardiology preferred. MUST BE BOARD CERTIFIED/ELIGIBLE IN: General Cardiology Clinical -Participates in Inpatient general cardiology consult service, non-invasive call & coverage, reading EKGs and Stress Tests. Opportunity to participate in Echo Lab and Call & Coverage for Transesophageal Echocardiography, Stress Test on call, and Echo reads if certified from a nationally accredited organization. Participates in outpatient clinics for USF Health. Duties include Diagnose and treat disorders and diseases of the cardiovascular system. Participate in didactic teaching and mentoring of medical and/or graduate students, residents, and/or post-doctoral fellows. Perform patient exams and order or conduct diagnostic testing. Develop ongoing treatment and disease-management plans. Prescribe medicine and coordinate referrals as necessary. Conduct early detection screenings. Maintain accurate patient records and charts. Communicate effectively with patients, physicians, staff, and administration. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Teaching –Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44406": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Clinical Psychology (Applied AI)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Psychology at the University of South Florida invites applications for a 9-month, full-time appointment of a tenure-track scholar in clinical psychology at the Assistant Professor level, with service to begin August 7, 2027. We seek a clinical scientist whose program of research develops, evaluates, studies, or uses artificial intelligence to advance clinical psychology and mental health. This work may seek to improve understanding of the mechanisms associated with psychological disorders or to develop, evaluate, and implement approaches to their assessment, prevention, and treatment. Relevant areas of research include, but are not limited to: AI-supported assessment, diagnosis, and clinical decision-making; digital and adaptive interventions, including interventions delivered through conversational agents; research on how AI affects clinical practice, clinical populations, and mental health outcomes; and the safe, effective, and responsible development and use of AI in clinical settings. The successful candidate will join a department with established strengths in psychopathology and addiction and will have opportunities to collaborate across the University of South Florida, including with USF Health and the Bellini College of Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity and Computing. Applicants should demonstrate an active, programmatic line of research; excellence or strong potential in undergraduate and graduate teaching; and a commitment to the clinical science approach. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must hold a doctoral degree in Psychology from an accredited institution and demonstrate achievement or strong potential in research, teaching, and service. Candidates must meet University criteria for appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor. Applications from individuals who are ABD will be considered, provided that all requirements for the doctoral degree are completed by the appointment start date. Strong preference will be given to applicants with a Ph.D. in Clinical Psychology from an PCSAS-, APA-, or CPA-accredited doctoral program and completion of an APA- or CPA-accredited predoctoral internship. Eligibility for licensure as a psychologist in Florida is also desirable. Information for applicants - When applying, please attach the following documents: Cover letter Statement describing your research program and teaching interests Curriculum vita up to 3 reprints or preprints Three (3) letters of recommendation should be sent directly to the Department Operations Manager, Giovanni Luciano, at gluciano1@usf.edu ; University of South Florida, Department of Psychology, 4202 E. Fowler Avenue, PCD 4118G, Tampa, FL 33620. The deadline for applications is October 31, 2026 . Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Institution. For disability accommodations, contact Giovanni Luciano by email, gluciano1@usf.edu , or phone, (813) 974-9380 The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . The successful candidate will be expected to maintain an active program of research, pursue external research funding, mentor doctoral students, and contribute to the program’s core undergraduate and/or graduate curriculum."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44414": {
      "title": "Research Associate Dr. Thomas' lab",
      "description": "Closing Date: 22/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Faculty - Other JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. This position includes substantial responsibility in clinical/translational data management and analysis, experimental design, manuscript and grant development, animal surgeries, molecular assays, and coordination across multidisciplinary projects. PhD degree from an accredited institution with demonstrated record of academic research achievement, or professional qualifications in the field of specialization above those which would be equivalent to the highest degree. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Research Associate. Key Responsibilities • Lead and assist with analysis of large clinical and experimental datasets • Perform and assist with rodent surgical procedures and post-operative monitoring • Conduct molecular, histological, and biochemical experiments • Contribute to experimental design, troubleshooting, and optimization • Assist in manuscript preparation, figure generation, and grant development • Coordinate research activities across trainees and collaborators • Maintain accurate records and support reproducible research practices • Participate in mentorship and training of junior laboratory personnel"
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44391": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Digital Media",
      "description": "Closing Date: 04/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Humanities, Arts, & Film (HAF) at the University of South Florida seeks to fill a 9-month, full-time, and tenure-earning position for an Assistant Professor of Digital Media Arts. Expected start date is August 7, 2027. Salary is negotiable. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . A Ph.D. in film studies, media studies, cultural studies, communication, or another related field from an accredited institution is required. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Preferred areas of expertise include digital art and aesthetics, video art and animation, and the social and cultural histories of film and video production, distribution, exhibition, and reception across narrative and non-narrative as well as theatrical and non-theatrical domains. When applying, please attach the following: Cover letter CV Names and contact information for three (3) references At later stages of the review process candidates will be asked for additional materials, including sample syllabi. Applications are due November 2, 2026. Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Institution. For disability accommodations, contact Meredith Donovan by email, cas-hcs@usf.edu , or phone, (813) 974-9380. The faculty member will teach interdisciplinary undergraduate and graduate courses and advise MA student thesis projects."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44392": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Audiovisual Media & Sound Studies",
      "description": "Closing Date: 04/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Humanities, Arts, & Film (HAF) at the University of South Florida seeks to fill a 9-month, full-time, and tenure-earning position for an Assistant Professor of Audiovisual Media & Sound Studies. Expected start date is August 7, 2027. Salary is negotiable. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . A Ph. D. in film studies, music studies, media studies, cultural studies or related field from an accredited institution is required. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Applications from individuals who are ABD are considered, but the degree must be conferred by the appointment start date. Preferred areas of expertise include the relationships between sounds and images in the context of analog and/or digital technologies; human and nonhuman soundscapes; national and transnational cultures; affect and emotion; and the social and cultural histories of viewing and listening techniques and practices. When applying, please attach the following: Cover letter CV Names and contact information for three (3) references At later stages of the review process candidates will be asked for additional materials, including sample syllabi. Applications are due November 2, 2026. Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Institution. For disability accommodations, contact Meredith Donovan by email, cas-hcs@usf.edu , or phone, (813) 974-9380. The faculty member will teach interdisciplinary undergraduate and graduate courses and advise MA student thesis projects."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44399": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor – Speech-Language Pathology (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The University of South Florida (USF), an AAU member institution, Department of Communication Sciences & Disorders invites applications for a nine-month Assistant Professor position in Speech-Language Pathology (tenure track). We especially encourage applicants who are advanced Assistant Professors or candidates with evidence of strong potential for externally funded research to apply. Successful applicants will demonstrate a clear and promising research agenda, evidence of research productivity commensurate with career stage, strong teaching skills, and a commitment to mentoring students and trainees. Why USF Communication Sciences and Disorders University of South Florida's Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders (CSD), home to a world-class, multidisciplinary faculty of speech-language pathologists, audiologists, sign-language interpreters, linguists, hearing scientists and speech scientists. Together, we serve the diverse and growing Tampa Bay community through culturally and linguistically responsive care delivered across schools, medical centers, private practices and community settings. Our department trains a diverse student body across each of these areas. We offer undergraduate degrees in language, speech and hearing sciences and sign-language interpreter training. Our graduate programs include a master's degree in speech-language pathology, a doctorate in audiology and a doctoral research degree in communication sciences and disorders. We pride ourselves on giving students the strongest possible preparation for these careers, and our faculty regularly win teaching awards acknowledging their commitment to student success. The excellence of our graduate programs is reflected in their strong national rankings — currently #18th for audiology and #40th for speech-language pathology (U.S. News & World Report, 2025). As part of this pedagogical effort, we operate three clinics and a sign-language interpreter agency, giving students real-world, hands-on training while providing high-quality services to our clients Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Communication Sciences and Disorders or related discipline from an accredited institution at time of hire. Demonstrated record of excellent or potential for excellence in academic research, teaching, and service, commensurate with experience. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Preferred Qualifications: Strong potential to develop an externally funded, sustainable research program appropriate for an Assistant Professor at an AAU institution Evidence of emerging research productivity, including peer-reviewed publications, presentations, or other scholarly dissemination commensurate with career stage Compelling, feasible, and impactful research agenda with potential for interdisciplinary collaboration Evidence of effective teaching experience or strong potential for excellence in teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate level Effective communication skills and evidence of leadership potential in research, teaching, service, or professional engagement Evidence of mentoring potential with students, trainees, or early-stage scholars Clinical expertise, professional certification, or applied experience that complement the candidate’s research and teaching areas HOW TO APPLY Apply through the USF online application system at jobs.usf.edu . Applicants are required to submit the following in support of their application: Cover letter CV Three-year research plan Summary of experience and philosophy related to teaching and mentoring of students and/or faculty Three (s) letters of recommendation (these can be collected as part of the application process or at a later date by the HRBP, but before any verbal/soft offer is made) Review of applications will begin early November 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. For questions about the position, please contact: Dr. Theresa “Terry” Chisolm , Search Committee Chair, chisolm@usf.edu For ADA accommodations, contact melaniesalarbux@usf.edu . Learn more: Department of Communication Sciences & Disorders The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . About the Position The University of South Florida (USF), an AAU member institution, Department of Communication Sciences & Disorders invites applications for a nine-month Assistant Professor position in Speech-Language Pathology. We especially encourage applicants who are advanced Assistant Professors or candidates with evidence of strong potential for externally funded research to apply. Successful applicants will demonstrate a clear and promising research agenda, evidence of research productivity commensurate with career stage, strong teaching skills, and a commitment to mentoring students and trainees. Responsibilities of the position include scholarship, teaching at the undergraduate and graduate level, student mentoring, and service to the department, college, university, community, and profession. Candidates should be prepared to contribute to the research mission of an AAU institution through high-quality scholarship, pursuit of external funding, and collaboration across disciplines. We are especially interested in the following research areas in speech-language pathology: early intervention, development and disorders in children with speech (e.g., childhood apraxia of speech, articulation/phonological disorders) or language disorders (e.g., multilingualism and disparities in child language and literacy, children with hearing loss and/or cochlear implants, school-age language and literacy), developmental differences (e.g., autism, or other disorders, educational support for children with speech/language/hearing differences), or specialized interventions for children (e.g., AAC, MMST), child feeding and swallowing. However, all areas of research related to childhood will be considered. The anticipated start date is August 7, 2027."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44401": {
      "title": "Instructor/Professor of Instruction (Open Rank) Interpreter Training / ASL",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders at the University of South Florida, a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), invites applications for a full-time (12-month) instructional faculty position (non-tenure track) supporting the undergraduate Interpreter Training Program and the American Sign Language course sequence. Why USF Communication Sciences and Disorders University of South Florida's Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders (CSD), home to a world-class, multidisciplinary faculty of speech-language pathologists, audiologists, sign-language interpreters, linguists, hearing scientists and speech scientists. Together, we serve the diverse and growing Tampa Bay community through culturally and linguistically responsive care delivered across schools, medical centers, private practices and community settings. Our department trains a diverse student body across each of these areas. We offer undergraduate degrees in language, speech and hearing sciences and sign-language interpreter training. Our graduate programs include a master's degree in speech-language pathology, a doctorate in audiology and a doctoral research degree in communication sciences and disorders. We pride ourselves on giving students the strongest possible preparation for these careers, and our faculty regularly win teaching awards acknowledging their commitment to student success. The excellence of our graduate programs is reflected in their strong national rankings — currently #18th for audiology and #40th for speech-language pathology (U.S. News & World Report, 2025). As part of this pedagogical effort, we operate three clinics and a sign-language interpreter agency, giving students real-world, hands-on training while providing high-quality services to our clients. Minimum Qualifications: Education: An earned master’s degree in interpreting, interpreter education, Deaf education, Deaf studies, ASL, linguistics, communication sciences and disorders, education, or a closely related field is required for appointment in the Instructor series; an earned doctoral degree in one of these fields or a closely related field is required for appointment in the Professor of Instruction series. Rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications and experience. National certification: National interpreting certification such as RID, NAD-IV or higher, or BEI-Master or higher. Professional interpreting experience: At least five years of professional interpreting experience. Teaching experience: At least three years of high school, college-, or university-level teaching experience in an ASL or interpreting program, with a demonstrated range of coursework. Student and intern evaluation: Demonstrated experience evaluating interpreting students and interns. ASL fluency: Native or near-native fluency in ASL Preferred Qualifications: Teaching experience : More than five years of college- or university-level teaching experience in interpreter education Program and curriculum experience : Experience in curriculum development, student assessment, program improvement, or fieldwork and internship coordination. Instructional effectiveness : Evidence of sustained instructional effectiveness. Course delivery : Experience teaching online, hybrid, or technology-supported courses. Specialized interpreting : Experience in trilingual interpreting (Spanish, ASL, and English), oral transliteration, or other specialized interpreting settings. Certification : ASLTA certification Program leadership : Demonstrated leadership of an interpreting program. Community and professional engagement : Demonstrated effectiveness working with students, Deaf communities, and professional partners. Advanced qualifications : Progressively advanced instructional leadership, program contributions, and professional service appropriate to the proposed rank. HOW TO APPLY Apply through the USF online application system at jobs.usf.edu . Applicants are required to submit the following in support of their application: Cover Letter CV Two (s) Letters of Recommendation (these can be collected as part of the application process or at a later date by the HRBP, but before any verbal/soft offer is made) Review of applications will begin late October 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. For questions about the position, please contact: Dr. Theresa “Terry” Chisolm , Search Committee Chair, chisolm@usf.edu For ADA accommodations, contact melaniesalarbux@usf.edu . Learn more: Department of Communication Sciences & Disorders The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . About the Position The Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders at the University of South Florida, a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), invites applications for a full-time (12-month) instructional faculty position supporting the undergraduate Interpreter Training Program and the American Sign Language course sequence. In accordance with USF’s instructional faculty career paths, candidates without a doctoral degree who hold an appropriate master’s degree may be considered for appointment in the Instructor series at the Assistant Instructor, Associate Instructor or Senior Instructor rank. Candidates with an earned doctoral degree relevant to the teaching assignment may be considered for appointment in the Professor of Instruction series at the Assistant Professor of Instruction, Associate Professor of Instruction, or Professor of Instruction rank. Appointment rank will be commensurate with the candidate’s degree, qualifications, experience, and record of accomplishment. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses in interpreter theory, interpreting practice (including practicum or internship), and ASL; and participate in service to the department, college, university, community, and profession. Depending on the level of experience, the successful candidate may also assume a leadership role as program director. The position requires a record of effective university-level teaching, substantial professional interpreting experience, commitment to student success, adherence to professional standards in interpreting, and engagement with students, Deaf communities, and professional partners."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44101": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States Position Description: The Department of Child and Family Studies in the USF College of Behavioral and Community Sciences is seeking an Assistant Professor of Instruction for its online Rehabilitation Counseling and Disability Sciences Program. This is a non-tenure earning faculty position. This position will teach courses in the online MA Program (Fall, Spring, and Summer) with particular focus on clinical classes and other tasks assigned by the Program Director. This position will teach 4 courses in the fall, 4 courses in the spring, and 3 courses in the summer semesters. They will also contribute to the overall program function, enhancing the curriculum, and participating in program activities. We seek individuals who bring enthusiasm and a deep commitment to academic excellence within the scholar-practitioner tradition. We are particularly interested in candidates who can provide leadership, work with individuals from varied backgrounds, stakeholders, and colleagues, and who have experience and credentials in clinical mental health counseling and/or rehabilitation counseling. This position requires a person to work from the USF Tampa campus. It is not a remote position. Minimum Qualifications: An earned doctorate (or ABD with degree conferred prior to appointment) in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP accredited program or closely related field who can be considered core faculty according to CACREP standards. Current Certified Rehabilitation Counselor, or licensed/eligible for licensure as an LMHC in Florida within 1 year. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of instructor. Preferred Qualifications: Holds both Certified Rehabilitation Counselor and LMHC credentials. Has two or more years of professional experience in supervision. Has two or more years of professional experience in graduate level teaching. Has two or more years of professional experience in delivering clinical services. Has at least one year of experience in teaching online courses both in asynchronous and synchronous formats. Criteria for the evaluation of candidates To ensure the fair and equitable evaluation of all candidates, the following criteria will be used in reviewing the applicants’ qualifications. Ranges for rating the criteria are weighted in terms of importance to the position. Applicants are required to submit the following in support of their application: Cover Letter Addressing Position Qualifications CV Two Letters of Recommendation "
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44251": {
      "title": "Assistant-Associate Professor",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States Position Description: The Department of Child and Family Studies in the USF College of Behavioral and Community Sciences is seeking three Assistant-Associate Professors for its Clinical Rehabilitation and Mental Health Counseling (CRMHC) program . The CRMHC Program is housed within the Department of Child and Family Studies in the College of Behavioral and Community Sciences at USF. It offers a comprehensive suite of CACREP -accredited graduate and undergraduate programs, including: Master of Arts in Clinical Mental Health Counseling Master of Arts in Clinical Rehabilitation Counseling Master of Arts in Rehabilitation Counseling and Disability Sciences (fully online) An undergraduate minor in Addiction and Substance Abuse These programs prepare students to become Licensed Mental Health Counselors (LMHCs) or Certified Rehabilitation Counselors (CRCs), with a strong emphasis on evidence-based practice, interdisciplinary collaboration, and service to individuals with disabilities and mental health needs. The University of South Florida (USF) College of Behavioral and Community Sciences (CBCS) proudly houses the Florida Center for Behavioral Health Workforce (FCBHW), commissioned by the Florida Legislature, to strengthen the state’s behavioral health system through workforce development. CBCS also houses a University Center for Excellence in Developmental Disabilities and recently established a research center in substance abuse and mental health research that is funded by the state of Florida. These three positions are tenure earning/tenured 9-month Assistant-Associate faculty positions. This position will teach in-person courses in the program during Fall and Spring semesters. The position will have responsibilities as a core faculty member, with responsibilities for both research and teaching. The role will include responsibilities for research and securing external grant funding, mentoring and advising graduate students, teaching, and university, community, and professional service. Successful applicants must meet University of South Florida criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor, including holding a doctoral degree from an accredited institution. This position will be a part of the USF Tampa Campus. Minimum Qualifications : · Earned doctorate in Counselor Education (preferably from a CACREP-accredited program) or a closely related field and meets the University’s criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. · Possession of or eligibility for licensure as a Licensed Mental Health Counselor (LMHC) in Florida or Certified Rehabilitation Counselor (CRC) status within one year of employment. Preferred Qualifications : · Strongly preferred: applicant meets the CACREP core faculty eligibility requirements · Evidence of a clear research focus and an early career record of scholarly activity · Teaching experience with master’s level courses in rehabilitation or mental health counseling · Experience providing clinical supervision · Knowledge of CACREP accreditation standards and/or participation in CACREP accreditation processes · Experience with grant writing · Scholarly peer-reviewed publications Criteria for the evaluation of candidates To ensure the fair and equitable evaluation of all candidates, the following criteria will be used in reviewing the applicants’ qualifications. Ranges for rating the criteria are weighted in terms of importance to the position. Applicants are required to submit the following in support of their application: Cover Letter to include how you identify professionally CV Statement of Teaching Philosophy (1-page limit) Explanation of Research Agenda (2-page limit) 3-5 Professional References (name, affiliation, title) Position open until filled. Review of applications will begin on September 14, 2026 Contact information: Leah Worthey; lworthey@usf.edu Essential Functions: Develop and maintain an active research line in clinical mental health and/or clinical rehabilitation counseling, including pursuit of external grant funding opportunities and scholarly publications and presentations. Develop/teach graduate-level courses in a variety of formats (in-person, online, and hybrid) and provide clinical supervision of rehabilitation and mental health counseling students. · Support and strengthen the program’s thesis track by mentoring graduate student research, serving on student thesis committees, and contributing to the ongoing development and advancement of the thesis program. Opportunity to mentor and support doctoral candidates within the interdisciplinary behavioral health doctoral program. Participate in service activities within the department, college, and university, as well as in professional counseling organizations. Work collaboratively and ethically with other faculty, staff, and students within the department, college, and university, while promoting the mission and goals of the department and counseling profession. Assessment of qualifications will be adjusted based on the capacity of the rank of the applicant (e.g. Assistant or Associate). ABD will be considered with appropriate experience. Degree must be conferred by the date of the appointment."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44376": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Tenure-Track (Criminology)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Criminology at the University of South Florida (USF) in Tampa invites applications for a 9-month tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning tentatively on or after August 6th, 2027. Area of specialization is open. Why USF Criminology? USF Criminology is a nationally recognized department with a strong record of research and graduate education. Our graduate program is currently ranked No. 18 nationally by U.S. News & World Report , and the department offers undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral programs. Faculty and students work in an active research environment, including research laboratories focused on cybercrime, human trafficking, prisoner reentry, and other areas of criminology and criminal justice. The department values rigorous scholarship, collaboration, and research that contributes to both the discipline and the communities we study. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU) and a Preeminent R1 research university serving nearly 50,000 students. The university offers substantial opportunities for interdisciplinary and applied research across a major research institution and the broader Tampa Bay region. Tampa offers an exceptional quality of life, combining year-round sunshine, abundant outdoor recreation, a vibrant cultural and dining scene, and the amenities of a major metropolitan area within a welcoming and diverse community. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Criminology, Criminal Justice, or a closely related social science discipline prior to the date of appointment. J.D. degrees are not acceptable. Evidence of a publication record. ABDs will be considered, but the degree must be conferred prior to the date of appointment. Preferred Qualifications Strong record of scholarly publication. Evidence of effective teaching at the university level. Evidence of grant experience or potential to secure external funding. Potential to make a significant contribution to the department’s doctoral program. HOW TO APPLY Apply through the USF online application system at jobs.usf.edu . Please submit: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Three references, to be contacted later Review of applications will begin October 2 nd , 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Salary is competitive and commensurate with qualifications and experience. For questions about the position, please contact: George Burruss Department and Search Committee Chair gburruss@usf.edu For ADA accommodations, contact taneisharobinson@usf.edu . Learn more: criminology.usf.edu The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . About the Position We are seeking a scholar who will contribute to the department’s research mission and doctoral program. Because the area of specialization is open, we welcome candidates working across the breadth of criminology and criminal justice and using a range of theoretical, methodological, and interdisciplinary approaches. The successful candidate should demonstrate research productivity and the potential to develop an externally funded research program. Evidence of effective university teaching, either in person or online, is preferred."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44370": {
      "title": "Open Rank Academic IBD Gastroenterologist",
      "description": "Closing Date: 14/03/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Division of Digestive Disease seeks a board-certified/board-eligible gastroenterologist with specialized training and expertise in Inflammatory Bowel Disease. The successful candidate will provide comprehensive care for patients with Crohn's disease, ulcerative colitis, indeterminate colitis, and other complex immune-mediated gastrointestinal disorders. The physician will join a collaborative multidisciplinary team dedicated to delivering innovative, evidence-based care while supporting education, research, and program development. Practice locations include ambulatory clinics and affiliated teaching hospitals throughout the Tampa Bay region. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu. Minimum: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Preferred: Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. MUST BE BOARD CERTIFIED/ELIGIBLE IN: Inflammatory Bowel Disease Clinical-2-3 days of outpatient IBD-focused clinics. 1-2 days of endoscopy procedures, Inpatient consult responsibilities as assigned. Participation in multidisciplinary conferences and care planning meetings. Gastroenterology inpatient consult coverage. Hospital and emergency department consultation support. Management of urgent IBD-related issues as needed. Teaching-Participate in didactic teaching and mentoring of medical and/or graduate students, residents and/or post-doctoral fellows. Participate in the development of the IBD Fellowship Program. Research-Maintain a nationally competitive research program with continued extramural funding, peer-reviewed publications, and collaboration with other faculty. You will participate in research with the Division of Digestive Diseases & Nutrition; Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD) Center, and in educational research (including grant writing) and other scholarly activities. Administrative-TGH Medical Director, Gastroenterology / IBD. Complete clinical obligations such as chart completion, patient follow-up, reviewing lung offers, triaging calls and labs, organizing outreach clinics and growing the referral network. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44361": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - American Politics",
      "description": "Closing Date: 21/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The School of Interdisciplinary Global Studies (SIGS) at the University of South Florida (Tampa campus) seeks to fill a 9-month, full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor of American Politics position. The start date of the position will be August 7, 2027. Salary is negotiable and dependent upon qualification and experience. Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Political Science or a closely related field from an accredited institution is required. Applications from individuals who are ABD will be accepted, but the degree must be conferred by appointment start date. Preferred Qualifications: Special consideration will be given to candidates whose research and teaching examine any of the following: American Political Institutions, American Political Development, political parties and movements, urban politics, women and politics, and/or indigenous politics. Applicants should submit the following documents with their application: 1. Cover Letter that addresses research and teaching 2. CV 3. Writing Sample 4. Sample Syllabi 5. Names and contact information for three (3) references. Shortlisted candidates will be contacted for letters of recommendation at a later date. Closing date for receiving applications is October 20, 2026 . The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Institution. For disability accommodations, contact Megan Eaton at (813) 974-2384, a minimum of five working days in advance. The successful candidate will pursue original research in the field of American Politics and teach four courses per year (2/2 semester schedule)."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44362": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Statistics (AI & Drug Discovery)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 02/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Mathematics & Statistics at the University of South Florida seeks to ﬁll a 9-month, full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Statistics/Data Science on our Tampa campus with research interests in statistical methodology for Artiﬁcial Intelligence (AI) innovations on biomedical or pharmaceutical applications such as AI-enabled Drug Discovery and Development, starting August 7, 2027. Salary is negotiable. We seek an outstanding researcher whose work lies at the intersection of statistical science, AI, and biomedical or pharmaceutical applications, particularly data-driven approaches to AI-enabled drug discovery and development. The successful candidate will contribute to the department’s growing research initiatives in AI-enabled data science and health analytics and will be expected to collaborate on interdisciplinary projects with researchers from USF Department of Chemistry, USF Health Morsani College of Medicine and Taneja College of Pharmacy, as well as experts from Moffit Cancer Center and Tampa General Hospital. Minimum Qualiﬁcations: Doctoral degree from an accredited institution in Statistics, Biostatistics, Mathematics with a concentration in Statistics or other disciplines with strong background in theoretical statistics, with a demonstrated record of achievement in academic research, teaching, and service. Doctoral degree must be conferred by August 1, 2027. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Preferred Qualiﬁcations: Doctoral degree from an accredited institution in Statistics, Biostatistics, Mathematics with a concentration in Statistics or other disciplines with strong background in theoretical statistics. Preference will be given to candidates who have strong theoretical foundation in Statistics and research experience in AI for drug discovery, evidenced by a strong record of research with publications in statistical or related journals. Interdisciplinary collaborative experience is strongly valued. Application Instructions: When applying, please attach a cover letter, CV, teaching philosophy, evidence of successful research and the names and contact information for three references. To receive consideration, applications must be submitted no later than December 1, 2026 . In addition, candidates should have at least three (3) recommendation letters submitted through MathJobs.org. Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Institution. For disability accommodations, contact Denise L. Marks at (813-974-9747/denise@usf.edu), a minimum of five working days in advance. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu. Applicants must demonstrate evidence of, or potential for, excellence both in research and teaching; previous teaching experience is preferred. The candidate hired to this position will be expected to teach effectively at both undergraduate and graduate levels in Statistics, to maintain a vigorous research program, to seek external research funding, and to develop a satisfactory record of service."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44342": {
      "title": "Academic Emergency Medicine Physician",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html This full-time clinical faculty position in Adult Emergency Medicine will provide patient care within the Tampa General Hospital Emergency Department system, including the main academic medical center and the South Campus Freestanding Emergency Departments. The physician will practice in a high-acuity, Level I Trauma Center that serves as the primary teaching site for the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine. This is position offers the opportunity to deliver high-quality, evidence-based emergency care in an academic environment that supports teaching, collaboration, and innovation across multidisciplinary teams. Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Must be board certified/Eligible in Emergency Medicine. Clinical responsibilities will include patient care at the Tampa General Hospital Emergency Department main Academic site and the South Campus Freestanding Emergency Departments. This position will participate in bedside teaching during overnight shifts; the main academic site has Medical Students and Residents present. Bedside teaching of residents and medical students, which are present across all academic sites."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44343": {
      "title": "Academic Emergency Medicine Physician & Core Faculty",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. This full-time clinical faculty position in Adult Emergency Medicine will provide patient care within the Tampa General Hospital Emergency Department system, including the main academic medical center and the South Campus Freestanding Emergency Departments. The physician will practice in a high-acuity, Level I Trauma Center that serves as the primary teaching site for the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine. The Residency Core Faculty Member will support the residency program through mentorship, curriculum development, and resident assessment while ensuring alignment with ACGME accreditation standards. This role also involves supporting the program in advancing the academic mission of USF and fostering an environment of excellence in clinical care, research, and teaching. Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Must be board certified/eligible in Emergency Medicine. Clinical responsibilities will include patient care at the Tampa General Hospital Emergency Department main Academic site and the South Campus Freestanding Emergency Departments. This position will participate in bedside teaching during overnight shifts; the main academic site has Medical Students and Residents present. As Core Faculty in the Emergency Medicine Residency Program, the individual will serve as a clinical educator, supervising and teaching residents and medical students within the emergency department and providing direct, real-time instruction in clinical decision-making and patient care. Teaching responsibilities include participating in the development and delivery of educational activities for the residency, as well as providing feedback and evaluation of resident performance to support their development. The faculty member participate in resident assessment through service on the Clinical Competency Committee (CCC) and/or Program Evaluation Committee (PEC). Additional duties include contributing to residency recruitment efforts, such as participating in interviews and application review, and engaging in scholarly activity consistent with ACGME expectations for core faculty."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42610": {
      "title": "TGH North Neurohospitalist",
      "description": "Closing Date: 31/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences, and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The USF Department of Neurology is recruiting a Neurohospitalist to provide services to TGH North, a group of hospitals located just to the north of Tampa, in the Crystal River and Spring Hill/Brooksville area. Appointment will be commensurate with experience. Duties will include comprehensive inpatient neurological care for patients admitted with neurological conditions, vascular/stroke and other acute and complex general neurologic care in consultation and follow up. This role focuses on the evaluation, diagnosis, and management of neurological disorders in the hospital setting, working closely with multidisciplinary teams to ensure timely, high-quality, and evidence-based care. On-Call responsibilities will be minimal, and this position will be pure inpatient care. This position is essential to maintaining efficient inpatient neurology services, improving patient flow, and delivering safe, patient-centered neurological care. Duty hours are Mon-Fri, day shifts only beginning at 8 am. QUALIFICATIONS MINIMUM: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor on the Clinical track. ADDITIONAL MINIMUM: Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full unrestricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. MUST BE BOARD CERTIFIED/ELIGIBLE IN: Neurology. Additional relevant fellowship training and board certifications are a plus but not required. CLINICAL- 95%- Responsible for providing medical care, inpatient hospital examinations/diagnosis and treatment/therapy. Prepares medical records and correspondence related to patient care. Conducts health counseling in preventative medicine for patients with the guidance of the attending doctor. OTHER - 5%-Other duties as assigned Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a state university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42696": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Headache",
      "description": "Closing Date: 31/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Neurology at the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine seeks academically-oriented Headache Neurologists to provide both outpatient and inpatient clinical care. Candidates must have an M.D. and be licensed or eligible for medical licensure in the State of Florida. Appointment will be commiserate with experience, and skilled clinical neurologists with backgrounds in private practice will also be considered. This position will include opportunities for medical student and resident teaching, and participation in a large, diverse department having comprehensive divisions providing state of the art services and clinical trials in Headache Neurology. USF Health is the major provider of tertiary care medical service to Tampa Bay and much of Florida's west coast; this region includes some of the world's most beautiful beaches and largest recreation centers. As a place to live, Tampa bay offers an excellent quality of life, as both a major metro area and a world renowned coastal resort community with a very reasonable cost of living. MINIMUM: This position requires licensure to practice medicine in accordance with Chapter 458, Florida Statutes, plus four years of appropriate experience. Completion of a residency program may substitute for the required experience. Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Responsible for providing medical care, including outpatient and in hospital examinations/diagnosis and treatment/therapy. Prepares medical records and correspondence related to patient care. Conducts health counseling in preventative medicine for patients"
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42300": {
      "title": "Open Rank-Lung Transplant Pulmonologist",
      "description": "Closing Date: 14/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine and Tampa General Hospital Transplant Institute is seeking a Lung Transplant, ECMO, and Cystic Fibrosis Pulmonologist to expand our Center for Advanced Lung Disease and Lung Transplant program. This full-time clinical position is at the Assistant Professor to Associate Professor Level. As a physician in the Center for Advanced Lung Disease, the candidate will work in a highly collaborative environment with CT surgeons, intensivists, and other transplant specialists. Pulmonologists within the program are responsible for the entire continuum of care for advanced lung disease patients including pre- and post-lung transplant in both inpatient and outpatient settings. As part of the academic team, the candidate will be expected to participate in the multidisciplinary ICU rounds with colleagues, residents and fellows, as well as participate in scholarly activities including clinical research and medical education. Successful candidates must have a medical degree or equivalent and have passed specialty Boards in Medicine and Pulmonary and Critical Care. The Tampa General Hospital Transplant Institute, in collaboration with the University of South Florida, has created the only Center for Advanced Lung Disease and Lung Transplant Program on the West Coast of Florida serving a population of almost 5 million people. The lung transplant program is part of a comprehensive multi-organ transplant institute (e.g., heart, lung, liver, kidney, and pancreas), which is consistently one of the largest transplant centers in the nation. This is an exciting opportunity to join a dynamic and growing transplant program. Minimal: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Preferred: Lung Transplant training and/ or experience. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Must be board certified/eligible in Internal Medicine/Pulmonary and Critical Care Clinical-Provides Pulmonary Transplant Services for the Center for Advanced Lung Disease at TGH and/ or other affiliated hospitals and clinics. Teaching-Participate in the USF fellowship program and be expected to develop didactic teaching sessions, grand rounds, clinical teaching of residents and students. Administrative-Complete all charting within 48 hours of encounter. Participate in all trainings and required USF/ TGH credentialing and regulatory documentation. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44308": {
      "title": "Dorothy Benjamin Term Scientist in Memory Disorders",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physicians’ Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The University of South Florida College of Nursing is one of 14 colleges at USF, a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities. Nationally recognized as a leader in nursing education and research, the College of Nursing serves around 2,000 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students each year. The Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) continues to be ranked No. 1 in Florida by U.S. News & World Report, and the college graduates the most new nurses of any institution in the state. The college has also been recognized as a Center of Excellence by the National League for Nursing, an honor given to only a select number of colleges in the country. Part of USF Health, an academic health center, the College of Nursing is committed to making life better through education, research, and patient care. Through immersive simulation, clinical education, and global engagement, the College of Nursing graduates Bull Nurses who are ready to lead with skill, compassion, and purpose. The University of South Florida College of Nursing is seeking an outstanding research scientist for the position of Dorothy Benjamin Term Scientist in Memory Disorders. The successful candidate is expected to contribute to the research, teaching, and service missions of the College and provide leadership in advancing and expanding memory disorders research within the College of Nursing. We are seeking a collegial, collaborative, and grant-funded faculty member with research interests focused on developing innovative solutions to address health conditions associated with neurocognitive disorders, particularly those affecting memory and other neurodegenerative conditions. The successful candidate will maintain a high level of externally funded research, publish regularly in peer-reviewed journals, disseminate research findings, and promote the translation of research into practice in collaboration with clinical and community partners. The incumbent will mentor junior faculty, clinician-scientists, and students; participate in the development and submission of interdisciplinary grant applications for centers and training programs; and contribute service to the College, University, and profession. The candidate may also teach at the graduate and/or undergraduate levels and will be expected to promote an environment of excellence and collaboration among faculty, staff, trainees, and students. Minimum Qualifications: Earned PhD in a health science field from an accredited institution with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant or Associate or Professor. Additional Minimum Qualifications: If a nurse, must be eligible for licensure as a Registered Nurse (RN) in the State of Florida. Demonstrated record of published research in scientific journals and recognition as a national and/or international authority in the candidate’s field of specialization. Demonstrated evidence of obtaining competitive federal extramural funding (e.g., NIH, NSF, ED). Demonstrated record of research relevant to memory disorders and/or related fields. Preferred Qualifications: Strong record of collaborative extramural research, education, scholarship, and professional service commensurate with appointment as Professor with tenure in an area of specialization represented within the College. Demonstrated record of research excellence, including successful sponsored research proposals and publications in high-quality, relevant journals. Ongoing record of scholarly publications and an active, fundable research agenda focused on memory disorders and/or related research. Demonstrated research project management experience, including budget development and oversight, personnel supervision, and management of funded research projects. Demonstrated ability to represent and advocate for the College of Nursing within the University and with external partners. Demonstrated ability to mentor early-career faculty, particularly in supporting scholarly development and successful progression toward promotion and tenure. PhD in Nursing or a related field. This is an in-person position and requires on-site presence at the College of Nursing. Maintain an active, externally funded program of research focused on memory disorders and/or related neurocognitive or neurodegenerative conditions. Secure and maintain competitive extramural research funding. Publish research findings in high-quality, peer-reviewed scientific journals and disseminate findings through appropriate professional and scientific venues. Promote the translation of research findings into practice through collaboration with clinical, academic, and community partners. Mentor junior faculty, clinician-scientists, postdoctoral scholars, and students in research and scholarly development. Participate in the development and submission of interdisciplinary grant applications, including proposals for research centers and training programs. Collaborate with faculty and researchers across the College, USF Health, the University, and external organizations. Contribute to the teaching mission of the College at the graduate and/or undergraduate level, as appropriate. Participate in service to the College, University, profession, and scientific community. Contribute to the continued growth and visibility of memory disorders research within the College of Nursing."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44296": {
      "title": "Assistant-Associate Professor/School of Social Work",
      "description": "Closing Date: 31/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The University of South Florida, School of Social Work invites applications for two tenure/tenure track Assistant/Associate Professor positions. We encourage applicants who are interested in joining our School of Social Work scholarly faculty in educating social work professionals and contributing to the knowledge base to find solutions to help people in need, address social problems, and to advance human rights and social justice. We are open to applicants whose research agenda focuses on substantive areas of interest (e.g., direct clinical social work practice, health, mental health, policy, community engagement, global health and global mental health, and AI, digital technologies, and simulations). As part of the College of Behavioral and Community Sciences, members of our faculty engage in innovative interdisciplinary, translational, and implementation research focusing on finding solutions to promote the quality of life, health and the safety of diverse populations and communities. Minimum Qualifications: MSW and Ph.D. in Social Work or related area (Ph.D. must be conferred by August 7, 2027). Preferred Qualifications: A demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, peer-reviewed publications, externally funded research or strong potential for securing external funding, and service MSW from a CSWE accredited School of Social Work 2 Years post graduate practice experience Applicants are required to submit the following in support of their application: 1. Cover Letter 2. CV The responsibilities of this position include: teach doctoral, master’s, and undergraduate level courses in Social Work; assist in Ph.D. student research and dissertation studies; and engage in scholarship, research, and grant and contract submissions, and service. Teaching will occur on the Tampa campus for face-to-face classroom instruction (candidates must be available on campus). This is a 9-month tenure/tenure-track continual appointment, subject to annual evaluations. Salary is commensurate with experience. See web site for University and Social Work descriptions: https://www.usf.edu/cbcs/social-work/ First review of applications will be October 9, 2026"
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/41258": {
      "title": "General Neurology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 31/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences, and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. This position will serve as a General Neurologist in the Department of Neurology at the University of South Florida at a rank of Assistant Professor. The successful candidate will be academically oriented and responsible for providing comprehensive medical care and health counseling to patients. Additional responsibilities include conducting health seminars, offering consultative health services, and participating in educational activities. This role provides opportunities to teach medical students, residents, and fellows. MINIMUM: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. ADDITIONAL MINIMUM: Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. CLINICAL- 90%- Responsible for providing medical care, including outpatient and in hospital examinations/diagnosis and treatment/therapy. Prepares medical records and correspondence related to patient care. Conducts health counseling in preventative medicine for patients. TEACHING -5% Conducts teaching to Fellow, residents and medical students in the Department of Neurology. OTHER -5% Other duties as assigned Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a state university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44279": {
      "title": "Open Rank  Inpatient",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html . Support inpatient psychiatry services at a new TGH Behavioral Health Hospital. This position will provide inpatient clinical care and case management to include the diagnosis, treatment and management of patients in an inpatient ED setting. Medical degree from an accredited institution. Completion of an accredited Psychiatry residency training program. Must meet university criteria for faculty appointment to the rank of assistant professor, associate or professor. Candidates must have or be eligible for an unrestricted Florida medical license. This candidate must obtain credentialing with USF Health and Tampa General Hospital. Provides inpatient psychiatry services and call coverage at Tampa General Behavioral Health Hospital to include the assessment, diagnosis and treatment Completes clinical documentation and other tasks as required"
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44281": {
      "title": "Social Emergency Medicine Fellowship Director- Physician",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The USF Department of Emergency Medicine seeks a board certified/board-eligible emergency and fellowship trained social medicine physician, to serve as Social Medicine Fellowship Director and Medical Director of the Gulf Coast Refugee Organization. This full time academic and clinical faculty position combines emergency department practice within the Tampa General Hospital Emergency Department system, including the main academic medical center and the South Campus Freestanding Emergency Departments, with leadership of a fellowship training program in social emergency medicine and health equity, and medical oversight of the Gulf Coast Refugee organization. The physician will practice in a high-acuity, Level I Trauma Center that serves as the primary teaching site for the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine. Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Clinical responsibilities will include patient care at the Tampa General Hospital Emergency Department main Academic site and the South Campus Freestanding Emergency Departments. This position will participate in bedside teaching at the main academic site has Medical Students and Residents present. The Fellowship Director will direct and administer the Social Medicine Fellowship, including curriculum design, fellow recruitment/selection and mentorship. They will mentor fellows in scholarly/research projects, community based advocacy, and career development. They will coordinate fellow rotations across street medicine, refugee health, and other social-medicine clinical settings, and represent the program through SAEM's Social EM and Population Health Fellowship Approval process and national conferences. In addition, they will teach and supervise emergency medicine residents and medical students, both on shift and through contributions to resident/student curricula on social determinants of health. Responsible to a chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a state university. Responsible for teaching, researching, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44283": {
      "title": "Emergency Medicine Nocturnist Physician",
      "description": "Closing Date: 26/01/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. This full-time clinical faculty position in Adult Emergency Medicine will provide overnight (nocturnist) patient care within the Tampa General Hospital Emergency Department system, including the main academic medical center and the South Campus Freestanding Emergency Departments. The physician will practice in a high-acuity, Level I Trauma Center that serves as the primary teaching site for the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine. This is a night-shift position offering the opportunity to deliver high-quality, evidence-based emergency care in an academic environment that supports teaching, collaboration, and innovation across multidisciplinary teams. Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Clinical responsibilities will include overnight (night-shift) patient care at the Tampa General Hospital Emergency Department main Academic site and the South Campus Freestanding Emergency Departments. This position will participate in bedside teaching during overnight shifts; the main academic site has Medical Students and Residents present. Bedside teaching of residents and medical students, which are present across all academic sites. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44285": {
      "title": "Assistant-Associate Professor (Tenure Track/Tenured) for the Marriage and Family Therapy Program",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States Position Description: The Department of Child and Family Studies in the College of Behavioral and Community Sciences at the University of South Florida seeks applicants for a full-time on campus, 9-month, tenure-earning or tenured faculty position in the Marriage and Family Therapy Program at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor, commensurate with qualifications and experience. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued growth and excellence of the Marriage and Family Therapy Program through research, teaching, graduate student mentorship, and service. The department seeks applicants whose scholarship advances the understanding of individuals, couples, families, and communities through systemic, relational, developmental, behavioral health, prevention, or family science perspectives. Candidates should demonstrate the potential to establish and maintain an active program of research, contribute to graduate education, collaborate across disciplines, and support the mission of the Department of Child and Family Studies. Applicants from Marriage and Family Therapy, Family Science, Human Development and Family Science, Family Studies, Counseling, Psychology, Social Work, Public Health, or closely related disciplines are encouraged to apply. Preference will be given to candidates whose expertise complements the educational mission of the Marriage and Family Therapy Program and who demonstrate the ability to contribute to graduate education, scholarly productivity, and interdisciplinary collaboration. Candidates who meet COAMFTE Core Faculty qualifications or possess experience in accredited Marriage and Family Therapy programs are especially encouraged to apply. The Department seeks a faculty member who will contribute to the continued growth of the Marriage and Family Therapy Program by strengthening its research enterprise, expanding graduate student research opportunities, fostering interdisciplinary collaboration, and advancing scholarship that promotes the health and well-being of individuals, couples, families, and communities. Minimum Qualifications: An earned doctorate (or ABD with degree conferred prior to appointment) in Marriage and Family Therapy, Family Science, Human Development and Family Science, Family Studies, Counseling, Psychology, Social Work, Public Health, or a closely related discipline. Evidence of an active research agenda with the potential for sustained scholarly productivity leading to external funding. Eligibility for appointment at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor at the University of South Florida. Preferred Qualifications: Established record of peer-reviewed scholarship focused on couples, families, relationships, behavioral health, prevention, resilience, human development, or family science. Experience obtaining or pursuing externally funded research. Experience with undergraduate and/or graduate-level teaching. Eligibility to serve as COAMFTE Core Faculty. Licensed or eligible to be licensed in the state of Florida (LMFT or equivalent) Applicants are required to submit the following in support of their application: Cover Letter CV Statement of Research Interests Statement of Teaching Philosophy Two Letters of Recommendation Position open until filled. Review of applications will begin on October 15, 2026 Contact information: Everette Coffman; coffman3@usf.edu Essential Functions The successful candidate will be expected to: Develop and maintain an active program of research and scholarly productivity consistent with expectations for a faculty member at a Research 1 university. Pursue external funding opportunities that support research, graduate education, and interdisciplinary collaboration. Teach graduate courses in both Fall and Spring semesters within the Marriage and Family Therapy curriculum or other departmental offerings aligned with the candidate's area of expertise. Mentor graduate students through research, thesis supervision, and professional development. Participate in departmental, college, university, and professional service activities. Support the mission and accreditation standards of the Marriage and Family Therapy Program, including clinical education and supervision when appropriate to the candidate's qualifications."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42833": {
      "title": "Neonatologist and Director of USF BPD Program – Neonatology Division - Open Rank Faculty",
      "description": "Closing Date: 24/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Pediatrics at the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine is seeking an Open Rank faculty member to serve the clinical and educational missions of the Division of Neonatology. The division is based at Tampa General Hospital (TGH) in Tampa, FL. TGH is a 1,018-bed teaching hospital affiliated with the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine. It is a private not-for-profit hospital and one of the most comprehensive medical facilities in west central Florida, serving a dozen counties with a population of over 4 million. In addition to being a Level 1 trauma center, it also has a Level 3 NICU. The 82-bed Jennifer Leigh Muma NICU is a designated Regional Perinatal Intensive Care Center designated by the State of Florida to deliver the highest level of medical care to premature and sick infants, and to women with high-risk pregnancies. USF/TGH Neonatology also participates in the Florida Perinatal Quality Collaborative, a statewide initiative to improve maternal and infant health outcomes in Florida. We are seeking a dedicated physician—preferably with expertise in Bronchopulmonary Dysplasia (BPD)—to join our team. This position may also include serving as BPD Physician Lead to Tampa General Hospital, with opportunities to lead program development, quality initiatives, and strategic growth. Minimum: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. BC/BE in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Additional Requirements: Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. MUST BE BOARD CERTIFIED/ELIGIBLE IN: Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine. Preferred: 5 years of professional neonatal/perinatal medicine experience. Experience with the national BPD collaborative. CLINICAL - The position includes the management of patients in the Jennifer Leigh Muma Neonatal Intensive Care Unit at Tampa General Hospital. TEACHING - The faculty member will contribute to departmental teaching programs for neonatal fellows, pediatric residents, and medical students. He/she will participate in the preparation and organization of new educational programs as well as university and departmental committee. RESEARCH -The faculty member will be encouraged to participate in ongoing research in the Division of Neonatology and contribute to divisional efforts to seek funding for extramural research. ADMINISTRATIVE -Act as the Bronchopulmonary Dysplasia (BPD) physician lead at Tampa General Hospital. OTHER - Other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42666": {
      "title": "Open Rank-Gastroenterology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of Internal Medicine at University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking an Open Rank physician to perform gastroenterology services at the Morsani Center and Tampa General Hospital. This is a full-time 12-month salaried faculty appointment and carries with it attending staff privileges at Tampa General Hospital (TGH) and affiliated hospitals. MINIMUM: Doctoral/Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate or Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Candidate must be Board-certified/eligible in Internal Medicine and/or Gastroenterology. PREFERRED: USF is especially interested in candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of the academic community through their research, teaching, and/or service. CLINICAL: Provides General GI ambulatory clinics, inpatient Call & Coverage, and endoscopy time, Participation in clinical teaching for medical students, residents and fellows in clinic, endoscopy center and hospital ward settings. ADMINISTRATIVE: Reviewing charts, phone calls with patients, finishing notes, answering MyChart messages, etc. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44081": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction - Mechanical Eng",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States Organizational Summary: The Department ( https://www.usf.edu/engineering/me/ ) has 30 full-time faculty members and offers B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. degrees in Mechanical and Aerospace Engineering, as well as a minor in Aerospace Engineering. The Department's faculty members collaborate with all departments in the College of Engineering, as well as the Colleges of Medicine, Arts & Sciences, Marine Science, Education, Nursing, and Public Health. The Department also has strong ties with numerous USF centers, including the Nanotechnology Research and Education Center ( http://www.nrec.usf.edu ), Center for Urban Transportation Research ( https://www.cutr.usf.edu ), Center for Assistive Rehabilitation Robotics & Technologies ( http://carrt.eng.usf.edu ), Clean Energy Research Center ( http://cerc.eng.usf.edu ), H. Lee Moffitt Cancer Center, and Global Center for Hearing and Speech Research. Established in 1964 and led by Dean Levi Thompson, the College of Engineering at the University of South Florida is ranked #56 among public institutions (#89 overall) by U.S. News & World Report’s 2025-2026 engineering graduate school rankings . The college serves more than 3,500 students, offering seven bachelor’s programs, which are ABET-accredited, as well as nine master’s and seven doctoral degrees. The college is actively engaged in local and global research activities with $46.9 million in research expenditures for the fiscal year 2024-2025. The college has 12 major research centers and institutes and is actively engaged in local and global research activities focused on sustainability, biomedical engineering, computing technology and transportation. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg, Sarasota-Manatee and USF Health. USF is recognized by U.S. News & World Report as a top 50 public university and the best value in Florida. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine as the No. 1 medical school in Florida and in the highest tier nationwide. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $738 million in research funding in 2024 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of more than $6 billion. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . Minimum Desired Qualifications : The position requires a doctoral degree in Aerospace Engineering or Mechanical Engineering or a closely related field from an accredited institution. The College of Engineering seeks candidates with a proven track record of teaching. Preferred Qualifications : The candidate should have demonstrated excellence in teaching and teaching publications, the potential for development of laboratories, and a strong commitment to mentoring undergraduate and graduate students. Position Summary: The Department of Mechanical Engineering at the University of South Florida invites applications for the following: A non-tenure track faculty position in Aerospace or Mechanical Engineering. Applicants with backgrounds in aeronautics and astronautics, as well as in all areas of mechanical engineering, are encouraged to apply. The position is available at the Assistant Professor of Instruction levels and is expected to commence in the Spring of 2027 or earlier. An application package should include a 1) cover letter, 2) detailed curriculum vitae, 3) teaching interests, 4) one-page statement of teaching and vision, and 5) contact information of at least four professional references. Applicants must electronically submit the application packet as a single PDF file. Applications will be considered starting immediately and will continue until the position is filled."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44082": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Instruction - Mechanical Eng",
