    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42726": {
      "title": "Regional Medical Director for Child Abuse Pediatrics - Clinical Faculty Position – Assistant/Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Pediatrics in the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine is seeking a clinical faculty member who is fellowship-trained and/or board-certified in Pediatrics, Family Medicine or Emergency Medicine with experience working in Child Abuse Pediatrics. BC/BE in Child Abuse Pediatrics is preferred, but not required. The position offers excellent opportunities for teaching, research, advocacy and a role in the development of a Center of Excellence at Muma Children’s Hospital at Tampa General Hospital (TGH). TGH partners with USF Health and is the primary teaching hospital. Muma Children’s Hospital is West Central Florida’s only ACS verified Pediatric Level I Trauma Center and is establishing a The Child Well‑Being Center of Excellence (COE), as a first‑in‑Florida, statewide‑recognized regional hub for pediatric trauma, child protection, and injury prevention. This position would play a crucial role in that development. The selected candidate will also serve as the Florida Department of Health Regional Medical Director for the Child Abuse Pediatrics program, covering both Hillsborough and Polk Counties. This position provides direct consultation and coordination with other physicians and healthcare workers in the evaluation and management of suspected cases of child maltreatment/abuse. The position includes both outpatient care and inpatient consultative services and provides clinical supervision to those providing medical care. The program works closely with multiple community agencies, including DCF and law enforcement. Currently, there is one USF pediatrician as part of the USF Health Child Abuse Program (CAP), who is also the Statewide Medical Director. The USF Health Child Abuse Program provides inpatient services, primarily at Muma Children’s Hospital at TGH as well as some community hospitals. TGH has an ACS certified Pediatric Trauma Program, and the USF Child Abuse program collaborates with the trauma team for clinical care, education and research. The USF Health Child Abuse Program provides outpatient services through the community Child Advocacy Center at Mary Lee's House, located in Tampa, and medical director coverage for the Children’s Home Society in Polk County. Both locations include a team of nurse practitioners, case coordinators, a team supervisor and psychology support. Minimum: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Board Certified in Pediatrics, Family Medicine or Emergency Medicine with prior experience working in Child Abuse Pediatrics with demonstrated expertise in managing child abuse and neglect cases. Completion of a 3-year, ACGME accredited Child Abuse Pediatrics fellowship is preferred, but not required. Additional Requirements: Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Clinical: The position includes both outpatient care and inpatient consultative services. Clinical duties include call coverage per the Child Abuse Program call schedule. The position is based out of Mary Lee’s House in Tampa, FL but regular travel to surrounding counties is required. Outpatient care and inpatient consultative care is provided by medical staff within the CAP program. This position provides supervision-oversight to those providing direct clinical coverage. Patient volume ranges from 1200-1500 in Hillsborough and 800-1000 in Polk County. Teaching: The selected candidate will be expected to contribute to departmental teaching programs involving residents, medical students, and house staff. He/she will participate in the preparation/organization of new educational programs as well as participation in the university/college assigned committees. The individual will be expected to effectively utilize his/her clinical practice as a teaching resource. Both students and residents will attend the outpatient clinics. Research: Collaborative effort within the Department and the University will be encouraged. Administrative: Serve as the Regional CPT Medical Director for Polk, Hardee, Highlands, and Hillsborough counties. Provide administrative oversight, direction and supervision as directed by the Regional Medical Director for Child Protection agreement. Perform all tasks related to Regional Medical Director for Child Protection Agreement. The Regional Medical Director will work with the Department of Children and Families and Law Enforcement in their investigations of alleged abuse. He/she will follow the Florida Department of Health Child Protection Team Handbook related to overall program deliverables and operations. He/she will provide recommendations and serve as a subject matter expert for community health providers, in court, on committees, and other community providers or outreach events. This position will act as the lead liaison of the child abuse team with the TGH Muma Children's Hospital service line leadership and participate in the Center of Excellence program development. Other: Other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42728": {
      "title": "Child Abuse Pediatrics Clinical Faculty Position -  Assistant/Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Pediatrics in the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine is seeking a clinical faculty member who is fellowship-trained and/or board-certified in Pediatrics, Family Medicine or Emergency Medicine with experience working in Child Abuse Pediatrics. BC/BE in Child Abuse Pediatrics is preferred, but not required. This position will join a growing team at Muma Children’s Hospital at Tampa General Hospital (TGH). Muma Children’s Hospital at TGH is establishing a The Child Well‑Being Center of Excellence (COE), as a first‑in‑Florida, statewide‑recognized regional hub for pediatric trauma, child protection, and injury prevention. As part of the only ACS‑verified Level I Pediatric Trauma Center in West Central Florida, this physician will help lead a multidisciplinary program dedicated to improving outcomes for vulnerable children across Hillsborough, Polk, and surrounding counties. The physician will provide comprehensive clinical services—including inpatient consultations, outpatient evaluations, forensic assessments, and multidisciplinary team collaboration - while working closely with the Department of Children and Families (DCF), child advocacy centers, law enforcement, and our hospital partner. In addition to direct patient care, the physician will contribute to program growth, support ACS Pediatric Level I Trauma requirements, engage in teaching and academic activities with USF Health, and participate in research and quality initiatives. This role offers a unique opportunity to help build Florida’s first Child Well‑Being Center of Excellence and shape a regional model of care for vulnerable children. Minimum: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Board Certified in Pediatrics, Family Medicine or Emergency Medicine with prior experience working in Child Abuse Pediatrics with demonstrated expertise in managing child abuse and neglect cases Completion of a 3-year, ACGME accredited Child Abuse Pediatrics fellowship is preferred, but not required. Additional Minimum: Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. CLINICAL: The position includes both outpatient care and inpatient consultative services. Clinical duties include call coverage per the Child Abuse Program call schedule. Outpatient care is primarily based out of Mary Lee’s House in Tampa, FL. TEACHING: The selected candidate will be expected to contribute to departmental teaching programs involving residents, medical students, and house staff. He/she will participate in the preparation/organization of new educational programs as well as participation in the university/college assigned committees. The individual will be expected to effectively utilize his/her clinical practice as a teaching resource. Both students and residents will attend the outpatient clinics. RESEARCH: Collaborative effort within the Department and the University will be encouraged. OTHER: Other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities.Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43389": {
      "title": "APRN/Instr. I",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Healthcare Support JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Pediatrics at the University of South Florida is seeking an Advanced Practitioner Registered Nurse or Physician Assistant that will function within a clinical team of professionals working autonomously in relation to the complete management of children and young people, complementing other professionals in the delivery of high-quality service provision. This position uses clinical judgment and autonomous decision-making skills in relation to assessment, diagnosis, and management of patients, and undertaking a range of clinical actions and professional boundaries following assessment of patient need and care requirements. MINIMUM: Master's or Medical degree from of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise an accredited institution in an appropriate field qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. ADDITIONAL MINIMUM: This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Preferred Qualifications: Experience as a Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant in a Pediatrics facility. Spanish or Haitian Creole language proficiency preferred. Clinical - 90% Performs professional nurse practitioner or physician assistant care according to established standards, practices, protocols and in accordance with the Florida Practice act for Advanced Nurse Practitioners. This includes performing initial components of assessment of patient condition, including history and physical etc. Provides clinical teaching experience for Masters of Nurse Practitioner and Physician Assistant students. Administrative - 10% Clinical administrative duties such as closing encounters, patient correspondence, clinical tasks, etc. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44183": {
      "title": "Advanced Practice Provider (APRN or PA)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The USF Department of Otolaryngology–Head & Neck Surgery is seeking two collaborative, motivated Advanced Practice Providers (APRN or PA) to join our growing academic team in clinic-based roles at the USF South Tampa Center and Morsani Center. Each APP will work with a different group of subspecialty faculty, building an independent clinic template while supporting faculty practices day to day. This is an opportunity to work alongside dynamic, subspecialty-trained faculty and our Otolaryngology residents within one of Florida's leading academic ENT programs—a department recognized among U.S. News & World Report's top 50 ENT service lines for five consecutive years and ranked among the top 20 nationally for research funding by the Blue Ridge Institute. New graduates and experienced APPs are both encouraged to apply; structured onboarding, faculty mentorship, and graduated clinical autonomy are central to how we develop our team. Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Previous experience working in Otolaryngology/ENT. CLINICAL – Build an independent outpatient clinic template under direct faculty support, with the goal of progressively expanding scope as expertise develops. Support faculty clinics through comprehensive patient evaluations, including focused medical histories, physical examinations, and ordering and interpretation of diagnostic studies. Develop and implement treatment plans for patients with a broad range of otolaryngologic conditions, prescribing medications and therapies within scope of practice and in accordance with departmental protocols. Provide postoperative care and follow-up, including management of complications and coordination of additional therapies. Learn and progressively perform basic Otolaryngology procedures, including flexible laryngoscopy, cerumen management, and nasal endoscopy/debridement, with structured faculty teaching. Triage patient phone calls and clinical inbox messages, including prescription renewals, perioperative concerns, and urgent scheduling needs. Partner with our nursing team on clinical education and protocol development, from procedure setup to patient instruction. Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams—including audiology, speech-language pathology, and oncology—to ensure coordinated care. DIVISIONAL & QUALITY – Take ownership of a divisional program area, such as cancer survivorship, in partnership with faculty leadership. Contribute to quality improvement work focused on access, transitions of care, patient experience, and outcomes. Contribute to workflow improvements and EPIC optimization in collaboration with the clinical leadership team. TEACHING & RESEARCH – Teach at the bedside and in clinic with our residents and rotating medical students and participate in departmental conferences and multidisciplinary tumor boards. Opportunities to join departmental clinical research and scholarly projects—with co-authorship and presentation at regional and national meetings—are available to those interested. Pursue ongoing professional development through CME and specialty society engagement (e.g., SPAO-HNS, AAPA, SOHN, AANP). ADMINISTRATIVE – Complete clinical documentation accurately and in a timely manner. Manage patient-specific paperwork on rotation with the broader APP and faculty team, including FMLA, disability, and procedural authorization documentation. OTHER – Performs other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42563": {
      "title": "APP - Hospitalist. Instr.I",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Neurology is seeking an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) or Physician Assistant (PA) to join the University of South Florida Neurology Hospitalist in the in the Crystal River and Spring Hill/Brooksville areas. The Advanced Practice Provider (APP) Neurology Hospitalist delivers comprehensive inpatient neurological care to patients admitted with acute and complex neurological conditions. Working collaboratively with neurologists, hospitalists, nurses, and multidisciplinary care teams, the APP evaluates, diagnoses, and manages a wide range of neurological disorders in the hospital setting. This role focuses on timely, evidence-based patient care, including conducting neurological assessments, ordering and interpreting diagnostic tests, initiating treatment plans, and monitoring patient progress throughout hospitalization. The APP also provides patient and family education, participates in discharge planning, and ensures continuity of care across services. Duty hours are Mon-Fri, day shifts only. The APP Neurology Hospitalist plays a vital role in improving patient outcomes, supporting clinical efficiency, and maintaining high standards of neurological care within the inpatient environment. Master's or Medical degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Clinical - 95%-The APRN/PA will be under the general supervision and in accordance with the standardized procedure. The position is responsible for performing inpatient physical examinations and treating common episodic and chronic healthcare problems, counseling patient and families, monitoring patient's progress, assisting with medical research projects. Works in collaboration with healthcare team members, consulting and referring as appropriate, but retains responsibility for ongoing clinical management of the patient. Updates patient's records, noting changes in medication and responses of patients. Notifies physicians of changes in patient condition. Other - 5%-Performs other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a state university. Responsible for teaching, service, and related activities. May be responsible for research and/or academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42631": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Pediatric Gastroenterology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physicians’ Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of Pediatrics at the University of South Florida (USF) Morsani College of Medicine is seeking a faculty member at the open rank to join its established Division of Pediatric Gastroenterology. The division offers a broad clinical scope within a strong academic environment and promotes robust multidisciplinary collaboration across pediatric subspecialties. This position is well suited for a motivated, collaborative physician seeking an academic clinical practice. The successful candidate will be expected to provide independent inpatient and outpatient care, including endoscopic procedures. Applicants with established or emerging expertise in a focused clinical area within pediatric gastroenterology are particularly encouraged to apply. The Division of Pediatric Gastroenterology at USF is known for its collegial culture and commitment to team-based care, academic growth, and excellent patient outcomes. Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Candidate must be Board Certified/Board Eligible in Pediatric Gastroenterology. Teaching Duties: Participates in the educational and training activities of the USF Department of Pediatrics which include teaching of residents and medical students, committee membership, research and quality improvement projects, lectures, and grand rounds. Clinical Duties: Provides inpatient coverage at Tampa General Hospital for pediatric gastroenterology patients, performs endoscopies, and manages patients in the outpatient setting."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42642": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Pediatric Neurology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences, and the USF Physician's Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html USF Pediatric Neurology has two dedicated beds for sleep and video-EEG monitoring at the Children's Hospital located within our partner hospital Tampa General Hospital (TGH). The Children's Hospital houses a level three Neonatal Intensive Care Unit (NICU) and a Pediatric Intensive Care Unit (PICU), one of only two PICUs in Florida and one of only 13 units nationwide awarded the Silver Beacon Award for Excellence by the American Association of Critical-Care Nurses. The expanding Division of Pediatric Neurology in the Department of Pediatrics at the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine seeks two open-rank pediatric neurologists for full-time, clinical, non-tenure earning faculty positions. The academic rank will be commensurate with the candidate's qualifications and experience. We are looking for neurologists with strong clinical skills and a passion for pediatrics to join our team in diagnosing and treating patients ages 0-21 who travel to USF Health for care from all over Florida. Our division comprises two board-certified neurologists, a nurse practitioner, and a registered nurse. On top of providing pediatric neurology services, one of our physicians also cares for children and adults alike with sleep disorders. Collaboration is at the heart of USF Health. One such example is the tandem work we perform with comprehensive adult epilepsy and stroke teams. To fill a critical niche, we are currently building a dedicated pediatrics program, allowing us the opportunity to grow our division and extend our reach even more. This opportunity is best suited for a motivated physician desiring a clinical practice in an academic setting. Clinical responsibilities will include providing outpatient care to children and adolescents at ambulatory sites and serving as an attending on a dedicated neurology inpatient service at TGH. Apart from fulfilling those, a successful candidate will also be expected to further the department's mission by teaching the house staff, medical students, and residents. There will also be ample research opportunities should the provider choose to participate. Qualifications MINIMUM: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals. Completed Child Neurology residency. Board-eligible Must possess or be able to obtain an unrestricted Florida medical license before start of employment. PREFERRED: Board-certified. Fellowship in any of the following: neonatal neurology, epilepsy, headache, stroke, behavioral neurology is a plus. Experience in academic medicine. Additional fellowships in neonatal neurology, epilepsy, headache, stroke, or behavioral neurology are a plus but not required. Responsibilities Diagnose and treat neurological conditions. Provide inpatient coverage. Participate in the education and training of house staff, medical students, and residents. Perform other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44185": {
      "title": "NICU-NNP APRN/PA Instructor I",
      "description": "Closing Date: 09/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The APRN/PA will act in accordance with Florida Statutes for the Nurse Practitioners Act. The care and management of critically ill infants requiring hospitalization in a level IV neonatal intensive care unit. This NICU Nurse Practitioner will cover night and/or day shifts as assigned including weekend coverage. The Neonatal Intensive Care Unit is based at Tampa General Hospital (TGH) in Tampa, FL. TGH is a 1,018-bed teaching hospital affiliated with the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine. It is a private not-for-profit hospital and one of the most comprehensive medical facilities in west central Florida, serving a dozen counties with a population of over 4 million. In addition to being a level one trauma center, it has a level 3 NICU. The 82-bed Jennifer Leigh Muma NICU is a designated Regional Perinatal Intensive Care Center designated by the State of Florida to deliver the highest level of medical care to premature and sick infants, and to women with high-risk pregnancies. USF/TGH Neonatology also participates in the Florida Perinatal Quality Collaborative, a statewide initiative to improve maternal and infant health outcomes in Florida. Neonatal services include a Neonatal Transport Team, Fetal Care Center, and Whole-Body Cooling. Pediatric subspecialties available for collaborative treatment of neonatal patients including Neurology, Neurosurgery, Ophthalmology, ENT, Cardiology, Pulmonology, Gastroenterology, Endocrinology, Hematology/Oncology, Nephrology, Metabolic Genetics. Minimum: Educational Requirements: Master’s Degree in Nursing: ARNP training; Florida License. BLS/AED certification is required and must be maintained. Any equivalent combination of experience and education. Experience Requirements: 2-5 years; at least 2 years of experience evaluating pediatric patients (2 years’ experience assessing neonates preferred) Minimum 1-year nursing experience in a physician’s office or clinic experience in an ambulatory health care facility preferred. BLS/AED certification is required and must be maintained. ACLS or PALS Master’s degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Must be board certified/eligible in. Clinical: Ongoing evaluation and management of neonates and infants requiring care in the neonatal intensive care unit, participation in multidisciplinary rounds, and coordination of care with ancillary staff and family. Attendance at high-risk deliveries and immediate stabilization of critically ill neonates under the supervision of the attending Neonatologist. Documentation of all orders, procedures, and progress notes on the patient's medical record. Performs procedures necessary for the care of neonates and infants in the intensive care unit including endotracheal intubation, umbilical line placement, PICC line placement, lumbar punctures, and peripheral arterial lines. Teaching: Supervision of pediatric residents and participation in the teaching of APP students, pediatric residents and medical students. Administrative: Participates in QA projects, educational sessions for clinical staff and attends scheduled organizational sessions. Other: Performs other duties as assigned by Chair. Preferred: Experience as an Advanced Practice Provider in a family medicine or pediatrics. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42942": {
      "title": "Open Rank Breast Surgeon",
      "description": "Closing Date: 31/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at https://health.usf.edu/ The University of South Florida (USF) Department of Surgery and Tampa General Hospital (TGH) is seeking a breast surgical oncologist to join the Division of Surgical Oncology. This is a full-time faculty appointment that carries with it attending staff privileges at Tampa General Hospital (TGH) and affiliated hospitals. TGH is a level 1 trauma center that serves as a tertiary care facility serving south central and west Florida. The successful candidate must be a BC/BE General Surgeon; be eligible for medical licensure in the State of Florida; and eligible to work in the United States. USF and affiliates partner to sponsor a nationally recognized General Surgery residency program. Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor. For Associate/Full Professor Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must have current, unrestricted medical licensure in the State of Florida or be eligible for unrestricted medical licensure in the State of Florida. Candidate must be Board Certified in General Surgery or Board Eligible in General Surgery. Candidates must be experienced surgeons in breast surgery with extensive knowledge and experience in clinical trials, demonstrated excellence in clinical care of patients with breast diseases, both benign and malignant. This role will require significant interaction with a multidisciplinary team of individuals, including medical and radiation oncology faculty. Actively participate in didactic education of multiple learners including residents, fellows, and medical students. Supervise, mentor, and train surgical residents and fellows."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44174": {
      "title": "Ophthalmologist Cornea Open Rank",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of Ophthalmology at the Morsani College of Medicine, University of South Florida is seeking for a 0.5 cFTE (open rank) position to join our Cornea/Comprehensive Ophthalmology clinical care team. This position will provide outpatient care at the USF Health Eye Institute, will supervise residents and fellows during their rotations, and will provide call coverage to Tampa General Hospital. Salary = C ommensurate with experience. Medical degree from an accredited institution. Completion of an accredited Ophthalmology residency training program. Must meet university criteria for faculty appointment to the rank of assistant professor, associate or professor. Candidates must have or be eligible for an unrestricted Florida medical license. This candidate must obtain credentialing with USF Health. If clinical, Board Certified/Eligible in: Cornea/Comprehensive Ophthalmology Resident, fellow, and medical student supervision and teaching. Provides outpatient retinal care to patients at the USF Health Eye Institute. Provides TGH call coverage."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44175": {
      "title": "Retina Open Rank",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of Ophthalmology at the Morsani College of Medicine, University of South Florida is seeking for a Ratina Faculty (open rank) position to join its clinical care team. This position will provide outpatient care at the USF Health Eye Institute, will supervise residents and fellows during their rotations, and will provide call coverage to Tampa General Hospital. Salary = Com mensurate with experience. Medical degree from an accredited institution. Completion of an accredited Ophthalmology residency training program. Must meet university criteria for faculty appointment to the rank of assistant professor, associate or professor. Candidates must have or be eligible for an unrestricted Florida medical license. This candidate must obtain credentialing with USF Health. Candidates must be Board Certified/Board Eligible in Retina. Resident, fellow, and medical student supervision and teaching Provides outpatient retinal care to patients at the USF Health Eye Institute. Provides TGH call coverage. Performs other duties as assigned by Department Chair."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42699": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Surgical Oncology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 31/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Tampa General Physicians (USFTGP). USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html ORGANIZATIONAL SUMMARY: The Department of Surgery at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking an academic Open Rank - Surgical Oncology/HPB Faculty to join the Division of Oncology Surgery. The University of South Florida, Department of Surgery invites applications for a mid-career Academic Surgical Oncologist with expertise in HBP surgery and strong interest in advancing our robotic HBP program. This is an exciting opportunity to join one of the nation's fastest growing academic health systems. USF Morsani College of Medicine has earned U.S. News and World Report Tier 1 designation for research, placing it among the top 16 research intensive medical schools for the second consecutive year. In addition, the Department of Surgery is ranked amongst the Top 50 departments for NIH funding. Tampa General Hospital Cancer Institute, despite its young age, has been recognized among the Top 10% of cancer centers nationally, ranked # 78 in Cancer Care for 2026 nationally. Tampa General Hospital has established substantial investment at the Cancer Institute as well as in advanced Minimally Invasive Surgery. Candidates should be Board Certified in General Surgery and fellowship trained in Complex Surgical Oncology or HBP Surgery. Demonstrated expertise in HBP surgery and strong interest in robotic surgery is highly preferred. Applicants with a record in academic scholarship are encouraged to apply. Associate Professor and Professor level candidates are welcomed, although exceptional Assistant Professor candidates will also be considered. Faculty appointment at USF Morsani School of Medicine with Academic Rank commensurate with experience. MINIMUM: Doctoral or Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Candidates should be Board Certified in General Surgery and fellowship trained in Complex Surgical Oncology or HBP Surgery. Demonstrated expertise in HBP surgery and strong interest in robotic surgery is highly preferred. Applicants with a record in academic scholarship are encouraged to apply. Associate Professor and Professor level candidates are welcomed, although exceptional Assistant Professor candidates will also be considered. Faculty appointment at USF Morsani School of Medicine with Academic Rank commensurate with experience. Candidates must be Board Certified/Board Eligible in General Surgery. Provide quality bedside teaching to students and residents. Complete medical student and resident evaluation in timely fashion. Participate in weekly M&M and resident education. Active participation and enrollment in clinical trials. Opportunity to enhance an already existing HBP robotic program within a rapidly expanding cancer center. High Volume and expanding referral base. Multiple organized Tumor Boards and close collaboration with Advanced Endoscopists, Medical and Radiation Oncology, Genetics and Palliative care. Participation in teaching Surgical Residents and Medical Students. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, service, and related activities. May be responsible for research and/or academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42989": {
      "title": "Geriatrics Open Rank",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of Psychiatry at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking a geriatric psychiatrist to join its outpatient care team. This position will provide outpatient clinical services at the Byrd Institute and will conduct and manage various clinical trials. Medical degree from an accredited institution. Completion of an accredited Psychiatry residency training program. Must meet university criteria for faculty appointment to the rank of assistant professor, associate or professor. Candidates must have or be eligible for an unrestricted Florida medical license. This candidate must obtain credentialing with USF Health. If clinical, Board Certified/Eligible in: PSYCHIATRY Geriatric Psychiatry experience Research: Supports various clinical trials including conducting medical assessments, overseeing study interventions and assessments, data collection and overall coordination of research trials according to protocols. Clinical: Provides outpatient psychiatric clinical care to include the evaluation, diagnosis, assessment, treatment and care of adult patients. Completes open encounters and other clinical documentation in a timely manner."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42676": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Vice Chair Education",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences, and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USFTGP. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Obstetrics & Gynecology (OB/GYN) at the University of South Florida is recruiting a Vice Chair of Education to direct and grow our academic mission across all our educational and training programs. We seek an individual with a demonstrated commitment to innovation in education and creating a learning environment of inquiry. The department has a robust OB/GYN residency program comprised of 24 residents and ACGME-accredited fellowships in Gynecologic Oncology, Maternal-Fetal Medicine, Reproductive Endocrinology & Infertility, Urogynecology, and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery. The residency and fellowship programs are highly competitive. Our educational programs are expanding as we start a new global health program and provide clinical training for the newly established USF Family Medicine residency. Undergraduate medical education includes third-year OB/GYN clerkship students, OB/GYN subspecialty sub-internships, and the Physician Assistant Program clinical rotation in OB/GYN. Department priorities include innovation in teaching, the development of robust mentor/mentee networks, and a learning environment that fosters excellence. MINIMUM: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must be Board-eligible/certified in Obstetrics and Gynecology. Applicants must demonstrate commitment to teaching and education with at least three years of recent experience as a residency or fellowship program director, associate program director, student clerkship director, or core faculty leadership experience in an accredited OB/GYN education program. Demonstrated experience with and commitment to advancing education within obstetrics and gynecology. Evidence of a strong history of educational program leadership. A candidate with a clinical practice, which can be in any area of obstetrics and gynecology, is preferred. Must be eligible for an unrestricted medical license in the State of Florida. PREFERRED: Successful candidates for these positions are expected to have an established record of accomplishment of academic productivity. For appointments at the level of Associate or Full Professor, preference is given to individuals with an established research program and/or grant portfolio transferrable to USF. Participation in graduate and/or medical student education and mentoring is also expected. The Morsani College of Medicine offers institutional salary support commensurate with experience and external sources of funding, competitive start-up packages, dry and wet laboratory space, excellent core facilities, and a collegial atmosphere to create an environment that promotes success. Overall Responsibility: This position reports directly to the department chair. The vice chair will be responsible for overseeing all department education programs and their staff. The successful vice chair will support the department's educational leaders and build innovative programs, collaborating with our residency program directors, associate program directors, fellowship directors, and clerkship directors. They will provide direct oversight to the program coordinators and administrative staff in the Education Division of the USF Department of OB/GYN. Specific Responsibilities: Continually define and refine the department's medical educational mission — undergraduate and graduate — exercising regular oversight over all educational programs. Supporting faculty in pre-clinical medical education endeavors. Work with the department chair on all educational matters in collaboration with department vice chairs, division chiefs, program directors, and associate program directors. Play a vital role in lifelong learning activities, including CME and professional development in the department, including Grand Rounds. Support the other vice chairs and section chiefs in the department regarding professional development efforts for clinician educators. Ensure a comprehensive clinical educational experience aligned with ACGME requirements and the goals of our trainees. Create a culture of scholarship, excellence, and inclusion. Serve as a national leader for innovative training models in education in OB/GYN. Adhere to best adherence practices with ACGME standards, including curriculum development, trainee evaluation, and feedback, policy development and implementation, monitoring duty hours, and trainee wellness. Collaborate closely with affiliate site leadership and faculty at Tampa General Hospital and Moffitt Cancer Center to create high-quality educational experiences. Cultivate a culture that expands our existing educational initiatives."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44123": {
      "title": "Dermatology APP/Instructor 1",
      "description": "Closing Date: 03/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Dermatology at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking an instructor to work as an Advanced Practice Provider (APP) and diagnose, monitor and treat patients with acute and chronic dermatologic illnesses. The APP will also provide medical triage on site, by telephone and perform other miscellaneous activities as deemed necessary by Director, such as developing preceptorships for Nurse Practitioners, CME activities, and protocol development. MINIMUM: Master's or Medical degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. Degree Equivalency Clause: Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree. • Senate Bill 1310- The Florida Senate (https://www.flsenate.gov/Session/Bill/2023/1310) is conditional upon meeting all employment eligibility requirements in the U.S. • SB 1310: Substitution of Work Experience for Postsecondary Education Requirements • A public employer may include a postsecondary degree as a baseline requirement only as an alternative to the number of years of direct experience required, not to exceed: • (a) Two years of direct experience for an associate degree; • (b) Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree; • (c) Six years of direct experience for a master’s degree; • (d) Seven years of direct experience for a professional degree; or • (e) Nine years of direct experience for a doctoral degree • Related work experience may not substitute for any required licensure, certification, or registration required for the position of employment as established by the public employer and indicated in the advertised description of the position of employment. • Minimum Qualifications that require a high school diploma are exempt from SB 1310. ADDITIONAL MINIMUM: This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Clinical-Diagnoses, monitors and treats patients with acute and chronic Dermatologic illnesses. Performs minor procedures i.e., biopsies, cryosurgery, electro-desiccation & curettage etc. Develops, assists and participates with the Director in the cosmetic surgery program. Develops and updates policies and procedures in collaboration with other program personnel. Develops and participates in clinical drug studies. Teaching-Support the Department's physician assistant student education program by coordinating clinical rotations, fostering positive learning experiences, and serving as a liaison between students, faculty, preceptors, and academic institutions. Research-Assist with patient recruitment efforts by helping identify prospective research participants and coordinating referrals to study teams. Administrative-Provide medical triage on site, by telephone as needed. Performs other miscellaneous activities as deemed necessary by Director, such as developing preceptorships for PA Students, CME activities, MA/LPN/RN training, clinical and procedural protocol development. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
