will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals. PREFERRED: Research experience in dry eye, glaucoma, cornea or neuro-optics. Maintain a nationally competitive research program with continued extramural funding, peer-reviewed publications, and collaboration with other faculty. Participate in didactic teaching and mentoring medical and graduate students. Participate in service functions of the department and university, as well as at the national levels, including committees, editorial boards, and study sections."
