    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44071": {
      "title": "Open Rank- Microbiome",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/01/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The USF Institute of Microbiomes is a strategic research initiative positioned to advance USF Health's national reputation in microbiome science, translational medicine, and precision health. Recruitment of high-caliber microbiome investigators is essential to support the Institute's continued growth, expand externally funded research programs, and strengthen multidisciplinary collaborations across the Morsani College of Medicine and USF Health. This posting aims recruit four well funded researchers to enhance the Institute's ability to conduct innovative research in host-microbiome interactions, infectious diseases, immunology, cancer, metabolic disorders, and other emerging areas of biomedical science. Minimum: Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. MD or MD/PhD; history of continuous NIH funding or other high profile international grants; current NIH funding at the level of at least one R01 and or greater than $350,000 in direct costs per year or other comparable international grants; H-index greater than 20; at least 5 year experience as a principal investigator in a highly renowned research institute or university. Research-Carry out research in microbiomes, publish, obtain high level grants, including NIH grants. Principal investigator, head of a research group. Contribute to recruit faculty and mentor USF scientists and MDs. Develop philanthropic relationships, contribute in defining strategic plans, scientific and recruitment priorities. Teaching-Provide didactic, benchside, and bedside teaching of medical students, graduate students, and post-doctoral fellows and provide college-wide seminars. Participate in training and mentoring of Medical Students/Graduate Students/Postdoctoral Scholars, sit on Dissertation Committees, Course instruction and/or course curriculum development, Grant writing and professional development in Scholarly Activities (i.e. publications, review papers, etc.) Administrative-Contribute to define the strategic research orientations on microbiome investigation at USF health, contribute to establish community relationships for philanthropy, contribute to recruit new faculty and mentor faculty members in planning, research and grant submissions. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44072": {
      "title": "Asst Professor-General Dermatology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/01/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Dermatology & Cutaneous Surgery at the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine is seeking an Assistant Professor to join our growing department and participate in furthering the academic, research and clinical missions in line with the Morsani College of Medicine. The ideal candidate will have a desire to serve at the forefront of dermatology by taking on complex patients, participating in research, teaching, and have a growth mindset as we embark on new innovations. Minimum Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Must be Board Certified/Eligible in Dermatology Clinical-Attend out-patient clinics and participate in hospital rounds at affiliated hospitals. Teaching-As assigned complete didactic sessions with medical students visiting on a dermatology rotation, and meet with students interested in dermatology seeking mentorship. Research-Initiate and recruit patients to clinical trials and maintain compliance with trial sponsor Administrative-Responsible for teaching, research, service and related administrative activities including development of clinical relationship with partner hospitals. Teaching medical students and residents through lectures, conferences, teaching rounds and teaching clinics Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44046": {
      "title": "Physician Asst/Instructor. I - Plastic Surgery",
      "description": "Closing Date: 22/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Advanced Practice Provider (APP) in the Department of Plastic Surgery is responsible for delivering high-quality, patient-centered care across the continuum of reconstructive and aesthetic plastic surgery services. Working collaboratively with plastic surgeons, residents, nurses, and multidisciplinary teams, the APP provides comprehensive outpatient and inpatient clinical management, perioperative care, first-assist support in the operating room, and patient education. This position plays a critical role in improving patient access, enhancing surgical efficiency, optimizing clinical outcomes, and supporting the academic, research, and educational missions of USF Health while maintaining the highest standards of quality, safety, and compassionate care. Master's or Medical degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. Degree Equivalency Clause: Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree. • Senate Bill 1310- The Florida Senate (https://www.flsenate.gov/Session/Bill/2023/1310) is conditional upon meeting all employment eligibility requirements in the U.S. • SB 1310: Substitution of Work Experience for Postsecondary Education Requirements • A public employer may include a postsecondary degree as a baseline requirement only as an alternative to the number of years of direct experience required, not to exceed: • (a) Two years of direct experience for an associate degree; • (b) Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree; • (c) Six years of direct experience for a master’s degree; • (d) Seven years of direct experience for a professional degree; or • (e) Nine years of direct experience for a doctoral degree • Related work experience may not substitute for any required licensure, certification, or registration required for the position of employment as established by the public employer and indicated in the advertised description of the position of employment. • Minimum Qualifications that require a high school diploma are exempt from SB 1310. This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Clinical : Perform comprehensive patient assessments, including medical history, physical examinations, and documentation for reconstructive and aesthetic plastic surgery patients. Evaluate new and established patients in both outpatient clinic and inpatient settings. Develop, implement, and modify treatment plans in collaboration with supervising plastic surgeons. Order, interpret, and communicate laboratory, radiographic, and diagnostic test results. Perform preoperative evaluations and surgical clearances within scope of practice. Provide postoperative care, including wound assessments, drain management, dressing changes, splinting, and suture/staple removal. Diagnose and manage common postoperative complications, escalating care to the attending surgeon as appropriate. Assist in the operating room as First Assist, including tissue handling, exposure, retraction, hemostasis, suturing, and wound closure. Performs other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44022": {
      "title": "APRN/Instructor 1.",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/01/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Advanced Practice Provider (APP) Instructor in the Division of Gastroenterology, and Nutrition provides comprehensive patient care services in both ambulatory and inpatient settings. The APP works collaboratively with gastroenterology faculty, fellows, nurses, and multidisciplinary teams to evaluate, diagnose, treat, and monitor patients with acute and chronic gastrointestinal and liver disorders. The position supports the clinical, educational, research, and service missions of USF Health and Tampa General Hospital while contributing to high-quality, patient-centered care. This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Must be board certified/eligible in: Certified Nurse Practitioner (AANP or ANCC) or • Certified Physician Assistant (NCCPA). • Master's or Doctoral degree from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse or Physician Assistant program. • Current Florida licensure as an APRN or PA (or eligibility for Florida licensure). • Eligibility for credentialing and privileging through affiliated clinical entities. • Demonstrated commitment to patient-centered care, education, and interdisciplinary collaboration. • Experience in Gastroenterology, Hepatology, Internal Medicine, Hospital Medicine, or a related specialty preferred. • Strong communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. • Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within a multidisciplinary team. Degree Equivalency Clause: Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree. • Senate Bill 1310- The Florida Senate (https://www.flsenate.gov/Session/Bill/2023/1310) is conditional upon meeting all employment eligibility requirements in the U.S. • SB 1310: Substitution of Work Experience for Postsecondary Education Requirements • A public employer may include a postsecondary degree as a baseline requirement only as an alternative to the number of years of direct experience required, not to exceed: • (a) Two years of direct experience for an associate degree; • (b) Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree; • (c) Six years of direct experience for a master’s degree; • (d) Seven years of direct experience for a professional degree; or • (e) Nine years of direct experience for a doctoral degree • Related work experience may not substitute for any required licensure, certification, or registration required for the position of employment as established by the public employer and indicated in the advertised description of the position of employment. • Minimum Qualifications that require a high school diploma are exempt from SB 1310. Clinical : • Provide comprehensive assessment, diagnosis, treatment, and management of patients with gastrointestinal, hepatobiliary, pancreatic, and liver diseases. • Conduct outpatient clinic visits, inpatient consultations, follow-up visits, and transitional care management. • Obtain medical histories, perform physical examinations, order and interpret diagnostic tests, and develop evidence-based treatment plans. • Coordinate care with gastroenterology faculty, primary care providers, surgeons, oncologists, radiologists, pathologists, and other specialists. • Provide patient and family education regarding disease processes, treatment plans, medications, lifestyle modifications, and preventive care. • Participate in quality improvement initiatives and support compliance with institutional, state, and federal regulations. • Document patient encounters accurately and timely within the electronic health record. • Participate in call coverage, inpatient service coverage, and other clinical duties as assigned. Teaching: • Participate in the education of medical students, residents, fellows, APP students, and other healthcare learners. • Provide bedside and clinic-based instruction related to gastrointestinal diseases and patient management. • Present educational conferences, case discussions, journal clubs, and didactic sessions as assigned. • Serve as a role model for evidence-based clinical practice and professional conduct. Research: • Support clinical research and quality improvement projects within the Division of Gastroenterology. • Assist with patient identification, screening, enrollment, and follow-up for clinical studies when appropriate. • Participate in data collection, analysis, manuscript preparation, presentations, and other scholarly activities. • Maintain compliance with institutional review board (IRB) and research-related requirements. Administrative: • Participate in divisional, departmental, and institutional committees as assigned. • Assist with development and implementation of clinical protocols, workflows, and best practices. • Contribute to performance improvement, patient safety, and operational initiatives. • Complete required institutional education, credentialing, and compliance activities. Performs other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44028": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Basic Science",
      "description": "Closing Date: 20/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States \"USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician?s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html\" The Department of Surgery at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking to hire Basic Science-Open Rank Faculty to join the Department of Surgery / Research Division. Tenured/Tenure-track faculty position (Assistant/Associate/Full Professor) The Department of Surgery in the Morsani College of Medicine of the University of South Florida (USF) invites applications for tenured/tenure-track faculty positions in the Division of Surgical Research. We seek applicants with an excellent record of achievement to join our interdisciplinary and interactive faculty. Expertise is required in studying fundamental and translational aspects in the pathophysiology of diseases relevant to the broad field of surgical research. Applicants should have a MD, PhD or equivalent degree and a strong publication track record, commensurate with experience and rank. Candidates for appointments at all levels must have current extramural funding, evidence of active contribution to graduate training and/or medical education. Physician scientists are encouraged to apply. Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing, or research in refereed and other professional journals. Candidates must be Board Certified/Board Eligible in . Teaching Duties: Candidates are expected to contribute to graduate and/or medical school education. Research Duties: To perform basic and translational research related to the pathophysiology of diseases relevant to the broad field of surgical research. Administrative Duties: Candidates are expected to serve on departmental, MCOM or University Committees as deemed appropriate by the Chair and Dean of MCOM. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF POSITION: Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44030": {
      "title": "Asst Professor Director of Heart Transplant",
      "description": "Closing Date: 20/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking a Open Rank to provide clinical simulation and bioksills expertise for USF Health CAMLS. This indidivual wil provide leadership to USF Health CAMLS in oversight of the virtual patient care center and the surgical interventional and training center including the management and oversight over simulation operations specialists and clinical simulation manager. The individual will provide expertise in the educational and operational principles of manikin and simulated patient simulation as well as bioskills simulation including cadaver-based training. The Director will also have experience in high education and oversee the new concentration of simulation-operations in the COPH Health Sciences Major including course instruction. Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Successfully complete program requirements of ACGME institutional and residency/fellowship. Direct supervision of residents. Timely completion of all training courses required by hospital including a Code of Conduct course and coding courses. Responsible (with authority) for all aspects of the CT Program to include call panel privileges, treatment protocols and guidelines, service policies, education community outreach, hospital executive interface, and performance improvement; promotes multidisciplinary approach to care. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43939": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Pediatric Neonatology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 06/01/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of Pediatrics at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine, is seeking an Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor to serve the clinical and educational missions of the Division of Neonatology. The division is based at Tampa General Hospital (TGH) in Tampa, FL. TGH is a 1,018-bed teaching hospital affiliated with the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine. It is a private not-for-profit hospital and one of the most comprehensive medical facilities in west central Florida, serving a dozen counties with a population over 4 million. In addition to being a level one trauma center, it has a level 3 NICU. The 82-bed Jennifer Leigh Muma NICU is a designated Regional Perinatal Intensive Care Center designated by the State of Florida to deliver the highest level of medical care to premature and sick infants, and to women with high-risk pregnancies. USF/TGH Neonatology also participates in the Florida Perinatal Quality Collaborative, a statewide initiative to improve maternal and infant health outcomes in Florida. Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full, unrestricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Teaching: The faculty member will contribute to departmental teaching programs for neonatal fellows, pediatric residents, and medical students. He/she will participate in the preparation and organization of new educational programs as well as university and departmental committees, grand rounds, lectures, etc. Research: The faculty member will be encouraged to participate in ongoing research in the Division of Neonatology and contribute to divisional efforts to seek funding for extramural research. Clinical: The position includes the management of patients in the neonatal intensive care unit at Tampa General Hospital. Other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/41914": {
      "title": "Open Rank Faculty (Research)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 20/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. Multiple open rank faculty positions are available in the Center for Molecular Psychiatry within the Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Neurosciences, in conjunction with the Neurosciences Institute at the University of South Florida. Candidates are expected to be highly engaged in collaborative research ventures and to provide mentorship to talented mentees. Successful candidates shall have an M.D. or Ph.D. in neuroscience, psychiatry, psychology, or related disciplines, a track record of scholarly research, publications, and history of, or evidence of potential for obtaining extramural funding. A research focus in basic, translational and/or clinical sciences which directly contributes to the etiology, prevention, diagnosis and/or treatment of the wide arrange of psychiatric disorders is appropriate. Expertise in cell-based or non-rodent animal model systems is preferred but not required. A PDF application packet including (1) current curriculum vitae, (2) statement of research accomplishments and future directions (3 pages) , and (3) contact information for three potential references should be emailed to yongxu@usf.edu Completion of a doctoral degree in a related field. Must be able to meet University criteria for appointment at rank of Assistant, Associate, or Professor Rank. Develop and maintain a nationally competitive research program with continued extramural funding, peer-reviewed publications, and collaboration with other faculty. Participate in didactic teaching and mentoring medical or graduate students or post-doctoral fellows. Participate in service functions of the institute, department, or university and at the national level. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/41953": {
      "title": "APRN/ PA - Intr. I - TGH Brooksville",
      "description": "Closing Date: 24/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Advanced Practice Registered Nurse (APRN) is critical for patient care across the ambulatory and inpatient settings within the Department of Neurosurgery & Brain Repair. APRNs have independent clinic sessions during the week in order to see pre-operative; post-operative; and established patients to ensure high-quality patient care across the continuum of care. APRNs support specific neurosurgeons during their clinic sessions that allow for additional patients to be scheduled within their templates. APRNs manage hospital care of neurosurgery patients according to the protocols established with the neurosurgeons and their hospital. APRN's may assist neurosurgeons in Operating Room. This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64 Manages hospital care of neurosurgery patients according to protocol established with neurosurgeons and their hospital. Observes, evaluates, and documents patient's physical, cognitive and emotional reactions in appropriate medical records systems. Prepares patients for discharge, which includes prescriptions and follow-up instructions and completion of Discharge Summaries. Acts as first assistant in neurosurgical operative cases at the request of faculty neurosurgeons with the potential for call coverage expectations as defined by the hospital partner. Conducts in-depth interviews with patients and/or family, constructs comprehensive medical histories, performs initial and periodic physical examinations and explores patient's interpretation of health needs. Performs post-operative assessments. Completes medical paperwork such as FMLA, Worker's Compensation, etc. Communicates with patients via MyChart and phone conversations. Updates patient's records, noting changes in medication and responses to patients. Writing orders to increase, decrease or change medication, subject to checking and counter-signing by physician. Participates in in-service education programs and professional associations. Under general supervision and in accordance with standardized procedures, an Advanced Practice Registered Nurse is responsible for performing physical examinations and treating common episodic and chronic health care problems, counseling patients and families, monitoring patient progress, assisting with medical research projects. Works in collaboration with other health care team members, consulting and referring as appropriate, but retains responsibility for ongoing clinical management of the patient. Performs other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43842": {
      "title": "Adjunct USF Health",
      "description": "Closing Date: 26/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Faculty - Other JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physicians’ Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The College of Nursing is one of 14 colleges that comprise the University of South Florida (USF) and one of four colleges within USF Health. USF is a member of the prestigious Association of American Universities and is designated as both a Research 1 and a Community-Engaged institution by the Carnegie Foundation. U.S. News & World Report has ranked USF as one of the nation's top 50 public universities for five consecutive years. In 2023, USF earned its highest ranking ever among all public or private universities. The College of Nursing is recognized as a nursing education and research leader, serving over 2,400 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students annually. For the third consecutive year, our Master of Science in Nursing program ranked No. 1 among all public Florida Institutions and is proudly positioned at No. 24 nationally. The College of Nursing is an integral part of the USF Health community. We live by our mission to employ the core values of excellence, innovation, inclusion, and respect to educate future nurses, advance nursing science, and implement evidence-based clinical practice to improve health and wellness. Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization. Degree Equivalency Clause: Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree. • Senate Bill 1310- The Florida Senate (https://www.flsenate.gov/Session/Bill/2023/1310) is conditional upon meeting all employment eligibility requirements in the U.S. • SB 1310: Substitution of Work Experience for Postsecondary Education Requirements • A public employer may include a postsecondary degree as a baseline requirement only as an alternative to the number of years of direct experience required, not to exceed: • (a) Two years of direct experience for an associate degree; • (b) Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree; • (c) Six years of direct experience for a master’s degree; • (d) Seven years of direct experience for a professional degree; or • (e) Nine years of direct experience for a doctoral degree • Related work experience may not substitute for any required licensure, certification, or registration required for the position of employment as established by the public employer and indicated in the advertised description of the position of employment. • Minimum Qualifications that require a high school diploma are exempt from SB 1310. Additional Minimum Qualifications: Must be eligible to practice and maintain licensure as an RN and/or APRN in the state of Florida as required for the position. At least one year of recent and continuous clinical experience in nursing. Must have reliable transportation and be able to drive to campus or clinical facilities. Preferred Qualifications: Previous academic teaching experience. National certification in a specialty area. Doctorate in area of specialization. This position reports to the program lead of the pathway, concentration, or major to which the adjunct faculty member is primarily assigned and may also report to the program's dean. Adjunct faculty may teach in the undergraduate and/or graduate programs pending verification of appropriate licensure, approval to practice, and/or certification. Additionally, adjunct faculty are required to mentor students and are encouraged to engage in college, university, community, and professional service activities. Faculty can expect to teach at any of the college’s three campuses (Tampa, St. Petersburg, and Sarasota/Manatee). The adjunct faculty are assigned to teach didactic or clinical courses to graduate and/or undergraduate nursing students. Clinical courses may require assigned clinical site orientation, clinical site visits, providing weekly instruction in healthcare facilities, laboratory, and/or simulation settings. The adjunct faculty may have the opportunity to serve on college committees and perform community and professional service activities where appropriate. Teaching assignments will be made according to the College of Nursing, and programs' curricular needs and/or priorities. Teaching assignments may be included but are not limited to: Undergraduate and/or Graduate Didactic/ Clinical/ Laboratory/ Simulation Interested in Teaching for USF CON? Submit resume, cover letter, nursing license, and three professional references (one must be current supervisor) at USF Careers. Serving as an adjunct faculty member offers several professional and personal benefits, including: Competitive compensation Flexible work schedule Impact the future of nursing by educating and mentoring nursing students while advancing the profession Strengthen leadership, mentorship, and communication skills Build academic experience by teaching in higher education Expand your professional network through connections with faculty, students, and healthcare professionals beyond your clinical setting Access to university resources (e.g. library resources, access to USF Perks, professional development opportunities, temporary retirement plan, etc.) Have Questions: NursingAdjunctsInquiries@usf.edu"
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43827": {
      "title": "Registered Dietitian - Peds. Gastroenterology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 22/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Division of Pediatric Gastroenterology, Hepatology & Nutrition is seeking a Registered Dietitian at an Instructor I faculty member to join its growing division. This position will include outpatient clinic duties, participation in research activities related to nutrition and health outcomes and teaching duties as a faculty member of the Department of Pediatrics. Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. Registered Dietitian with the Commission on Dietetic Registration. CLINICAL - Anticipated 7-8 half day outpatient clinical sessions per week in USF Health clinics. Duties such as preparing for clinic, reviewing patient records, documenting encounters, patient correspondence, and follow-up clinical tasks. Participation in patient support through telephone or electronic communication as needed. RESEARCH – Participation in research activities related to nutrition and health outcomes, which may include study design, patient recruitment, data collection, analysis, manuscript preparation, and grant development. Research effort may also involve collaboration with faculty on ongoing studies and contributing to publications and presentations. TEACHING - May include lectures, small group facilitation, or precepting dietetic interns. RESEARCH - Participation in research activities related to nutrition and health outcomes, which may include study design, patient recruitment, data collection, analysis, manuscript preparation, and grant development. Research effort may also involve collaboration with faculty on ongoing studies and contributing to publications and presentations. OTHER - Other duties as assigned, which may include presenting at grand rounds, teaching medical students, residents, and dietetic interns, providing in-services for clinical staff, and precepting interns or students in clinic. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, service, and related activities. May be responsible for research and/or academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/40752": {
      "title": "Adjunct-COPH",
      "description": "Closing Date: 20/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Faculty - Other JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physicians’ Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html Open positions reports to the COPH Senior Associate Dean for Academic Affairs. Adjunct faculty may teach in the undergraduate and/or graduate programs pending SACS credentialing. Additionally, adjunct faculty may be required to mentor students and are encouraged to engage in college, university, community, and professional service activities. Founded in 1984, the USF College of Public Health (COPH) was the first college of public health in the state of Florida and has led the way in public health as one of the first colleges to develop an integrated core and practice-based curriculum designed to better address the complex challenges of today’s world. The USF COPH is consistently ranked #1 in the state of Florida and in the top 25 nationally for nearly 20 years in public health degree programs. As of Fall, 2022 the college has awarded over 10,000 degrees and currently serves 5,404 students in undergraduate and graduate programs including 100 online courses plus 6 online degree programs. With an all source budget of over $80 million, including $28.4 million in research awards, there are nearly 100 teaching and research faculty and over 300 support and project staff. Fully accredited by the Council on Education for Public Health (CEPH), the College is also home to three other accredited programs, the Commission on Accreditation of Healthcare Management Education (CAHME) accredited Master of Health Administration, the Accreditation Council for Genetic Counseling (ACGC) accredited Master of Science in Public Health in Genetic Counselling, and the Accreditation Council for Education in Nutrition and Dietetics (ACEND) accredited Dietetic Internship linked to an MPH in Nutrition. See the COPH website at http://health.usf.edu/publichealth/ to learn more about our dynamic and innovative faculty and College. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in public health, health education, allied health, or closely related field from an accredited institution. Demonstrated professional experience or education in public health. Experience teaching health-related information to clients, educators, or students. Must be able to be credentialed by SACS to teach undergraduate courses in public health. The adjunct faculty are assigned to teach health science and public health courses to graduate and/or undergraduate nursing students. Adjunct faculty must be credentialed by SACS to teach courses. The adjunct faculty may serve on college committees and perform community and professional service activities where appropriate."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43635": {
      "title": "Open Rank-Palliative Care Faculty",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences, and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Internal Medicine at the University of South Florida is seeking an Open Rank Faculty to provide Palliative Care services in an outpatient patient care setting. Appointment as a USF faulty member carries with it attending staff privileges at Tampa General Hospital (TGH) and affiliated hospitals. TGH is a level 1 trauma center that serves as a tertiary care facility serving south central and west Florida. Palliative Care Services will be provided at the TGH Cancer Institute. Tampa General Hospital’s Cancer Institute is nationally recognized for world-class care that is revolutionizing cancer treatment and is one of Florida's few cancer centers backed by academic medicine. As a national and global leader in cancer care, TGH is accredited by the Commission on Cancer (CoC) and takes a multidisciplinary approach to delivering high-quality, patient-centered cancer care, and demonstrating a commitment to improving patient outcomes and quality of life for all cancer patients. Appointment at the rank of Associate Professor requires a minimum of five years of continuing and productive service as an Assistant Professor, or the equivalent. Appointment at the rank of Full Professor requires a minimum of five years of continuing and productive service as an Associate Professor or the equivalent. Minimum: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in referred and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full unrestricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. MUST BE BOARD CERTIFIED/ELIGIBLE IN: Palliative Care Medicine Clinical-The primary objective of palliative medicine is to help patients and families understand the status and likely progression of their illness and to help their physicians understand what is most important to the patient. This may involve conversations around prognosis, advanced directives, expertly managing pain and symptom distress and or facilitating transition to community services. Inpatient call and coverage for the hospice and palliative care service line. Developing ongoing treatment and disease management plans. Prescribe medicine and coordinate referrals as necessary. Conduct early detection screenings. Maintain accurate patient records and charts. Communicate effectively with patients, staff, physicians and administration. Teaching-Participate in didactic teaching and mentoring of medical and/or graduate students, residents, and/or post-doctoral fellows Administrative-Protected time for administration, research, and/or education is consistent with holding specific leadership roles and fulfilling said responsibilities. Should you no longer hold those leadership roles (for any reason), the protected time may be removed and will be made up by an increase in cFTE assignments related to clinical patient care. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43637": {
      "title": "Opne Rank- Advanced Endoscopy Faculty",
      "description": "Closing Date: 01/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences, and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. To provide Advanced Endoscopy in both ambulatory clinics and inpatient call & coverage. Participation in clinical teaching for medical students, residents and fellows in clinics, endoscopy center and hospital ward settings. Minimum: Doctoral/Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate or Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Candidate must be Board-certified/eligible in Internal Medicine and/or Gastroenterology. Preferred: USF is especially interested in candidates who can contribute to the diversity and excellence of the academic community through their research, teaching, and/or service. Clinical-Perform advanced endoscopic procedures such as EUS, ERCP, EMR, ESD, and POEM. Diagnosing and treat GI disorders by interpreting patient history, diagnostic tests, and endoscopic findings. Consult with patients and collaborate with multidisciplinary team. Document patient records, treatment plans, and progress reports accurately. Participate in research, clinical trials, and scholarly activities to advance endoscopic practice. Train residents and fellows, and medical students. Teaching-Participate in didactic teaching and mentoring of medical and/or graduate students, residents, and/or post-doctoral fellows Administrative-Reviewing charts, phone calls with patients, finishing notes, answering MyChart messages, etc. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43601": {
      "title": "APRN/PA/ Instr. I - Lakeland",
      "description": "Closing Date: 29/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Health Care JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. This is for a replacement APP to support physicians in clinic. The APP will be seeing pre-op and post-op patients and routine return visits. Additionally, they will work in tandem with physicians to maximize patient templates. They are responsible for placing orders, answering MyChart messages and phone calls from patients, and completing extensive paperwork such as FMLA and disability forms. Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. CLINICAL - 90% - Key liaison to Lakeland USF Neurosurgery staff working to provide optimal continuity of care through standardization of care plans and protocols. - Obtain the history and physical examination, ordering and interpreting diagnostic and therapeutic test/procedures in coordination with Faculty supervising physician. - Regularly confers with faculty physicians regarding diagnosis, treatment, best form of therapy projected, and alerts physicians to abnormal findings.- Returns patient phone calls, renews prescriptions, coordinates rehabilitative therapy, and assesses post-procedure problems. - Provides outpatient clinic care including evaluation of new patients, established patients, and post op care. - Provides pre- and post- procedure education, assessment, and care of patients. - Documentation of all orders, procedures, and progress notes on the patient's electronic medical record. - Represents and supports the mission, philosophy, and goals of the Department. - Participates in clinical and education objectives required for licensure, certification, and credentialing. - Writes orders for changes in medication(s) and arranges plan details. ADMINISTRATIVE - 10% - Completes medical paperwork such as FMLA, Worker's Compensation, etc. Communicates with patients via MyChart and phone conversations. Updates patients' records, noting changes in medication and responses to patients. Writing orders to increase, decrease, or changed medication, subject to checking and counter-signing by physician. Participates in in-service education programs and professional associations. Performs other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43603": {
      "title": "Hydrocephalus APRN/PA - Instr. I",
      "description": "Closing Date: 29/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Health Care JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Neurosurgery at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking an Open Rank faculty position within our multidisciplinary Cerebral Spinal Fluid Disorder Center. We welcome a dedicated and innovative clinician to join our collaborative team of physiatrists, neurosurgeons and physical therapists committed to advancing the diagnosis and treatment of CSF disorders. Work in a state-of-the-art academic medical center with CSF disorder research and treatment facilities. Collaborate with a multidisciplinary team to diagnosis, treat and provide longitudinal care for these chronic diseases. Participate in research and education in CSF dynamics, hydrocephalus and intracranial hypertension and engage in teaching medical students, residents and fellows. Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. CLINICAL - Collaborate with a multidisciplinary team to diagnose, treat, and provide longitudinal care for patients with hydrocephalus and intra cranial hypertension. Evaluate and manage patients with chronic CSF disorders and help grow the center's research and collaborative programs. Evaluate patients with chronic hydrocephalus, including idiopathic normal pressure hydrocephalus (iNPH) and acquired and congenital hydrocephalus. Evaluate patients with pseudotumor cerebri/idiopathic intracranial hypertension (IIH). Establish the differential diagnosis for each patient, distinguishing CSF disorders from conditions with overlapping presentations. Perform and interpret lumbar punctures, including opening-pressure measurement and diagnostic high-volume taps. Provide longitudinal follow-up of patients with shunts. Contribute to and help expand the center's clinical registry. Build and strengthen multidisciplinary collaborations within and beyond the center. Teaching - Engage in teaching medical students, residents, and fellows. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42186": {
      "title": "Open Rank Hematologist",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Morsani College of Medicine, Department of Internal Medicine, Division of Hematology is seeking a Academic Hematologist (Open-Rank) with a desire to work in benign/classical Hematology. This position will have a 2/8th appointment with the VA to provide clinical care for malignant hematology cases (Hodgkin's and non-Hodgkin’s lymphoma) with and without fellows in clinic, take 3 weekend calls a year with fellows, and be able to supervise fellows dealing with chemotherapy unit issues. This position will work within the USF Hemophilia Treatment Center specializing in diagnosis and treatment and management of bleeding disorders. Additionally, this position will have an opportunity to engage in FDA approved Gene therapy. Our center has its own 340B program that helps support our wide range of patient care activities and staff, including RN, NP, Physical Therapist, Social worker, and administrative staff. We have our own clinical research team that supports our clinical research activities. Additional academic responsibilities may include advising and mentoring students in the development of scholarly projects; assessing, reviewing, and evaluating student educational activities and progress; and serving on university-wide, medical school, and/or departmental committees. Prefer: 1-3 years of physician experience with benign hematology. Previous experience in an academic medical center and proven track record in teaching and/or clinical research preferred. Extensive thrombosis experience is a plus as we are evolving our activities into a hemostasis/thrombosis center. Applicants with a track record in clinical or basic research in hemostasis or thrombosis are particularly encouraged to apply. Minimum: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Preferred: Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Must be board certified in Internal Medicine Clinical-The candidate will practice in an outpatient clinic with some inpatient consults treating patients. Lead outreach efforts to improve outcomes in at risk patients. Additionally, assume a role of liaison for health care decisions between the patients and the health care providers in the community, including the primary care physicians, internists, dentists, and other providers. Complete clinical obligations such as chart completion, patient follow-up, etc. Teaching-Education and Training of medical students, residents, and fellows who rotate through the Hematology and Medical Oncology clinical service. Position may also do precepting medical students in an ambulatory clerkship. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43595": {
      "title": "APRN/PA - Instr. I - General Sugery",
      "description": "Closing Date: 28/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Health Care JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician's Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of Surgery at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking an APRN/PA to further increase our patient access and provide coordination and continuity of care for patients in the division of General/Gastrointestinal Surgery. Applicants are expected to: a) (i) have graduated from an institution approved by the Accreditation Review Commission on Education for the Physician Assistant (ARC-PA), (ii) be currently certified by the National Commission on Certification of Physician Assistants (NCCPA), (iii) have a valid State Florida Medical License, and (iv) to have a minimum of 2 years of experience with in the care of surgical patients. OR b) (i) have graduated from an institution approved by the Accreditation Board for Specialty Nursing Certification ( ABSNC), (ii) have a current acute care nurse practitioners (ACNPs) in adult-gerontology (AG) patients, (iii) have valid State Florida Medical License, and (iv) to have a minimum of 2 years of experience with in the care of surgical patients. Master's or Medical degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Candidates must be Board Certified/Board Eligible in ARC-PA or NCSBN + ACNP-AG. PREFERRED: Experience with General, Foregut, and/or Bariatric Surgery patients This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Candidates must be Board Certified/Board Eligible in ARC-PA or NCSBN + ACNP-AG. CLINICAL DUTIES: Clinical duties include direct patient care for established and acute patients, including pre-and post-op patients. Serves as an extension of our physician providers in the Gastrointestinal Surgery division. OTHER DUTIES: Performs other duties as assigned by Division Chief. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF POSITION: Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42163": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Structural Biology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 20/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Molecular Medicine is housed in the Morsani College of Medicine, which is a college within USF Health. USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physicians’ Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of Molecular Medicine seeks candidates for a tenured or tenure-track position who use structural biology-based approaches and cryo-EM to understand the molecular basis of disease that complement the department's existing strengths in infectious, neurological, and oncological diseases. The successful candidate for this position is expected to have already established a nationally recognized, competitively funded research program, and have experience mentoring and educating graduate and medical students. A highly competitive salary and start-up package commensurate with experience will be provided to the successful candidate to promote continued success. Minimum: Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate Professor, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor: M ust have established a national and/or international reputation in the field as evidenced by significant publications and competitive research grants. Preferred: Ph.D. in biochemistry or a related field, with research experience evidenced by peer-reviewed publications and successful grant writing. Preference will be given to candidates with interdisciplinary training, a record of collaboration, and direct experience with Cryo-EM techniques. Please upload a single PDF that includes a cover letter, research and mentoring statement (3 pages), and teaching statement (1 page), along with your CV for consideration for this position. The search committee will begin reviewing applications January 15, 2026. Research: Maintain a nationally recognized research program funded by federal and private grants that leads to significant manuscripts in respected scientific journals. Teaching: Will be responsible for teaching and mentoring graduate (MS and PhD) and medical students (MD). Administrative: Will be expected to serve on department and college service committees as assigned. Serve the scientific community by reviewing manuscripts and grants, and participate in scientific societies."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43581": {
      "title": "Professor, Chair, Biostatistics and Data Science",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physicians’ Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The incumbent of this position serves as a senior-level faculty member in Biostatistics and Data Sciences. In addition, the incumbent serves as Chair of the Department. As a ranked professorial faculty position at USF, the incumbent will have teaching, research, scholarship, and service responsibilities. The Chair will provide strategic leadership to strengthen and expand the Department’s research profile, educational excellence, collaborative engagement, and impact in biostatistics, data science, artificial intelligence, and quantitative population health.” The successful candidate will play a central role in advancing the Department’s visibility, faculty recruitment, interdisciplinary integration, and research competitiveness, while furthering the goals and mission of the College of Public Health. This position reports directly to the Dean who will meet with the incumbent annually to discuss the specific assignment for the upcoming academic year and evaluate performance for the previous year. Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in referred and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Professor. Additional Minimum Qualifications: A minimum of two years of sustained accomplishment as an Associate Professor in a university or equivalent setting, including evidence of scholarly productivity, leadership, teaching effectiveness, and service. A record of excellence teaching in biostatistics or related quantitative courses, including a clearly defined teaching philosophy and a record of participation on and as major professor for thesis and/or dissertation committees for master's and doctoral candidates where applicable. A national and/or international record of excellence in independent and/or collaborative research and/or creative scholarly work in Biostatistics and Data Sciences or related discipline supported by substantial and sustained publications or their equivalent. A record of substantive contribution of service to the University and to the field, profession, and community. Compelling evidence of significant achievement among peers in one's discipline or professional field at the national or international level. A record of collegiality and participation as a citizen of a university or other equivalent institution. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated commitment to faculty development, mentorship, retention, and advancement across career stages. Demonstrated expertise in Biostatistics and Data Sciences or related discipline. Administrative experience leading multidisciplinary teams. Commitment to and experience in attracting, retaining, and graduating doctoral students. Ability to create and support a collaborative research and learning community. Extensive publication record in peer-reviewed journals relevant to the field of Biostatistics and Data Sciences. Demonstrated record of securing and sustaining extramural funding appropriate to the discipline and career stage. Commitment to faculty governance and collegiality. Demonstrated expertise or leadership experience in emerging areas such as data science, machine learning, artificial intelligence, computational epidemiology, or health informatics. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Instructional Duties: 20% FTE Teach graduate level public health and Biostatistics and Data Sciences related courses where interests and needs align. Collaborate in teaching with other faculty within the College and participate in college-wide teaching initiatives. Advise graduate students at both master’s and doctoral levels, including serving on thesis and dissertation committees as needed. Research Duties: 35% FTE Collaborate with faculty across the Department, College, USF Health, and the broader university to advance innovative methodological, collaborative, and translational quantitative research. Apply for and obtain competitive extramural funding for research grants. Disseminate scholarly achievements through peer-reviewed publications, presentations, and active translation to the field. Service Duties: 5% FTE Participate in service activities at the university, professional, and community levels, including serving on special work groups and other university service roles. Participate at the local, state, and national level in professional organizations and activities. Serve on Department, College, and University committees; actively participate in local, state, and national public health organizations and professional associations; and contribute actively to community engagement. Administrative Duties: 40% FTE Specific responsibilities of the Department Chair include: Exercising leadership by developing effective goals and plans for the department, representing the faculty and serving as a role model for faculty, staff, and students. Managing Department staff and student employees, finances, and resources effectively and efficiently, in accordance with College and University policies. Practicing fair, balanced, and transparent leadership in managing the various constituencies within the Department and facilitating the work of faculty. Fostering excellence in the education, research, and service programs of the Department, including collaboration with other department chairs, center directors, and designated mission leads. Facilitating the recruitment and retention of a diverse and talented faculty, staff, and student body to fulfill the needs and missions of the Department and College. Advocating for equitable salary and academic work conditions for Department faculty, staff, and student employees, facilitating their continuing academic and professional development. Encouraging the development of research and teaching programs and fostering interdisciplinary activities. Responsible for ensuring timely, fair, and equitable completion of the annual faculty assignment and evaluation processes. Responsible for ensuring completion of the staff evaluation process and that their students are evaluated consistently with the expectations of the Graduate Assistant Collective Bargaining Agreement. Actively participating as a member of the College Leadership team, providing overall direction for the continued growth and improvement in quality of all College mission areas. Contributing to the reputation and overall welfare of the College and University. Facilitate meaningful engagement and integration of affiliated and jointly appointed quantitative faculty across the university to strengthen the Department’s collaborative and educational mission. Collaborating with other Department Chairs regarding the assignment and evaluation of faculty who have joint (secondary) appointments in their respective departments as well as College-wide program directors for shared teaching responsibilities necessary to meet the academic mission of the College. Advance the national visibility and reputation of the Department through strategic partnerships, faculty success, innovative programming, and research leadership. The Chair is also expected to maintain a record of personal success in his/her field and participate in the teaching, research, and service programs of the Department. The Chair serves as an advisor to the Dean of the College of Public Health and as a member of the Executive Committee of the College."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43541": {
      "title": "Open Rank-General Cardiology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 24/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences, and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. In partnership with Tampa General Hospital (TGH) Heart & Vascular Institute (HVI), the Division of Cardiovascular Sciences, Section of General & Preventive Cardiology, is seeking an academic non-invasive general cardiologist for a full-time position at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor rank. Preference is placed for candidates with expertise in hypertension management or vascular disease to lead a resistant hypertension program or a medical vascular program. Candidates with expertise in sports cardiology are also encouraged to apply. This is a full-time, 12-month salaried faculty appointment and includes attending staff privileges at Tampa General Hospital (TGH) and affiliated hospitals. There is a desire for candidates with a strong interest in and commitment to teaching. Appointment at the rank of Associate Professor requires a minimum of five years of continuing and productive service as an Assistant Professor, or the equivalent. Appointment at the rank of Full Professor involves a minimum of five years of ongoing and productive service as an Associate Professor, or the equivalent. MINIMUM: Doctoral/Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate or Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in referred and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. The candidate would need to have an expertise in hypertension management or vascular disease, to lead a resistant hypertension program or a medical vascular program. Candidates with expertise in sport cardiology are encouraged to apply ADDITIONAL MINIMUM: Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full unrestricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. PREFERRED: Applicants with teaching experience with students/residents, experience with administrative organization/leadership of outpatient practices, and/or clinical research/scholarship experience will be most competitive. Level II certification in Echocardiography is preferred. Desire expertise in adult non-invasive assessment of heart disease, including surface echo and trans-esophageal echocardiography, stress echo and adult congenital heart disease. Desire experience with exercise testing, ECG interpretation, consulting and attending in a coronary intensive care unit or similar environment. Two years’ experience in Non-Invasive Cardiology preferred. MUST BE BOARD CERTIFIED/ELIGIBLE IN: General Cardiology CLINICAL- Participates in Inpatient general cardiology consult service, non-invasive call & coverage, reading EKGs and Stress Tests. Opportunity to participate in Echo Lab and Call & Coverage for Transesophageal Echocardiography, Stress Test on call, and Echo reads if certified from a nationally accredited organization. Participates in outpatient clinics for USF Health. Duties include Diagnose and treat disorders and diseases of the cardiovascular system. Participate in didactic teaching and mentoring of medical and/or graduate students, residents, and/or post-doctoral fellows. Perform patient exams and order or conduct diagnostic testing. Develop ongoing treatment and disease-management plans. Prescribe medicine and coordinate referrals as necessary. Conduct early detection screenings. Maintain accurate patient records and charts. Communicate effectively with patients, physicians, staff, and administration. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. TEACHING-Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43544": {
      "title": "Open Rank-Cardiology (Moffitt)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 24/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Division of Cardiovascular Sciences, Section of General & Preventive Cardiology, is seeking an academic General cardiologist for a full-time position at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor rank. Preference is placed for the candidates with expertise in cardiology oncology. This is a full-time, 12-month salaried faculty appointment and includes attending staff privileges at Moffitt Cancer Center. There is a desire for candidates with a strong interest in and commitment to teaching. Appointment at the rank of Associate Professor requires a minimum of five years of continuing and productive service as an Assistant Professor, or the equivalent. Appointment at the rank of Full Professor involves a minimum of five years of ongoing and productive service as an Associate Professor, or the equivalent. MINIMUM: Doctoral/Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate or Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in referred and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full unrestricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. PREFERRED: Applicants with teaching experience with students/residents, experience with administrative organization/leadership of outpatient practices, and/or clinical research/scholarship experience will be most competitive. Level II certification in Echocardiography is preferred. Desire expertise in adult non-invasive assessment of heart disease, including surface echo and trans-esophageal echocardiography, stress echo and adult congenital heart disease. Desire experience with exercise testing, ECG interpretation, consulting and attending in a coronary intensive care unit or similar environment. Two years’ experience in Non-Invasive Cardiology preferred. MUST BE BOARD CERTIFIED/ELIGIBLE IN: General Cardiology CLINICAL-patient consultations and outpatient care primarily at H. Lee Moffitt Cancer Center & Research Institute, non-invasive cardiology call & coverage, reading EKGs and Stress Tests. Opportunity to participate in Echo reads if certified from a nationally accredited organization. Duties include Diagnose and treat disorders and diseases of the cardiovascular system. Participate in didactic teaching and mentoring of medical and/or graduate students, residents, and/or post-doctoral fellows. Perform patient exams and order or conduct diagnostic testing. Develop ongoing treatment and disease-management plans. Prescribe medicine and coordinate referrals as necessary. Conduct early detection screenings. Maintain accurate patient records and charts. Communicate effectively with patients, physicians, staff, and administration. TEACHING-Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43547": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Nutrition",
      "description": "Closing Date: 24/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physicians’ Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The incumbent will serve as a full-time, non-tenure earning faculty position in the Practice Pathway in the Department of Community and Health Sciences. As a ranked professorial faculty position at USF, the incumbent will have teaching, scholarship, and service responsibilities. In addition, the incumbent will serve as Coordinator of the COPH Nutrition Program responsible for providing day-to-day instructional leadership, program coordination, and administrative support for the growing Nutrition Program. The incumbent will report directly to the Chair of the Department of Community and Health Sciences who will meet annually with the incumbent to discuss the specific assignment for the upcoming assignment year and to review performance during the previous year. The Director of the Nutrition Program will provide day-to-day direction for the duties related to the role of Coordinator, as well as provide input into the incumbent’s annual assignment and evaluation. Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Additional Minimum Qualifications: Five years as a public health or healthcare professional or master's degree and three years of professional public health or healthcare experience. Teaching experience (may be as a teaching assistant or in another instructional capacity). Demonstrated ability to fulfill expectation of continued growth as a scholar/researcher. Independent, sustained funded research is not required. Demonstrated ability to fulfill expectation of contributions in the area of service commensurate with the College's mission. Demonstrated ability to fulfill expectation of collegiality and participation as a citizen of the University. Experience with ACEND standards, accreditation processes. Registered dietitian. Preferred Qualifications: Defined area of teaching expertise within nutrition or public health. Innovation in curriculum design, online learning, competency-based education, or course development. Experience coordinating or assisting with ACEND-accredited programs (e.g., DPD, DI, FDE, GP). Minimum five years of professional practice as a Registered Dietitian. Established record of scholarly activity consistent with practice-based scholarship (e.g., technical reports, professional presentations, program evaluation, applied research). Experience engaging diverse communities or leading practice-based initiatives aligned with public health nutrition. Demonstrated ability to collaborate in multi-disciplinary academic or practice environments. Instructional Duties: 85% FTE Instruction • Develop and teach on-line and in-class courses related to the Nutrition Program; participate in college-wide teaching initiatives. • Contribute to USF Health interprofessional education programs. • Collaborate in teaching with faculty in other Colleges in USF Health and the University. • Advise MPH, MSPH and doctoral students. • Serve on thesis and doctoral committees as appropriate. Program Coordinator • Assist with curriculum development, revision, sequencing, and alignment across undergraduate and graduate nutrition offerings. • Support preparation and maintenance of materials needed for accreditation or external review (e.g., syllabi, assessment plans, competency mapping, workforce development tracking). • Collaborate with faculty across USF to recruit and retain students in the Nutrition Program. • Contribute to development of student advising materials, webpages, recruitment collateral, and program communications. • Serve on the Nutrition Program Admissions Committee and assist with application review and student onboarding. • Support continuous quality improvement processes for coursework, student outcomes, and program performance. • Provide operational support for program events, outreach, community engagement, and professional development initiatives. Research/Scholarship Duties: 5% FTE Contribute to the scholarly literature through publication in peer-reviewed journals, presentations and active translation to the field. Collaborate with faculty across the College, USF Health, and USF to participate in translational research initiatives. Independent, sustained funded research is not required. Service Duties: 10% FTE Engage in service activities at the department, college, university, community and professional levels. Serve on faculty governance committees, special work groups, or other college and university committees. Participate at the national and state level in professional organizations and activities. Contribute to the community through service related to professional and other expertise. Administrative Duties: 0% FTE (Restricted to individuals with formal College-wide administrative appointments by the Dean. Direct administrative effort related to specific course/program/concentration should be reflected in the Instruction category, Other Instructional Related. Direct administrative effort related to a specific research project should be reflected in the Research category. Center Directors should be reflected in College or Sponsored Research depending upon the funding source.)"
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43530": {
      "title": "APRN/PA - Instr. I - Cardiology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Health Care JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. Minimum: Master's or Medical degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. Additional Minimum: This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. MUST BE BOARD CERTIFIED/ELIGIBLE IN: Family Practice or Adult Gerontology Acute Care CLINICAL - 95%- Evaluates patients with suspected or confirmed cardiology diagnoses through diagnostic testing and history taking, including those referred from Internal Medicine, Emergency Medicine, or other specialties. Triages inpatient consultations and patient phone calls, renews prescriptions, coordinates care, and manages post-procedure concerns. Assesses patients with rhythm disorders or cardiac devices and provides pre- and post-procedure education for pacemaker, ICD, ablation, WATCHMAN implant, and electrophysiology procedures in outpatient settings. Performs comprehensive History and Physical Exams and independently manages electrophysiology clinic patients under general supervision. Initiates, monitors, and adjusts anti-arrhythmic therapies, orders tests, and prescribes medications, regularly consulting with faculty electrophysiologists on treatment plans and abnormal findings. Addresses inquiries via the medical record and documents all orders, procedures, progress notes, and device interrogations, including holter and event monitor tracings. ADMINISTRATIVE - 5% - Support and arrange patient care with the referring provider, handle outpatient follow-ups, and make recommendations based on findings. Educate patients and their families about diagnoses, results, and next steps. Respond to patient and staff questions through the medical record system. Record all orders, procedures, and progress notes in the patient's electronic medical record. Performs other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43552": {
      "title": "Open Rank - OB/GYN Generalist",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician's Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at https://health.usf.edu/. The Department of OB/GYN at the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine is seeking a highly qualified academic generalist to join our growing Division of Specialists in General OB/GYN. This is an exciting opportunity for an academic generalist with a commitment to excellence in patient care, education and scholarly activity. Faculty enjoy career growth opportunities customized to their interests. Leadership opportunities are available with this position. About the USF Department of OB/GYN: The department has ACGME-approved fellowships in Gynecologic Oncology, Maternal-Fetal Medicine, Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery, and Reproductive Endocrinology and Infertility. Its Research Division in Reproductive Science, and Gynecologic Oncology has well established and funded lines of basic/translational research. MINIMUM: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate or Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing, or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Board Certified/Board Eligible in Obstetrics & Gynecology. Must have completed Residency in Obstetrics and Gynecology with an interest in teaching and patient care. Must have or be eligible for a Florida Medical License. Positive factors for consideration include, but are not limited to, an excellent record of clinical care with several years of teaching/supervising experience and demonstrated leadership skills. We will also consider new OBGYN graduates with academic career interests. Great communication skills and the ability to work in a team-based environment are required. Provide general Obstetrics and Gynecology care, including ambulatory care, deliveries, surgery and complete maternal care. Co-manage patient care with MFM faculty. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42171": {
      "title": "Open Rank - MFM",
      "description": "Closing Date: 20/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences, and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician's Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of South Florida (USF) is recruiting a Maternal Fetal Medicine physician to fill its open academic position. This new physician will join our established MFM team who provide comprehensive maternal-fetal care. The Division's clinical scope is broad, including coverage of labor and delivery, the antepartum service, obstetrical ultrasound, prenatal diagnosis procedures, and perinatal consultation. We have an active and growing fetal therapy program that includes laser therapy and in-utero surgical procedures, as well as robust clinical programs for managing pregnancies complicated by placenta accreta and other complex medical and surgical conditions, including cardio-obstetrics. Our primary clinic is located at 2 Tampa General Circle, Tampa, FL 33606. Clinical activities are complemented by opportunities in medical education and participation in statewide perinatal quality collaborative initiatives. Most of the Division members are actively engaged in clinical/translational research or other innovative clinical programs that match their interests. We have an ACGME-accredited MFM Fellowship and a robust OB/GYN residency program comprised of 24 residents. The MFM Division is actively involved in educating fellows, residents, and medical students. Our primary affiliate, Tampa General Hospital (TGH), boasts more than 6,200 deliveries annually and has an 82-bed Level IV NICU. MINIMUM: Must possess an MD or equivalent degree from an accredited institution and be board-eligible/certified in Obstetrics and Gynecology. Candidates must have successfully completed a Maternal-Fetal Medicine fellowship. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Interest in the education of residents and fellows. Must be eligible for an unrestricted medical license in the State of Florida. Successful candidates for these positions are expected to have an established record of academic productivity. Salary and academic rank are commensurate with experience, qualifications, and sources of external funding. For appointments at the level of Associate or Full Professor, preference is given to individuals with an established research program and/or grant portfolio transferable to USF. Participation in graduate and/or medical student education and mentoring is also expected. The Morsani College of Medicine offers institutional salary support commensurate with experience and external sources of funding, competitive start-up packages, dry and wet laboratory space, excellent core facilities, and a collegial atmosphere to create an environment that promotes success. CLINICAL: Provide general and high-risk Obstetrics and Gynecology care, including ambulatory care, deliveries, and surgery. TEACHING: Teach medical students and residents through lectures, rounds, and clinical activity in patient offices, labor and delivery, and the operating room. ADMINISTRATIVE: Close encounters timely, follow up with patient requests. OTHER DUTIES: Professional development and service. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42172": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Urogyn",
      "description": "Closing Date: 20/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician's Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, Division of Urogynecology & Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery at the University of South Florida (USF) is seeking a urogynecologist. Our division values each member’s diverse and complimentary interests and talents. We enjoy working together to deliver the very best care to our vibrant community while also striving to advance the field of urogynecology through innovation in clinical care, teaching, research, and leadership within our system and beyond. The position includes responsibilities for clinical care, teaching and research at the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine and Tampa General Hospital. There are opportunities for clinical, administrative, research, and/or teaching leadership for a qualified candidate. An interest in clinical, educational, quality improvement, translational or basic science research is desired. The successful candidate should have academic qualifications for the rank of assistant professor or associate professor. MINIMUM: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Candidates must be Board Certified/Board Eligible in Obstetrics & Gynecology and Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery. Candidates must have successfully completed a Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery fellowship. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. TEACHING: Teach medical students and residents by lecture, rounds, and clinical activity in the office and operating room. CLINICAL: Provide Urogynocology care, including ambulatory care and surgery in the hospital. OTHER DUTIES: General administration duties that include documenting and reviewing patient chart Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42173": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Minimally Invasive Gynecologic Surgery (MIGS)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 20/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician's Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of South Florida (USF) is actively recruiting to fill one open academic position within the division of Gynecologic Specialty Services. This board-eligible/certified, fellowship-trained, minimally invasive gynecologic surgeon will join our growing, busy division. Preference will be given to a candidate with academic experience and expertise to help grow the Gyn Specialty Services division and assist with establishing a MIGS fellowship. However, new graduates are also welcome to apply and must be both comfortable and proficient in complex benign gynecology, dedicated to quality patient care, and have an interest in clinical research. The goal of the Gynecologic Specialty Services Division is to encompass faculty with diverse backgrounds and levels of experience and complementary skills. The primary focus of the MIGS subspecialist will be the clinical care of endometriosis, fibroids and chronic pelvic pain patients at USF, supervision and teaching of fellows, OBGYN residents, and medical students, and conducting of clinical research. Clinical responsibilities include office-based procedures and gynecologic surgery. MINIMUM: Doctoral/Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Candidate must be Board Certified/Board Eligible in Obstetrics & Gynecology. Candidate must also have completed an AAGL MIGS fellowship. Special attention will be given to graduates of programs with focus on chronic pelvic pain. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. TEACHING: Teach medical student and residents by lecture, rounds, and clinical activity in patient office and the operating suite. CLINICAL: Provide general gynecologic care, including minimally invasive gynecologic surgery in the inpatient and outpatient settings. OTHER DUTIES: General administration duties that include documenting and reviewing patient chart. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43523": {
      "title": "Open Rank- Virology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 22/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The University of South Florida (USF) and the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine (MCOM) are launching an open-rank call for tenured/tenured-track high level scientists in the field of Virology. Essential functions of this position include carrying out research on viruses and viral diseases at the Institute for Translational Virology and Innovation (ITVI) Directed by Dr. Robert C Gallo, publishing, obtaining high-level grants, including NIH grants, and serving as a Principal investigator, head of a research group, contributing to the recruitment of faculty, and mentoring USF scientists and MDs. Develop philanthropic relationships, contribute to defining strategic plans, scientific and recruitment priorities. MINIMUM: Doctoral/Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate or Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. PREFERRED PhD, MD or MD/PhD; Preferred: History of continuous NIH funding or other high profile international grants; current NIH funding at the level of at least one R01 or greater than $250,000 in direct costs per year or other comparable international grants; At least 5 papers with an impact factor above 10; H-index greater than 30; at least 3 years experience as a principal investigator in a highly renowned research institute or University. TEACHING-Provide didactic, benchside, and bedside teaching of medical students, graduate students, and post-doctoral fellows and provide college-wide seminars. Participate in training and mentoring of Medical Students/Graduate Students/Postdoctoral Scholars, sit on Dissertation Committees, Course instruction and/or course curriculum development, Grant writing and professional development in Scholarly Activities (i.e. publications, review papers, etc.) RESEARCH-Carry out research in virology, publish, obtain high level grants including NIH grants. Act as Principal investigator, head of a research group. Contribute to recruit faculty and mentor USF scientists and MDs. Develop philanthropic relationships, contribute in defining strategic plans, scientific and recruitment priorities. ADMINISTRATIVE-Contribute to define the strategic research orientations on virology investigation at USF health, contribute to establish community relationships for philanthropy, contribute to recruit new faculty and mentor faculty members in planning, research and grant submissions. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42138": {
      "title": "APRN/Instr. I",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences, and the USF Physician's Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The APRN will act in accordance with Florida Statutes for the Nurse Practitioners Act. The care and management of critically ill infants requiring hospitalization in a level IV neonatal intensive care unit. This NICU Nurse Practitioner will cover night and/or day shifts as assigned including weekend coverage. The Neonatal Intensive Care Unit is based at Tampa General Hospital (TGH) in Tampa, FL. TGH is a 1,018-bed teaching hospital affiliated with the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine. It is a private not-for-profit hospital and one of the most comprehensive medical facilities in west central Florida, serving a dozen counties with a population of over 4 million. In addition to being a level one trauma center, it has a level 3 NICU. The 82-bed Jennifer Leigh Muma NICU is a designated Regional Perinatal Intensive Care Center designated by the State of Florida to deliver the highest level of medical care to premature and sick infants, and to women with high-risk pregnancies. USF/TGH Neonatology also participates in the Florida Perinatal Quality Collaborative, a statewide initiative to improve maternal and infant health outcomes in Florida. Neonatal services include a Neonatal Transport Team, Fetal Care Center, and Whole-Body Cooling. Pediatric subspecialties available for collaborative treatment of neonatal patients including Neurology, Neurosurgery, Ophthalmology, ENT, Cardiology, Pulmonology, Gastroenterology, Endocrinology, Hematology/Oncology, Nephrology, Metabolic Genetics. Educational Requirements: Master’s Degree in Nursing: ARNP training; Florida License. BLS/AED certification is required and must be maintained. Any equivalent combination of experience and education. Experience Requirements: 2-5 years; at least 2 years of experience evaluating pediatric patients (2 years’ experience assessing neonates preferred) Minimum 1-year nursing experience in a physician’s office or clinic experience in an ambulatoryhealth care facility preferred. BLS/AEDcertificationis requiredand must be maintained.ACLS or PALS Master’s degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Clinical: Ongoing evaluation and management of neonates and infants requiring care in the neonatal intensive care unit, participation in multidisciplinary rounds, and coordination of care with ancillary staff and family. Attendance at high-risk deliveries and immediate stabilization of critically ill neonates under the supervision of the attending Neonatologist. Documentation of all orders, procedures, and progress notes on the patient's medical record. Performs procedures necessary for the care of neonates and infants in the intensive care unit including endotracheal intubation, umbilical line placement, PICC line placement, lumbar punctures, and peripheral arterial lines. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43517": {
      "title": "Open Rank - MD/PhD Research",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Research Support JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician's Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html.The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine is undergoing a strategic expansion of its research enterprise. The department is seeking to recruit tenure-track faculty at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor to complement and enhance its growing cadre of innovative, collegial, collaborative, and well-funded faculty. The department is particularly interested in candidates whose research programs will strengthen and expand existing areas of excellence in women’s health, reproductive biology, maternal-fetal medicine, placental biology, gynecologic disease, reproductive endocrinology, infertility, oncology, inflammation, cardiovascular and metabolic health, and translational medicine. Through discovery, education, clinical care, and service, faculty in the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology strive to advance scientific knowledge and improve the health of women and pregnant individuals across the lifespan. The department provides a dynamic and collaborative environment for cutting-edge, interdisciplinary research that bridges basic, translational, and clinical investigation. Faculty collaborate across the Morsani College of Medicine, USF Health, affiliated hospitals, and research institutes to develop new diagnostics, therapeutics, and preventive strategies for conditions affecting reproductive, maternal, fetal, and gynecologic health. This position includes developing and leading an independent research program, conducting collaborative and programmatic research with departmental and institutional faculty, publishing findings in peer-reviewed journals, pursuing and securing extramural funding, and contributing meaningfully to the academic mission of the department and college. The successful candidate will also support the research development of faculty, fellows, residents, medical students, graduate students, and other trainees. The candidate will be expected to participate in departmental, college, and institutional service, which may include serving on committees or task forces, assisting with research operations, mentoring trainees, contributing to scholarly activities, and supporting initiatives that advance the department’s research enterprise. Minimum Qualification MD, PhD, MD/PhD, or equivalent doctoral degree in medicine, biomedical sciences, reproductive biology, women’s health, public health, or a related field. Evidence of scholarly productivity, including peer-reviewed publications. Demonstrated potential or established record of extramural research funding. Eligibility for appointment at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. Preferred Qualifications Established or emerging research program relevant to obstetrics, gynecology, reproductive biology, maternal-fetal medicine, placental biology, gynecologic disease, women’s health, or related fields. Strong record of federal or foundation research funding. Experience in an academic medical center or health sciences environment. Demonstrated commitment to mentoring trainees and supporting faculty scholarly development. Experience conducting translational, clinical, population health, or basic science research relevant to women’s and reproductive health. Strong track record of interdisciplinary collaboration. Develop and maintain an innovative, independent, and extramurally funded research program. Conduct collaborative and interdisciplinary research with faculty within the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, Morsani College of Medicine, USF Health, and affiliated institutions. Publish high-impact scientific research in peer-reviewed journals. Pursue and secure federal, foundation, and other extramural funding. Support the development of a strong, collaborative, and well-funded departmental research enterprise. Mentor faculty, fellows, residents, medical students, graduate students, and research staff in scholarly and research activities. Contribute to the teaching, mentoring, and service missions of the department and college. Participate in faculty meetings, research meetings, committees, and other departmental activities. Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong record of scholarly productivity and peer-reviewed publications. Experience developing or contributing to externally funded research programs. Ability to build collaborative, interdisciplinary research programs. Experience mentoring students, residents, fellows, or junior faculty in research. Excellent interpersonal, communication, leadership, and professionalism skills. Commitment to advancing the research, education, and service missions of an academic medical center."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43493": {
      "title": "Audiologist - Instr. I",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Health Care JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The University of South Florida is seeking an Audiologist to join the Otolaryngology- Head & neck Surgery Department. Our multidisciplinary ear, nose, and throat (ENT) team provides patient care at multiple USF and Tampa General Hospital (TGH) ailiated locations. We are seeking a clinical Audiologist to be an integral member of the ENT healthcare team and evaluate patients with ear abnormalities and/or auditory-vestibular disorders through case history, clinical observation and diagnostic tests. Audiologist will contribute to multidisciplinary approach to treatment and care planning, and will provide (re)habilitative programs for patients with auditory-vestibular disorders. Audiologist also plans and implements hearing protection and fall prevention programs, along with (re)habilitation services, including individualized selection of hearing assistive technology (hearing aids, bone conduction solutions, etc), fitting with verification and validation measures, counseling, and orientation and self-management support. Audiologist with pediatric experience is preferred that provides evidence-based patient care with a whole-child and whole-family approach. We aim to provide excellent evidence based practice and allow clinicians to grow in their clinical skills and interests. Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. Degree Equivalency Clause: Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree. • Senate Bill 1310- The Florida Senate (https://www.flsenate.gov/Session/Bill/2023/1310) is conditional upon meeting all employment eligibility requirements in the U.S. • SB 1310: Substitution of Work Experience for Postsecondary Education Requirements • A public employer may include a postsecondary degree as a baseline requirement only as an alternative to the number of years of direct experience required, not to exceed: • (a) Two years of direct experience for an associate degree; • (b) Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree; • (c) Six years of direct experience for a master’s degree; • (d) Seven years of direct experience for a professional degree; or • (e) Nine years of direct experience for a doctoral degree • Related work experience may not substitute for any required licensure, certification, or registration required for the position of employment as established by the public employer and indicated in the advertised description of the position of employment. • Minimum Qualifications that require a high school diploma are exempt from SB 1310. Minimum Qualifications • Ability to obtain Florida state license in audiology required. • Ability to obtain ASHA CCC-A certification. • Work requires a Doctorate in Audiology or a Master's degree in Audiology. • No experience required. 4th year AuD Externship/Residency is considered relevant clinical experience. Preferred Qualifications • Experience working with patients of all ages with special interest in pediatric patients, or expertise in electrophysiology, and Interest in clinical mentorship teaching and supporting scholarship/research. CLINICAL • Independently maintains a clinical caseload in designated clinical area. • Provides evidence based evaluation and treatment to diverse, medically challenging patient populations. • Advise and counsel patients and their families regarding test results, hearing loss treatment and (re)habilitation options, and preventative measures. • Recommend (re)habilitations programs with hearing assistive technology, Dispense hearing aids and other listening devices. Counsel and advise patients and their families in the care, use and maintenance of their hearing aids and/or other listening devices. • Provides quality service delivery techniques that facilitate optimum services to meet patient needs being sensitive to patient's age and social determinants of health. • Completes required documentation accurately and within the designated time frame which may include report writing, billing, department documentation requirements. • Works collaboratively as part of a multidisciplinary team as well as with Division colleagues to promote best care of the patient. • Participates in the clinical peer review process. • Participates in performance improvement initiatives within assigned work area under the supervision of division leadership. • Takes initiative to remain current in clinical practice through lectures, literature, and other educational opportunities. • Organizes daily schedule to prioritize responsibilities including the integration of meetings, responsibilities, or tasks into schedule without negative impact on patient care or productivity. • Maintains confidentiality pertaining to patient care and all Division policies and procedures. • Functions in a self-directed manner and takes ownership to manage self and work including responsibility for actions and accountability for results. • Maintains professional demeanor and is responsible for quality care in all interactions. • Uses technology (e.g., computer skills, electronic medical record system) to meet job requirements. • Maintains productivity standards. • Completes clinical privileges consistent with job responsibilities and annual assignment for personal development plan. • Performs duties/ tasks/ assignments as directed to support Division goals or needs. • Meets and adheres to ASHA, state licensure board and Division clinical practice guidelines. TEACHING – • Support clinical trainee programs (e.g., ENT Residents, AuD interns and externs, etc) within the clinical setting. • Engage actively with the Otolaryngology residency program and Doctor of Audiology program in the Department of Communication Sciences & Disorders (CSD) Department. • Serve as a clinical resource for residents, medical, and APP students rotating through the department, modeling team-based care. RESEARCH – • Support clinical research/scholarship by promoting research opportunities as appropriate to potentially eligible patients. • Opportunity to participate in departmental clinical research initiatives, including ongoing trials. • Opportunity to contribute to scholarly projects led by faculty colleagues and trainees (residents, MD, AuD and/or PhD students), with potential for coauthorship and presentation at regional and national meetings. • Ability to engage with the broader USF/TGH research enterprise as opportunities and interests align. Administrative - • Complete clinical documentation accurately and in a timely manner, including patient encounters and patient messages. • Manage patient-specific paperwork including all hearing aid and other technology ordering/dispensing documentation. • Participate in departmental/division quality improvement initiatives. Performs other duties as assigned."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43458": {
      "title": "Open Rank- Infectious Disease",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Internal Medicine Division of Infectious Diseases and International Medicine is pleased to announce a faculty position available at the Morsani College of Medicine (MCOM) as a non-tenure track Infectious Diseases Clinician Educator. The infectious diseases clinician will provide inpatient/outpatient infectious diseases consultation to adult patients, within USF Health. The successful candidate will be able to demonstrate a record of excellence in patient care and an interest in working immunocompromised patient population. Additionally, demonstrating a record of scholarly activities and possess experience working in an academic medical center environment that supports appointment in the College at rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. Appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or above requires a minimum of five years of continuing and productive service as an Assistant Professor/Associate Professor, or the equivalent. MINIMUM: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. PREFERRED: Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. Must be board certified/eligible in Infectious Disease. CLINICAL -The candidate will see patients and provide quality clinical care, within the USF Health System consisting of both inpatient services and Outpatient clinic services. At the discretion of department leadership, assignments may be at Tampa General Hospital, Moffitt Cancer Center or other USF affiliated sites. TEACHING -Bedside/Teaching of Medical Students, Residents, and Fellows during ID Service Rounds OTHER-Service and Professional Development. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43438": {
      "title": "APRN/PA - Instr. I -  Endocrinology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 10/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Health Care JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. Under general supervision and in accordance with standardized procedures, this position is responsible for performing physical examinations and treating common episodic and chronic health care problems, counseling patients and families, monitoring patient progress, assisting with medical research projects. Works in collaboration with other health care team members, consulting and referring as appropriate, but retains responsibility for ongoing clinical management of the patient, including diabetes management and ongoing care. Minimum -Master's degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. Additional Minimum- This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Candidates must be Board Certified/Board Eligible in Certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64 Preferred - Experience in Diabetes mellitus (DM), DM technologies, and obesity management. Clinical - 100% Manages the health care of select patient populations through advanced health assessment, diagnosis, intervention, and evaluation in a collaborative practice agreement with a physician. Prescriptive responsibilities are reviewed by collaborative physician. Coordinates the care of select patient populations, in a collaborative practice agreement with a physician, to ensure promotion of health and wellness through education of patients and families, coordination of services and placing referrals. Develops treatment plans, treats patients with acute problems including illnesses and minor injuries following a predetermined protocol in a collaborative practice agreement with a physician. Instructs and counsels patients, involves patients in informed decision making with regard to illness, procedures, treatment regiments and activities of daily living. Considers the patients and families' physical, psychosocial, educational and safety needs when planning care. Provides referral of patients needing diabetes education including pump and sensor training to the appropriate individuals at the USF Diabetes Center. Will work in an outpatient setting, acting as a member of the interdisciplinary team that facilitates the continuum of care and education of patients with diabetes. Participates in professional development and life long learning. Participates in service education programs and professional associations. Assesses development needs of staff and develops and delivers appropriate educational programs to meet staff needs. Maintains compliance with established policies and procedures, quality assurance, safety, environmental, infection control and requirements of accreditation and regulatory agencies. May participate in medical research projects, follow treatment protocols, screen and refer patients for research participation. Will assist in collection of data, attend research meetings, and follow up with patients. Provide referral of patients needing diabetes education including pump and sensor training to the appropriate individuals at the USF Diabetes Center. Will work in an outpatient setting, acting as a member of the interdisciplinary team that facilitates the continuum of care and education of patients with diabetes. Maintains compliance with established policies and procedures, quality assurance, safety, environmental, infection control and requirements of accreditation and regulatory agencies. May participate in medical research projects, follow treatment protocols, screen and refer patients for research participation. Will assist in collection of data, attend research meetings, and follow up with patients. Performs other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, service, and related activities. May be responsible for research and/or academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43232": {
      "title": "APRN  or PA/ Instr. I",
      "description": "Closing Date: 09/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Health Care JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The USF Department of Otolaryngology–Head & Neck Surgery is seeking a collaborative, motivated Advanced Practice Provider (APRN or PA) to join our growing academic team in a hybrid inpatient/transition-of-care role. This is a unique opportunity to work alongside a dynamic, subspecialty-trained faculty and our Otolaryngology residents within one of Florida's leading academic ENT programs—a department recognized among U.S. News & World Report's top 50 ENT service lines for five consecutive years and ranked among the top 20 nationally for research funding by the Blue Ridge Institute. The successful candidate will divide their time between inpatient consultative care at Tampa General Hospital and outpatient care at the USF South Tampa Center and/or Morsani Center, with a particular focus on bridging the inpatient-to-outpatient transition for our most complex patients. We are building this role for a clinician who values teamwork, thrives in a teaching environment, and is eager to develop into a true subspecialty expert in Otolaryngology. New graduates and experienced APPs are both encouraged to apply; structured onboarding, faculty mentorship, and graduated clinical autonomy are central to how we develop our team. Minimum: Master's or Medical degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. Additional Minimum: This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Previous experience working in Otolaryngology/ENT preferred. Clinical - • Clinical Management: Perform daily rounds, physical exams, and assessments for a designated caseload of inpatients. Will also maintain an outpatient clinic to see appropriate new patients and focus on follow up care for patients after hospital discharge. • Diagnostic & Treatment Planning: Order, interpret, and act upon laboratory tests, EKGs, and imaging results. • Prescriptive Authority: Prescribe medications, therapies, and non-pharmacological interventions within the scope of practice. • Procedures: Perform and become proficient in bedside/ENT procedures, such as wound management, tracheostomy care, suture removal, nasal endoscopy, otomicroscopy, and laryngoscopy depending on specialty, credentialing and clinical education from our department. • Discharge Planning: Coordinate the care plan to facilitate timely discharge and reduce length of stay. • Collaboration & Communication: Participate in interdisciplinary rounds, consult with specialists, and communicate changes in patient condition to the attending physician. • Documentation: Maintain accurate, timely electronic medical records (EMR) for all patient encounters. • Mentorship: Act as a clinical resource for bedside nursing staff Teaching - Engage actively with the Otolaryngology residency program, supporting teaching at the bedside and contributing to a culture of shared learning between APPs, residents, and faculty. •Participate in departmental educational conferences, multidisciplinary tumor boards, and case discussions. •Serve as a clinical resource for medical and APP students rotating through the department, modeling team-based care. •Pursue ongoing professional development through CME, specialty society engagement (e.g., SPAOHNS, SOHNS), and structured departmental learning opportunities. Research - Opportunity to participate in departmental clinical research initiatives, including ongoing trials in head and neck oncology, voice and hearing innovation, and airway pathology. •Opportunity to contribute to scholarly projects led by faculty and residents, with potential for coauthorship and presentation at regional and national meetings. •Ability to engage with the broader USF/TGH research enterprise as opportunities and interests align. Administrative - Complete clinical documentation accurately and in a timely manner, including consult notes, discharge summaries, and outpatient encounters. •Manage patient-specific paperwork on rotation with the broader APP and faculty team, including FMLA, disability, and procedural authorization documentation. •Participate in departmental quality improvement initiatives focused on metrics such as readmission rates, length of stay, transitions of care, and patient experience. •Contribute to operational workflow improvements and EPIC optimization in collaboration with the clinical leadership team. Other - Performs other duties as assigned by Chair. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42777": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Genetics",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of Pediatrics, Division of Genetics & Metabolism, University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, Tampa is seeking a physician who is Board Certified or eligible in Clinical Genetics for a full-time Clinical Faculty position at the Assistant Professor level or above. The successful candidate will join a team of 1 clinical geneticist, 1 biochemical geneticist, 1 Nurse practitioner, 5 genetic counselors, 3 metabolic dietitians, and 4 research coordinators. Primary responsibilities include the evaluation and management of pediatric and adult patients with genetic and metabolic disorders in both the outpatient and inpatient settings. Outpatients may be seen at USF Health Clinics. The inpatient services will include consultations at Tampa General Hospital and St. Joseph’s Hospital. As a clinical teaching faculty, the chosen candidate will be expected to participate in the education and training of medical students, residents, and genetic counselor students, as well as participate in research programs, including clinical trials and other clinical research. Medical degree from an accredited institution. Candidates must be board certified or board eligible in Clinical Genetics and Genomics and be eligible for full unrestricted Florida Medical License. Must meet university criteria for faculty appointment to the rank of assistant professor, associate or professor. Clinical: The candidate will provide inpatient consultative services for inborn errors of metabolism and general genetics at Tampa General Hospital and general genetics at St. Joseph’s Children’s Hospital, as well as outpatient USF Health clinics. Research : Participate in research programs to expand the scholarly activities of the division. The incumbent will be encouraged to participate in clinical trials and other clinical research. Teaching: Participate in the education and training of medical students, residents, fellows and genetic counselor students. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42003": {
      "title": "Open Rank-Palliative Care Physician",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences, and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Internal Medicine at the University of South Florida is seeking an Open Rank Faculty to provide Hospice and Palliative Care services in an inpatient patient care setting. Appointment as a USF faulty member carries with it attending staff privileges at Tampa General Hospital (TGH) and affiliated hospitals. TGH is a level 1 trauma center that serves as a tertiary care facility serving south central and west Florida. Appointment at the rank of Associate Professor requires a minimum of five years of continuing and productive service as an Assistant Professor, or the equivalent. Appointment at the rank of Full Professor requires a minimum of five years of continuing and productive service as an Associate Professor or the equivalent. Minimum: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in referred and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Preferred: Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full unrestricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Must be Board Certified in Palliative Care Medicine Clinical-The primary objective of palliative medicine is to help patients and families understand the status and likely progression of their illness and to help their physicians understand what is most important to the patient. This may involve conversations around prognosis, advanced directives, expertly managing pain and symptom distress and or facilitating transition to community services. Inpatient call and coverage for the hospice and palliative care service line. Developing ongoing treatment and disease management plans. Prescribe medicine and coordinate referrals as necessary. Conduct early detection screenings. Maintain accurate patient records and charts. Communicate effectively with patients, staff, physicians and administration. Teaching-Participate in didactic teaching and mentoring of medical and/or graduate students, residents, and/or post-doctoral fellows. Administrative-Protected time for administration, research, and/or education is consistent with holding specific leadership roles and fulfilling said responsibilities. Should you no longer hold those leadership roles (for any reason), the protected time may be removed and will be made up by an increase in cFTE assignments related to clinical patient care. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43324": {
      "title": "Neonatology APP/ Instr. I",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Health Care JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences, and the USF Physician's Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The APRN will act in accordance with Florida Statutes for the Nurse Practitioners Act. The care and management of critically ill infants requiring hospitalization in a level IV neonatal intensive care unit. This NICU Nurse Practitioner will cover night and/or day shifts as assigned including weekend coverage. The Neonatal Intensive Care Unit is based at Tampa General Hospital (TGH) in Tampa, FL. TGH is a 1,018-bed teaching hospital affiliated with the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine. It is a private not-for-profit hospital and one of the most comprehensive medical facilities in west central Florida, serving a dozen counties with a population of over 4 million. In addition to being a level one trauma center, it has a level 3 NICU. The 82-bed Jennifer Leigh Muma NICU is a designated Regional Perinatal Intensive Care Center designated by the State of Florida to deliver the highest level of medical care to premature and sick infants, and to women with high-risk pregnancies. USF/TGH Neonatology also participates in the Florida Perinatal Quality Collaborative, a statewide initiative to improve maternal and infant health outcomes in Florida. Neonatal services include a Neonatal Transport Team, Fetal Care Center, and Whole-Body Cooling. Pediatric subspecialties available for collaborative treatment of neonatal patients including Neurology, Neurosurgery, Ophthalmology, ENT, Cardiology, Pulmonology, Gastroenterology, Endocrinology, Hematology/Oncology, Nephrology, Metabolic Genetics. Educational Requirements: Master’s Degree in Nursing: ARNP training; Florida License. BLS/AED certification is required and must be maintained. Any equivalent combination of experience and education. Experience Requirements: 2-5 years; at least 2 years of experience evaluating pediatric patients (2 years’ experience assessing neonates preferred) Minimum 1-year nursing experience in a physician’s office or clinic experience in an ambulatory health care facility preferred. BLS/AED certification is required and must be maintained.ACLS or PALS Master’s degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64 Degree Equivalency Clause: Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree. • Senate Bill 1310- The Florida Senate (https://www.flsenate.gov/Session/Bill/2023/1310) is conditional upon meeting all employment eligibility requirements in the U.S. • SB 1310: Substitution of Work Experience for Postsecondary Education Requirements • A public employer may include a postsecondary degree as a baseline requirement only as an alternative to the number of years of direct experience required, not to exceed: • (a) Two years of direct experience for an associate degree; • (b) Four years of direct experience for a bachelor’s degree; • (c) Six years of direct experience for a master’s degree; • (d) Seven years of direct experience for a professional degree; or • (e) Nine years of direct experience for a doctoral degree • Related work experience may not substitute for any required licensure, certification, or registration required for the position of employment as established by the public employer and indicated in the advertised description of the position of employment. • Minimum Qualifications that require a high school diploma are exempt from SB 1310. Clinical: Ongoing evaluation and management of neonates and infants requiring care in the neonatal intensive care unit, participation in multidisciplinary rounds, and coordination of care with ancillary staff and family. Attendance at high-risk deliveries and immediate stabilization of critically ill neonates under the supervision of the attending Neonatologist. Documentation of all orders, procedures, and progress notes on the patient's medical record. Performs procedures necessary for the care of neonates and infants in the intensive care unit including endotracheal intubation, umbilical line placement, PICC line placement, lumbar punctures, and peripheral arterial lines. Teaching: Supervision of pediatric residents and participation in the teaching of APP students, pediatric residents and medical students. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a state university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/41930": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Reproductive Endocrinology and Infertility (REI) Physician",
      "description": "Closing Date: 21/10/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physicians’ Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The USF Health Morsani College of Medicine at the University of South Florida is the top-ranked medical school in Florida and has been named to the highest tier of medical schools in the nation, according to U.S. News & World Report. The Morsani College of Medicine’s Tier 1 status is a testament to its world-class research and educational programs, reflecting USF’s continuous growth and rapid rise in the national rankings. Over the past decade spanning from fiscal year 2014 to 2024, the college has experienced a remarkable 158% increase in research funding from the National Institutes of Health and a 212% increase in total research funding. This achievement also builds upon USF’s standing as a leading national research institution. The university attained a record-breaking $738 million in research funding for fiscal year 2024. USF also recently reached a historical milestone by becoming the first public university in Florida in 40 years to be invited to join the prestigious Association of American Universities, a group of the top 3% of universities in the U.S. and Canada. In partnership with Tampa General Hospital, the USF Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is proud to be ranked #5 in the nation and #1 in Florida, a reflection of our leadership in clinical care, education, and innovation. Position Summary The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of South Florida (USF) seeks a board-certified or board-eligible physician in Reproductive Endocrinology and Infertility (REI) for a joint clinical and academic appointment with Shady Grove Fertility (SGF) Tampa Bay. The successful candidate will provide exceptional, evidence-based reproductive clinical care and surgery, contribute to the advancement of research and education in the field, and collaborate with a multidisciplinary team in a high-volume academic medical center. This role offers a unique opportunity to integrate clinical practice with academic responsibilities, including teaching, research, and scholarly activities. The ideal candidate will be committed to excellence in patient care, medical education, and academic productivity. The primary focus of the REI will be the clinical care of fertility patients at SGF Tampa Bay locations, performance of reproductive surgeries at USF/TGH, supervision and teaching of REI fellows, ob-gyn residents, and medical students, and conducting of clinical research. The USF Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology is home to four ACGME-accredited fellowship programs, FPMRS, Maternal-Fetal Medicine, Gynecologic Oncology, and Reproductive Endocrinology and Infertility, as well as a highly regarded OB/GYN residency program with 7 trainees per year. The department fosters a strong academic community dedicated to advancing women’s health through excellence in clinical care, education, and research. Appointment Type: Full-Time, Joint Clinical and Academic employment with Shady Grove Fertility Tampa Bay Location: USF Health – Tampa Campus and Shady Grove Fertility, Tampa Bay Required: MD, MD/Ph.D. or DO from an accredited medical school. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic, research, and service. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in referred and other professional journals and be recognized authority in the field of REI. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full unrestricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. Board-certified or board-eligible in Obstetrics and Gynecology and REI. Demonstrated excellence in clinical care and commitment to patient-centered practice. Preferred: Academic teaching and research experience Record of scholarly publication or research funding Interest in leadership, program development, or innovation in reproductive medicine Responsibilities: Clinical: Provide comprehensive care in reproductive endocrinology and infertility, including: Fertility evaluations and treatments (e.g., IUI, IVF, ovulation induction) Endocrine disorders affecting reproduction Fertility preservation and third-party reproduction Reproductive surgery (minimally invasive, hysteroscopic, laparoscopic) at Tampa General Hospital Participate in outpatient clinics, surgical procedures, and on-call coverage as needed Collaborate with nursing, embryology, and allied health staff to ensure high-quality patient outcomes Support expansion of clinical programs, including innovations in ART, fertility preservation, LGBTQ+ family-building, etc. Academic Responsibilities: Teaching: Educate and mentor medical students, residents, and fellows Lead or participate in didactic sessions, journal clubs, and grand rounds Serve as a preceptor in clinical rotations Research and Scholarly Activity: Participate in or lead clinical, translational, or basic science research aligned with REI Seek external funding and publish findings in peer-reviewed journals Present at regional and national conferences Administration and Leadership: Participate in departmental, college, and university service. Represent the department as appropriate in institutional initiatives and external professional activities."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42327": {
      "title": "Hydrocephalus Open Rank",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences, and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Neurosurgery at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking an Open Rank faculty position within our multidisciplinary Cerebral Spinal Fluid Disorder Center. We welcome a dedicated and innovative clinician to join our collaborative team of physiatrists, neurosurgeons and physical therapists committed to advancing the diagnosis and treatment of CSF disorders. Work in a state-of-the-art academic medical center with CSF disorder research and treatment facilities. Collaborate with a multidisciplinary team to diagnosis, treat and provide longitudinal care for these chronic diseases. Participate in research and education in CSF dynamics, hydrocephalus and intracranial hypertension and engage in teaching medical students, residents and fellows. Minimum: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Preferred: Experience in management of cerebral spinal fluid disorders is preferred but not required. CLINICAL - Collaborate with a multidisciplinary team to diagnose, treat and provide longitudinal care for patients with hydrocephalus and intra cranial hypertension. TEACHING - Engage teaching medical students, residents, and fellows."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42767": {
      "title": "Professor/Director, Cancer Control, Prevention and Epidemiology Program at TGH Cancer Institute",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/01/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences, and the USF Physicians’ Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The incumbent serves as a senior-level faculty member in cancer epidemiology research. As a ranked professorial faculty position at USF, the incumbent will have teaching, scholarship, and service responsibilities. In addition, the incumbent will serve as Director of the Cancer Control, Prevention, and Epidemiology Program at the TGH Cancer Institute, collaborating with faculty across USF Health to lead interdisciplinary initiatives in translational and population-based cancer research. The incumbent will report directly to the Chair of the Department of Epidemiology who will meet annually with the incumbent to discuss the specific assignment for the upcoming assignment year and to review performance during the previous year. The Director of the TGH Cancer Institute will provide day-to-day direction for the duties related to the role of Director of the Cancer Control, Prevention and Epidemiology Program, as well as provide input into the incumbent’s annual assignment and evaluation. Incumbent is expected to obtain extramural funding to cover a minimum of 40% of annual base salary plus benefits costs beginning the fourth year of employment. Documents to be uploaded with the application include a letter of application addressing the advertised minimum and preferred qualifications for the position to which applying, a CV, and a list of three references. Review of applications will not begin until all required documents are uploaded into Careers. References will not be contacted without notifying applicants in advance. Minimum Qualifications: Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in referred and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Professor Additional Minimum Qualifications: Two years of sustained accomplishment at the Associate Professor level as an Epidemiologist at an accredited university – or the equivalent in a government, military, or research setting. National and/or international record of excellence in independent and/or collaborative research in cancer epidemiology (e.g., cancer etiology, prevention, early detection, treatment outcomes, survivorship, health equity, or cancer-related public health genomics) supported by substantial publications of research finding. Record of sustained extramural funding in the areas referenced above. Record of excellence in teaching including a clearly defined teaching philosophy, participation as a major professor for thesis and/or dissertation committees and successful direction of the work of master's and doctoral candidates, or equivalent trainees where applicable. Record of substantive contribution of service to their university or organization and to the field, profession, and community. Compelling evidence of significant achievement among peers in one’s discipline or professional field at the national or international level. Record of collegiality in their university or organization. Preferred Qualifications : Current extramural funded research providing a minimum of 40% salary support. Record of leading strategic research initiatives. Record of mentoring junior faculty or equivalent. Record of successfully leading multidisciplinary cancer related research teams or institutional programs that include cancer center, medical center, or medical system engagement, analogous to the Tampa General Hospital Cancer Institute, Moffitt Cancer Center, USF Health, or U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs medical facilities. Demonstrated record of collaborative cancer related research partnerships involving cancer centers, medical centers, or health systems, including institutions such as the Tampa General Hospital Cancer Institute, Moffitt Cancer Center, USF Health, or U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs. Classroom and/or online teaching experience as an epidemiologist at the graduate level, particularly in cancer epidemiology or related public health topics. Record of applied innovative teaching approaches in academic and/or practice-based settings. Leadership in professional or scientific organizations related to epidemiology, cancer research, or public health. Research program that aligns with the strategic priorities of the Department of Epidemiology of the USF College of Public Health and the TGH Cancer Institute. Instructional Duties: 20% FTE Teach courses in cancer epidemiology and/or epidemiologic methods at the master’s or doctoral levels. Advise graduate students; chair and serve on master’s and doctoral student committees. If interests and expertise allow, contribute to undergraduate teaching and research mentorship. This will involve teaching or co-teaching three courses per year. Extramural research support can replace one or two courses, if research time is required to meet the extramural commitments. Also contribute to student and junior faculty mentorship and academic leadership, in alignment with departmental and institutional priorities. Research/Scholarship Duties: 70% FTE Serve as Director of the Cancer Control, Prevention, and Epidemiology Program at the TGH Cancer Institute. Responsibilities include shaping and implementing the program’s strategic vision; fostering collaborative research between USF and TGH investigators; mentoring faculty, trainees, and staff; and guiding translational and population-based initiatives that enhance cancer control and equity across the region. The Director will also represent the program in institutional planning efforts and contribute to elevating its national visibility and impact. This will be supported at a 10% effort level within this 70% FTE responsibility. Establish and maintain an externally funded research program in cancer epidemiology, focused on areas such as cancer etiology, prevention, early detection, treatment outcomes, survivorship or health equity using molecular, clinical, behavioral, environmental or policy-relevant approaches. Secure competitive funding to support research activities and meet the required salary support level by the start of the fourth year of employment. Collaborate across departments and institutions on interdisciplinary initiatives. Publish scholarly work in peer-reviewed journals and present findings at national and international conferences. Mentor graduate students; provide leadership in interdisciplinary cancer research initiatives; and represent the department in college- and university-level strategic planning related to cancer prevention and public health. Service Duties: 10% FTE Engage in service activities at the departmental, college, university, and professional levels. This includes participation in faculty governance, committees, and special initiatives, as well as involvement in professional organizations and scientific review activities. Also includes serving as a formal mentor (Department or College) to junior faculty. Contribute to community and public health service efforts by applying professional expertise to local, regional, or national initiatives that align with the department’s mission and the field of cancer epidemiology. Administrative Duties : 0 % FTE (Restricted to individuals with formal College-wide administrative appointments by the Dean. Direct administrative effort related to specific course/program/concentration should be reflected in the Instruction category, Other Instructional Related. Direct administrative effort related to a specific research project should be reflected in the Research category. Center Directors should be reflected in College or Sponsored Research depending upon the funding source.) ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF POSITION: The creation, dissemination and translation of knowledge through collaborative research; teaching and advising graduate students; and active engagement in professional and community service. Serving as Director of the Cancer Control, Prevention and Epidemiology Program at TGH Cancer Institute, collaborating closely with faculty in the Department of Epidemiology and USF Health."
    },
