    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42770": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Physics - Energy Storage, Conversion, and Harvesting",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Physics at the University of South Florida, Tampa, seeks to fill a 9-month, full-time, tenure-earning position at the Assistant Professor level in experimental Applied Physics. Applicants should have an outstanding record of research, a commitment to teaching and demonstrate the potential for developing a research program that engages students. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. The successful candidate will develop an active experimental research program capable of attracting external funding and producing high-impact peer-reviewed publications with students. The starting date is August 7, 2026. The Physics Department has strong research programs in experimental/theoretical biophysics, condensed matter, and optics. The University of South Florida also offers excellent opportunities to interact with research programs in the College of Arts and Sciences, Engineering, and Medicine, as well as the Moffitt Cancer Center. The minimum requirement for this position is a doctoral degree from an accredited institution in Physics or a closely related field. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Preference will be given to candidates with existing strengths in the areas of energy conversion, energy storage, and/or energy sustainability. Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access institution. For disability accommodations contact Edwin Perez ( edwinperez@usf.edu ), a minimum of five working days in advance. This position is subject to Foreign Influence Screening. House Bill 7017 (“HB 7017”) How To Apply: When applying, please attach the following required materials: Cover letter Curriculum vita with publication record Statement of teaching philosophy (1 page) Research plan (2-3 pages) *In addition, applicants should have three (3) letters of recommendation sent to physearch@usf.edu . All applications completed by December 1, 2025 will be given full consideration, although the search will continue until the position is filled. Questions regarding this search should be directed to Prof. George S. Nolas, Search Committee Chair, at physearch@usf.edu ."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42773": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Biomedical Physics",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Physics at the University of South Florida, Tampa campus, seeks to fill a 9-month, full-time, tenure-earning position at the Assistant Professor level in experimental biomedical sciences or biophysics. The appointment start date is August 7, 2026. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Our Physics Department has well-established research programs in experimental and theoretical biophysics, materials physics, and optics. We also interact with other researchers in USF’s Colleges of Arts and Sciences, Engineering, and Medicine, as well as the nearby Moffitt Cancer Center. The minimum requirement for this position is a doctoral degree from an accredited institution in Physics or a closely related field, relevant postdoctoral experience, and demonstrate potential for attracting independent extramural funding. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Preference will be given to candidates who have demonstrated strengths in the areas of optical and/or molecular biophysics and the potential for collaborations in basic or translational biomedicine. How To Apply: When applying, please attach the following required materials: Cover letter Curriculum vita with publication record Statement of teaching philosophy (1 page) Research plan (2-3 pages) In addition, applicants should have three (3) letters of recommendation sent to physearch@usf.edu . All applications completed by December 1, 2025 will be given full consideration, but the search will continue until the position is filled. Questions regarding this search should be directed to Prof. Ghanim Ullah, Search Committee Chair ( physearch@usf.edu ). Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access institution. For disability accommodations contact Edwin Perez ( edwinperez@usf.edu ), a minimum of five working days in advance. This position is subject to Foreign Influence Screening. House Bill 7017 (“HB 7017”) The successful candidate will establish a nationally recognized research program, teach effectively at the undergraduate and graduate levels, and mentor student research at all levels."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42775": {
      "title": "Pediatric ENT Open Rank",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of Otolaryngology at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking an Open Rank to fill the position of Pediatric Otolaryngology. The candidate should be Fellowship Trained in Pediatric Otolaryngology. This position will join our core faculty in a growing department which has its flagship clinical site at Tampa General Hospital (TGH). The provider would work closely with our current staff members of subspecialists and with the local outreach community. This is a full-time 12-month salaried faculty appointments open rank and carries with it attending staff privileges at TGH. TGH is a level 1 trauma center that serves as tertiary care facility covering south central and west Florida. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, service, and related activities. May be responsible for research and/or academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or statewide committees. Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be recognized by authority in the field or specialization. Teaching Duties • Enhance current otolaryngology residency experiences by offering center as unique rotation focused on demonstrating multi-disciplinary care and experiences with specialists focused on care of complex pediatric otolaryngology surgery patients. • Support resident-driven research experience by discussing pediatric otolaryngology diseases with cohort opportunities • Within two years, establish a Pediatric Otolaryngology-fellowship training program Administrative Duties • Enhance current otolaryngology residency experiences by offering center as unique rotation focused on demonstrating multi-disciplinary care and experiences with specialists focused on care of complex pediatric otolaryngology surgery patients. • Support resident-driven research experience by discussing pediatric otolaryngology diseases with cohort opportunities • Within two years, establish a Pediatric Otolaryngology-fellowship training program Clinical Duties • Dedicate clinical efforts to improving medical and surgical outcomes for pediatric otolaryngology patients with a focus on prevention • Ease of referral from TGH ER, Brandon Healthplex and within patient radius • Engage in broad CME sessions within community to promote center and faculty as thought leaders in the community and region Other Duties As assigned by the Chair"
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42783": {
      "title": "Vascular Surgery - TGH North",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of Surgery at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking an open-rank academic Vascular Surgeon to join the Division of Vascular Surgery at TGH North, located at TGH Brooksville /TGH Spring Hill /TGH Crystal River. MINIMUM: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. Candidates must be Board Certified/Board Eligible. PREFERRED: Certified (or eligible for certification according to current requirements) by the American Board of Surgery or American Osteopathic Board of Surgery in Surgery, with Added Qualifications in Vascular Surgery. Demonstrated proficiency in the field of Vascular Surgery. Demonstrated commitment to teaching health care professional students, residents, and practicing clinicians. 5% TEACHING DUTIES: Successfully complete program requirements of ACGME institutional and residency/fellowship . Direct supervision of residents. 95% CLINICAL DUTIES: Responsible (with authority) for all aspects of the Vascular Program to include call panel privileges, treatment protocols and guidelines, service policies, education, community outreach, hospital executive interface, and performance improvement; promotes multidisciplinary approach to care. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF POSITION: Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State University. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42787": {
      "title": "Open Rank - General Endocrinology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 19/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of Health Informatics Institute at University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine, USF Diabetes and Endocrinology Center is seeking a BC/BE Internal Medicine Endocrinologist for full-time, faculty position. All candidates must have or be eligible for an unrestricted Florida medical license. The salary for this position is negotiable. USF DDE is administratively housed within- and has the support of the USF Health Informatics Institute in the development of research proposals and publication of findings. Currently USF DEC is #18 in USA based on US New ranking. The USF DDE operates in collaboration with Tampa General Hospital, USF’s major teaching hospital, the James A. Haley Veterans Hospital, and the H. Lee Moffitt Cancer Center & Research Institute. A major facet of the USF DDE is the USF Diabetes Center (USF DC), a state-of-the-art facility for education, clinical care, and clinical research with a large and expanding portfolio of clinical research studies in both Type 1 and Type 2 Diabetes, and general endocrinology. In collaboration with other specialties, USF DEC developed multiple programs including weight management, pituitary comprehensive pituitary program, thyroid/parathyrpid program, and osteoporosis program. Therefore, candidates with clinical and clinical research foci in general endocrinology, especially pituitary interest are encouraged to apply. Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. BC/BE Internal Medicine Endocrinologist. All candidates must have or be eligible for an unrestricted Florida medical license. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. This position is expected to be an outstanding clinician that will contribute to the expansion of Center clinical services and clinical research initiatives with pituitary disorders and other general endocrine disorders, and consultative services to assist regional primary care physicians in their patient care. This position’s main focus will be on general endocrinology, especially pituitary disorders. Clinical responsibilities include outpatient clinical care, participation in the USF DC faculty call schedule, and consultation at area hospitals. Professional Development and other duties as assigned. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42745": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Instruction - Physics",
      "description": "Closing Date: 18/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Physics at the University of South Florida, Tampa, seeks to fill a full-time, 9-month, non-tenure earning Assistant Professor of Instruction position starting August 7, 2026. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Applicants must have a doctorate degree from an accredited institution in Physics or a closely related field and have experience in teaching both calculus and algebra based General Physics courses. Conclusion of this search is subject to final budget approval. According to Florida Law, applications and meetings regarding them are open to the public. USF is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access Institution. For disability accommodation, contact Edwin Perez ( edwinperez@usf.edu ), a minimum of five working days in advance. This position is subject to Foreign Influence Screening. House Bill 7017 (“HB 7017”) The position involves teaching 3-4 undergraduate classes in both Fall and Spring semesters. How To Apply: Apply online by completing the required information and including your experience as it relates to the qualifications stated. When applying to an opening you will have the opportunity to upload the required application materials listed below. Only online applications are accepted for this position. Complete the online application and attach the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vita Statement of teaching philosophy (1 page) Student comments from courses taught previously All applications completed by January 5, 2026 , will be given full consideration, the position will be open until filled."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42709": {
      "title": "Open Rank-Rheumatology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 17/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Internal Medicine at University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking an Open Rank Clinical Faculty to perform Rheumatology services at the Morsani Center for Advanced Healthcare, USF South Tampa Center, TGH Health Park and Tampa General Hospital. This is a full-time 12-month salaried faculty appointment and carries with it attending staff privileges at Tampa General Hospital (TGH) and affiliated hospitals Minimum: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Must be Board Certified/Eligible in: Internal Medicine/Rheumatology Clinical: Practice in an outpatient clinic with some inpatient consults treating Rheumatology patients. Lead outreach efforts to improve outcomes in at risk patients. Administrative: Provide oversight and leadership of the clinical simulation and bioskills team at USF Health CAMLS including daily operations of the clinical skills and bioskills lab, oversight of staff of simulation operations specialists, and content oversight and simulation expertise for CAMLS courses and programs. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42697": {
      "title": "Burn, Wound, and General Reconstruction-Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States ORGANIZATIONAL SUMMARY: USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician?s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html POSITION SUMMARY: The University of South Florida's Department of Plastic Surgery is seeking a fellowship trained hand surgeon at the Assistant Professor level to join our growing plastic surgery team at USF/Tampa General Hospital (TGH)/Moffitt Cancer Center. Successful faculty candidates will be appointed in the USF Health Department of Plastic Surgery and provide care at one of the busiest hospitals in Florida. Candidates must be a physician and eligible for licensure in the State of Florida, and must have completed a plastic surgery residency and a complex extremity/hand focused fellowship POSITION QUALIFICATIONS: MINIMUM: Docotral Degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate for the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Professor. Board certified or board eligible (according to current requirements) by the appropriate American Board with added qualifications in Plastic Surgery. Must hold or be eligible to hold a full unrestricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan and be a member of the medical staff in good standing at the hospitals where he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. RESPONSIBILITIES: The position includes the management of patients in inpatient and outpatient settings. Outpatients may be seen at the University of South Florida College of Medicine Medical Clinics, and TGH sites. Complete clinical obligations such as chart completion, patient follow-up, finalize billing, etc"
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42698": {
      "title": "Open Rank - CT Surgeon-Thoracic & Cardiovascular Surgery",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Surgery at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking an open-rank academic cardiac trained CT Surgeon to join the Division of Cardiothoracic Surgery. MINIMUM: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. Candidates must be Board Certified/Board Eligible. PREFERRED: Certified (or eligible for certification according to current requirements) by the American Board of Surgery or American Osteopathic Board of Surgery in Surgery, with Added Qualifications in CT Surgery. Demonstrated proficiency in the field of CT Surgery. Demonstrated commitment to teaching health care professional students, residents, and practicing clinicians. RESPONSIBILITIES: TEACHING DUTIES: Successfully complete program requirements of ACGME institutional and residency/fellowship . Direct supervision of residents. CLINICAL DUTIES: Responsible (with authority) for all aspects of the CT Program to include call panel privileges, treatment protocols and guidelines, service policies, education community outreach, hospital executive interface, and performance improvement; promotes multidisciplinary approach to care. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF POSITION: Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher level administrator of a State University. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42700": {
      "title": "Reconstructive Urology - Open Rank",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Urology at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking a Open Rank to fill the position of Reconstructive Urologist. The candidate should be Fellowship Trained in Reconstructive Urology. This position will join our core faculty in a growing department which has its flagship clinical site at Tampa General Hospital (TGH). The provider would work closely with our current staff members of subspecialists and with the local outreach community. ORGANIZATIONAL SUMMARY: USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician's Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html POSITION SUMMARY: The Department of Urology at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking a Open Rank to fill the position of Reconstructive Urologist. The candidate should be Fellowship Trained in Reconstructive Urology. This position will join our core faculty in a growing department which has its flagship clinical site at Tampa General Hospital (TGH). The provider would work closely with our current staff members of subspecialists and with the local outreach community. This is a full-time 12-month salaried faculty appointments open rank and carries with it attending staff privileges at TGH. TGH is a level 1 trauma center that serves as tertiary care facility covering South, Central and West Florida. MINIMUM: Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Candidates must be Board Certified/Board Eligible in Urology Focus in Reconstructive Urology. PREFERRED: Fellowship trained in Reconstructive Urology. TEACHING: - Enhance current urology residency experiences by offering center as unique rotation focused on demonstrating multi-disciplinary care and experiences with specialists focused on care of complex reconstructive surgery patients. - Support resident-driven research experience by discussing reconstructive diseases with cohort opportunities - Within two years, establish a Reconstructive-fellowship training program RESEARCH: - Establish reconstructive urologic cohort that will serve as launching point for center-based scholarly work as well as promote use of data by other USF faculty interested in outcomes - Work with industry to develop and trial emerging technologies within center - Work with pharmaceutical and device collaborators on developing unique study protocols QUALITY and SAFETY - Monitor, report and identify quality and safety gaps among urologic patients on an ongoing basis ADMINISTRATIVE DUTIES: - Marketing - With establishment of clinic, strategize within first fiscal year to determine realistic proportion of volume increase within a 1 yr., 3yr. and 5 yr. model - Determine current patient radius and volumes - Assess best-practice revenue models for clinic to consider methods to enhance billing and collection of revenues within USF and TGH care models - Philanthropic funding through TGH foundation - NIDDK or other grants Establish regional/national multi-disciplinary reconstructrive urology center based at TGH. - More multidisciplinary clinics helps US News and World report rankings - Other duties as assigned. CLINICAL DUTIES: - Dedicate clinical efforts to improving medical and surgical outcomes for reconstructive patients with a focus on prevention. - Ease of referral from TGH ER, Brandon Healthplex and within patient radius - Engage in broad CME sessions within community to promote center and faculty as thought leaders in the community and region Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42672": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Urologic Surgeon, Stone Specialty",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html Open Rank - Urologic Surgeon, Stone Specialty The USF Department of Urology is searching for a Residency Trained Provider with a clinical interest in Stone Disease and General Urology to join as core faculty. He/She would join a growing Department which has its flagship clinical site at Tampa General Hospital. This new recruit would be expected to provide the full service line in the management of patients with nephrolithiasis and general urology pathology. The provider would work closely with our current staff members of subspecialists and with the local outreach community. This is a full-time 12-month salaried faculty appointment open rank and carries with it attending staff privileges at Tampa General Hospital (TGH) and affiliated hospitals. TGH is a level 1 trauma center that serves as a tertiary care facility serving south central and west Florida Minimum Qualifications: Must have a medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. Must hold or be eligible for a full unrestricted Florida medical license. Preferred: Candidate must have completed residency in Urology and have special focus in urological surgical procedures related to nephrolithiasis. Candidate should either have American Board of Urology certification or be eligible for certification. Clinical Establish multi-disciplinary clinic that integrates care between urology, nephrology (Elias Doumit), and nutrition/dietician to offer comprehensive and innovative care to stone patients. • Dedicate clinical efforts to improving medical and surgical outcomes for stone patients with a focus on prevention. o Ease of referral from TGH ER, Brandon Healthplex and within patient radius • Engage in broad CME sessions within community to promote center and faculty as thought leaders in the community and region Research Establish stone-specific disease cohort that will serve as launching point for center-based scholarly work as well as promote use of data by other USF faculty interested in stone-related outcomes • Work with industry to develop and trial emerging technologies within center • Work with pharmaceutical and device collaborators on developing unique study protocols QUALITY and SAFETY • Monitor, report and identify quality and safety gaps among stone patients on an ongoing basis Teaching Enhance current urology residency experiences by offering center as unique rotation focused on demonstrating multi-disciplinary care and experiences with specialists focused on care of stones • Support resident-driven research experience by discussing stone-specific disease cohort opportunities • Within five years, establish a Stone-fellowship training program. Administrative • Marketing • With establishment of clinic, strategize within first fiscal year to determine realistic proportion of volume increase within a 1 yr., 3yr. and 5 yr. model o Determine current patient radius and volumes • Assess best-practice revenue models for clinic to consider methods to enhance billing and collection of revenues within USF and TGH care models • Discuss alternate revenue strategies including but not limited to nutraceuticals, alternate diagnostics and other to maximize clinical revenue o Philanthropic funding through TGH foundation o NIDDK or other grants • More multidisciplinary clinics helps US News and World report rankings"
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42670": {
      "title": "Neuropsychologist- Open Rank",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States ORGANIZATIONAL SUMMARY: USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician's Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html POSITION SUMMARY: The department of neurosurgery is seeking a neuropsychology candidate to join our growing team. This position will: -Provide outpatient neuropsychological care following standard guidelines. -Works in the capacity of a licensed provider in a competent, capable, professional manner which exemplifies the current standard of care in neuropsychology. -Assists patients and their families during their entry and passage through the services in the USF Neuropsychology Division Clinics. - Assesses neurobehavioral care using the appropriate neuropsychological assessments following current standards of practice. -Develops a treatment plan and communicates with family and the patient MINIMUM: The successful candidate will be a graduate from an approved school and training program in psychology, and completed postdoctoral training in neuropsychology. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. PREFERRED: The incumbent knows and utilizes continuous quality improvement methodologies and practices evidence-based neuropsychology SPECIAL SKILLS/TRAINING: Preference given to candidates whom are board certified in clinical neuropsychology The incumbent will participate in the undergraduate medical education program including the Behavioral Medicine Course, the Neuropsychology Residency and subspecialty lectures as needed. The incumbent will teach residents in Neuropsychology. The candidate will be able to teach the fundamentals of neuropsychological evaluation in the adult and geriatric populations. The incumbent will serve as an enrichment supervisor for neuropsychology residents as well as medical students interested in neuropsychology. The incumbent will participate and collaborate with research projects in the Department of Neurosurgery and the USF Concussion Center as well as potentially other Centers in USF Health (e.g., Byrd Alzheimer's Disease Research Center and Movement Disorders, ALS, Multiple Sclerosis, etc.) that require the services of a neuropsychologist. Provide outpatient neuropsychological care following standard guidelines. Works in the capacity of a licensed provider in a competent, capable, professional manner which exemplifies the current standard of care in neuropsychology. Assists patients and their families during their entry and passage through the services in the USF Neuropsychology Division Clinics. Assesses neurobehavioral care using the appropriate neuropsychological assessments following current standards of practice. Develops a treatment plan and communicates with family and the patient"
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42673": {
      "title": "Ophthalmology Researcher (Optic Nerve) (Open Rank)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 12/02/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Department of Ophthalmology at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking a junior faculty member to join its research mission. This position will perform basic science and/or translational research in specialized areas such as keratoconjunctivitis sicca (dry eye). This position will also be responsible for teaching to include didactic and bench-side teaching of undergraduate and graduate students and postdoctoral fellows; presenting at departmental grand rounds and college seminars. ORGANIZATIONAL SUMMARY: USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician's Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html POSITION SUMMARY: The Department of Ophthalmology at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine is seeking a junior faculty member to join its research mission. This position will perform basic science and/or translational research in specialized areas such as keratoconjunctivitis sicca (dry eye). This position will also be responsible for teaching to include didactic and bench-side teaching of undergraduate and graduate students and postdoctoral fellows; presenting at departmental grand rounds and college seminars. MINIMUM: Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor. PREFERRED: Optic nerve research experience Maintain a nationally competitive research program with continued extramural funding, peer-reviewed publications, and collaboration with other faculty. Participate in didactic teaching and mentoring medical and graduate students. Participate in service functions of the department and university, as well as at the national levels, including committees, editorial boards, and study sections."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/40018": {
      "title": "General Cardiology APRN or PA",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobFunction: Instructors JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Division of Cardiovascular Sciences and the Department of Internal Medicine at the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine is seeking an Advanced Registered Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant for a full-time position at the Instructor rank. Evaluation with diagnostic testing and history taking in the patient population with a suspected or confirmed cardiology diagnosis referred from Internal Medicine, Emergency physicians or other specialty. Communication with patient, family and referring provider regarding recommendations and findings based on current guidelines. Education regarding diagnosis, testing and results. Independently provides care to patients in cardiology clinic under general or indirect supervision. Manages medical problems; initiates, monitors and alters pharmacologic or lifestyle regimens. MINIMUM: Master's or Medical degree from an accredited institution in an appropriate field of specialization or equivalent qualifications based on professional experience and otherwise qualified to perform assigned duties. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Instructor. This position requires graduation from an accredited Advanced Practice Registered Nurse academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 464 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64, or graduation from an accredited Physician Assistant academic degree program and certification as outlined in Florida Statutes 458 and 459 and Florida Administrative Code, Chapter 64. Preferred Certified Acute Care or Acute Care Adult Gerontologic Nurse Practitioner, or Physician Assistant. Candidates must be Board Certified/Board Eligible. PREFERRED: Certified Acute Care or Acute Care Adult Gerontologic Nurse Practitioner or Physician Assistant ADMINISTRATIVE DUTIES: Assist and coordinate patient care with referring provider, outpatient follow up and recommendations based on findings. Education of patient and family regarding diagnosis, findings, and follow-up. Address patient and staff inquiries and questions via medical record. Documentation of all orders, procedures, and progress notes on the patient’s electronic medical record. CLINICAL: Evaluation with diagnostic testing and history taking in the patient population with a suspected or confirmed cardiology diagnosis referred from Internal Medicine, Emergency physicians, or other specialties. Triages inpatient consults, and patient phone calls renew prescriptions, coordinates care, and assessed post-procedure problems. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, service, and related activities. May be responsible for research and/or academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees. Performs other duties as assigned."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/37300": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor (Heart Institute)",
      "description": "Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States We are seeking candidates for tenured or tenure-track positions at all ranks, who work on themes of heart failure (systolic, diastolic, congenital), regenerative cardiovascular medicine including tissue engineering, and molecular imaging. Successful candidates for this position are expected to have already established or have the potential to establish a nationally recognized, competitively funded research program including graduate/medical student mentoring. We are seeking candidates for tenured or tenure-track positions at all ranks, who work on themes of heart failure (systolic, diastolic, congenital), regenerative cardiovascular medicine including tissue engineering, and molecular imaging. Successful candidates for this position are expected to have already established or have the potential to establish a nationally recognized, competitively funded research program including graduate/medical student mentoring. Successful candidates will be provided with dry and wet laboratory space in the new downtown campus of the Morsani College of Medicine. Based on qualifications, the home department may be Molecular Pharmacology & Physiology, Internal Medicine, Surgery, Biomedical Engineering, or other relevant departments at USF. Successful candidates will be offered institutional salary commensurate with experience and highly competitive start-up packages that promote success. MINIMUM: Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate or Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing, or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. MD, PhD, MD/PhD with at least 1 National Institutes of Health (NIH) grant performing basic research in cardiovascular disease. PREFERRED: MD, PhD, MD/PhD with more than 1 National Institutes of Health (NIH) grant performing basic research in cardiovascular disease. TEACHING DUTIES: Provide didactic and benchside teaching of medical students, graduate students, and post-doctoral fellows and provide college-wide seminars RESEARCH: Perform basic and translational research related to heart disease. Publish in major peer-reviewed journals, continue to maintain NIH and other grants. ADMINISTRATIVE DUTIES: Serve in governance, service, and community outreach tasks OTHER DUTIES: As assigned by Chair"
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/43122": {
      "title": "Open Rank - MFM",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/04/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences, and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician's Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology at the University of South Florida (USF) is recruiting a Maternal Fetal Medicine physician to fill its open academic position. This new physician will join our established MFM team who provide comprehensive maternal-fetal care. The Division's clinical scope is broad, including coverage of labor and delivery, the antepartum service, obstetrical ultrasound, prenatal diagnosis procedures, and perinatal consultation. We have an active and growing fetal therapy program that includes laser therapy and in-utero surgical procedures, as well as robust clinical programs for managing pregnancies complicated by placenta accreta and other complex medical and surgical conditions, including cardio-obstetrics. Our primary clinic is located at 2 Tampa General Circle, Tampa, FL 33606. Clinical activities are complemented by opportunities in medical education and participation in statewide perinatal quality collaborative initiatives. Most of the Division members are actively engaged in clinical/translational research or other innovative clinical programs that match their interests. We have an ACGME-accredited MFM Fellowship and a robust OB/GYN residency program comprised of 24 residents. The MFM Division is actively involved in educating fellows, residents, and medical students. Our primary affiliate, Tampa General Hospital (TGH), boasts more than 6,200 deliveries annually and has an 82-bed Level IV NICU. MINIMUM: Must possess an MD or equivalent degree from an accredited institution and be board-eligible/certified in Obstetrics and Gynecology. Candidates must have successfully completed a Maternal-Fetal Medicine fellowship. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Interest in the education of residents and fellows. Must be eligible for an unrestricted medical license in the State of Florida. Successful candidates for these positions are expected to have an established record of academic productivity. Salary and academic rank are commensurate with experience, qualifications, and sources of external funding. For appointments at the level of Associate or Full Professor, preference is given to individuals with an established research program and/or grant portfolio transferable to USF. Participation in graduate and/or medical student education and mentoring is also expected. The Morsani College of Medicine offers institutional salary support commensurate with experience and external sources of funding, competitive start-up packages, dry and wet laboratory space, excellent core facilities, and a collegial atmosphere to create an environment that promotes success. CLINICAL: Provide general and high-risk Obstetrics and Gynecology care, including ambulatory care, deliveries, and surgery. TEACHING: Teach medical students and residents through lectures, rounds, and clinical activity in patient offices, labor and delivery, and the operating room. ADMINISTRATIVE: Close encounters timely, follow up with patient requests. OTHER DUTIES: Professional development and service. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42105": {
      "title": "Chair Radiation Oncology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 14/11/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html. The USF Health Morsani College of Medicine (MCOM), in collaboration with Tampa General Hospital (TGH) as part of the integrated USF - TGH Academic Health System, is seeking a distinguished and dynamic individual to serve as the Chair of Radiation Oncology. This position also includes the role of Medical Director for Radiation Oncology at Tampa General Hospital. The Chair of Radiation Oncology will be responsible for leading the MCOM’s Department of Radiation Oncology, fostering a culture of excellence in clinical care, research, and education. The ideal candidate will be eligible to be a Full Professor in the medical school, with a national reputation in Radiation Oncology and proven leadership skills in academic medicine. This role requires a visionary leader who can drive the department's strategic initiatives and enhance its national standing. Further, the Chair must mentor and cultivate faculty, providers, trainees, and work in a highly collaborative cancer institute environment at TGH. MD or equivalent degree with board certification in Radiation Oncology. Full Professor with a national reputation in Radiation Oncology. Proven leadership skills in academic medicine, with experience in leading, managing, and developing a high performing multidisciplinary team. Demonstrated experience with large-scale cancer clinical trials and NIH-funded investigation. Experience working in an NCI-funded cancer center environment is strongly preferred. Strong commitment to clinical excellence, research, and education. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Doctoral degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in referred and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Associate Professor or Full Professor. Provide leadership and oversight for the Department of Radiation Oncology, ensuring the highest standards of clinical care, research, education, and faculty development. Serve as the Medical Director for Radiation Oncology at Tampa General Hospital, overseeing clinical operations and ensuring the delivery of high-quality patient care. Develop and implement strategic plans to advance the department's mission and goals."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/42275": {
      "title": "Radiation Oncology",
      "description": "Closing Date: 09/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine is accepting applications for a Clinical Radiation Oncology Faculty position to begin in 2026. This is a full-time position in the Department of Radiology, Division of Radiation Oncology at the University of South Florida, Morsani College of Medicine for an American Board of Radiology board eligible/certified candidate. The candidate is expected to engage in clinical, research, teaching, and administrative activities, while working closely with our clinical partner, Tampa General Hospital (TGH). The candidate will be responsible for the coordination of care within the Cancer Institute and with other services and relevant affiliated sites with USF Health. Medical Degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing or research in refereed and other professional journals and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full un-restricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties Provide outpatient radiation therapy services and consults at various TGH locations. Supply appropriate quality assurance measures to qualify for industry accreditation. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher level administrator of a State university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44550": {
      "title": "ReliaQuest Endowed Professorship",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/12/2026 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States The Bellini College of AI, Cybersecurity & Computing invites applications for the ReliaQuest Endowed Professorship in AI and Cybersecurity, a senior tenured appointment at the associate professor or professor level. The University of South Florida invites applications for the ReliaQuest Endowed Professorship in AI and Cybersecurity, a senior tenured appointment at the associate professor or professor level with an anticipated start in fall 2027. This is an opportunity for an accomplished scholar to build a nationally visible program at the intersection of artificial intelligence and cybersecurity and to help shape a university-wide and regional agenda connecting research, talent development, industry, government, and national security. Why Tampa Bay, and why now: Tampa Bay offers an unusual concentration of university, industry, government, and military partners working at the convergence of AI, cybersecurity, and national security. CyberBay brings these sectors together to position the region as a national hub; its inaugural 2025 conference drew more than 800 participants, including attendees from outside Florida. The region is also home to MacDill Air Force Base, U.S. Central Command, U.S. Special Operations Command, and many mission partners. This concentration of expertise and organizations positions the successful candidate to develop durable research programs, workforce initiatives, translational partnerships, and public impact. About the Bellini College and USF: The Bellini College opened in 2025, supported by Arnie and Lauren Bellini’s $40 million gift, bringing together faculty, students and programs from the Department of Computer Science and Engineering. It serves more than 3,000 students and includes 46 tenure-track and 24 teaching faculty members, with undergraduate and graduate programs spanning AI, cybersecurity and computing. Its hub-and-spoke model connects faculty and programs across USF to develop interdisciplinary research and education. Bellini College faculty currently lead $12.8 million in active externally funded research from federal, state, and industry sources. Research infrastructure includes the shared GAIVI GPU cluster, cloud computing options through Google Cloud and Microsoft Azure, and USF’s AWS-supported Secure Research Environment incorporating GovCloud for defense and national security research, complemented by university research computing and technical support. Cyber Florida at USF, which works closely with Bellini College, provides additional opportunities for research funding and collaboration through its statewide mission to support cybersecurity research and development and its partnerships with government, industry, and defense organizations. The College houses the USF Institute for Artificial Intelligence + X, the Rapid7 Cyber Threat Intelligence Lab, and the Center for Innovation, Technology, and Aging. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities and reported $531 million in research expenditures for fiscal year 2025 Qualifications : Applicants must hold a doctorate in computer science, cybersecurity, artificial intelligence, computer engineering or a closely related field and have a record that meets USF’s requirements for appointment with tenure at the proposed rank. Candidates should demonstrate a distinguished scholarly record, sustained success in securing competitive external funding, evidence of research leadership and collaboration, and a record of teaching and mentoring appropriate for a tenure-track appointment at the associate professor or professor level. Evidence of developing collaborations across disciplines or with external partners is particularly relevant. The University of South Florida is a top-ranked research university serving approximately 50,000 students from across the globe at campuses in Tampa, St. Petersburg and USF Health. In 2025, U.S. News & World Report recognized USF with its highest overall ranking in university history, as a top 50 public university for the seventh consecutive year and as one of the top 15 best values among all public universities in the nation. U.S. News also ranks the USF Health Morsani College of Medicine in the highest tier, placing it as one of the top 16 medical schools in the nation and inside the top 10 among public universities. USF is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), a group that includes only the top 3% of universities in the U.S. With an all-time high of $750 million in research funding in 2025 and as a top 20 public university for producing U.S. patents, USF uses innovation to transform lives and shape a better future. The university generates an annual economic impact of nearly $10 billion for the state of Florida. USF’s Division I athletics teams compete in the American Conference. Learn more at www.usf.edu . The opportunity. The successful candidate will be expected to sustain a nationally recognized, externally funded research program; lead ambitious collaborative initiatives; advance innovation; strengthen and expand the cohort of early-career researchers; contribute to undergraduate and graduate education; and translate scholarship into impact through partnerships with industry, government, and community organizations. Through the stature and resources of the endowed position, the appointee will be well positioned to convene talent across USF and the region, shape new research and educational directions, mentor the next generation of scholars and leaders, and catalyze programs and partnerships with lasting impact for the Bellini College, USF, and the Tampa Bay region. Application materials: Applicants must submit a single PDF containing: (1) a cover letter describing their interest in the position and the opportunity they would pursue at USF; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) a statement of research accomplishments and future agenda, including plans for collaboration and external funding; (4) a statement of teaching and mentoring; and (5) the names and contact information of at least three references. Review timeline. For full consideration, applications should be received by 12/15/26 . Review will continue until the position is filled. Questions and confidential inquiries may be directed to the search chair Dr. Larry Hall at lohall@usf.edu."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44551": {
      "title": "Open Rank - Academic Palliative Medicine Physician",
      "description": "Closing Date: 11/04/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The Department of Internal Medicine at the University of South Florida is seeking an Open Rank Faculty member to provide Palliative Care services in an outpatient patient care setting. Appointment as a USF faculty member carries with it attending staff privileges at Tampa General Hospital (TGH) and affiliated hospitals. TGH is a level 1 trauma center and a tertiary care facility serving south central and west Florida. Palliative Care Services will be provided at the TGH Cancer Institute. Tampa General Hospital’s Cancer Institute is nationally recognized for world-class care that is revolutionizing cancer treatment and is one of Florida's few cancer centers backed by academic medicine. As a national and global leader in cancer care, TGH is accredited by the Commission on Cancer (CoC) and takes a multidisciplinary approach to delivering high-quality, patient-centered cancer care, and demonstrating a commitment to improving patient outcomes and quality of life for all cancer patients. Medical degree from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in the field of specialization with a demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Must meet university criteria for appointment to the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor. For Associate/Full Professor - Normally will have produced creative work, professional writing, or research in refereed and other professional journals, and be a recognized authority in the field of specialization. Must hold or be eligible for a full, unrestricted Florida Medical License or foreign equivalent required. To perform this position, the candidate will need to obtain and maintain a full, unrestricted FL Medical License, maintain credentials in the USF Health faculty practice plan, and be a medical staff member in good standing at the hospitals he/she is assigned to perform clinical duties. The candidate will participate in the teaching of residents, fellows, and medical students in clinical medicine. Must be Board Certified/Board Eligible in Palliative Care Medicine. Clinical: Location: Brandon Outpatient TGH Cancer Center aka Brandon Healthplex, Clinic team members: MD, APP, RN clinician, 2 MA’s, Psychologist, SW Schedule: Monday through Friday clinic. 4 clinical days per week. 1 administrative day. First patient at 8am. Last patient typically at 3:30pm. 10 patients slotted per day (7 established, 3 new). Can be more at provider discretion. Call coverage: At this time - no overnight, weekend, or holiday calls. Oncology teams provide call coverage . Teaching: Participate in didactic teaching and mentoring of medical and/or graduate students, residents, and/or post-doctoral fellows, including Hospice & Palliative Care fellows. Administrative: Additional protected time for administration, research, and/or education is consistent with holding specific leadership roles and fulfilling said responsibilities. Responsible to a Chair or other appropriate higher-level administrator of a state university. Responsible for teaching, research, service, and related administrative activities. Responsible for academic advising and related activities. May represent the university, college/school, or department/unit on university and/or Statewide committees."
    },
    "https://jobs.usf.edu/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/USF/job/44559": {
      "title": "Director, School of Physical Therapy & Rehabilitation Sciences",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/04/2027 Category: Faculty JobFunction: Professor, Asst & Assoc Prof JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Tampa, FL, United States USF Health's mission is to envision and implement the future of health. It is the partnership of the University of South Florida Morsani College of Medicine, the College of Nursing, the College of Public Health, the Taneja College of Pharmacy, the School of Biomedical Sciences and the School of Physical Therapy and Rehabilitation Sciences; and the USF Physician’s Group. USF is a global research university ranked 34th in federal research expenditures for public universities. For information regarding the USF Health, please visit our website at http://health.usf.edu/index.html The School of Physical Therapy & Rehabilitation Sciences is located within USF Health as part of the Morsani College of Medicine (MCOM). The USF Health Morsani College of Medicine enrolled its first class in 1971 and is fully accredited by the Liaison Committee for Medical Education. The college awards doctorates in Medicine (MD) and, through its School of Biomedical Sciences, PhD and MS degrees in Medical Sciences. Specially designed programs are available, including combined MD/MBA, MD/MPH, and an Honors Research program. To meet the growing demand for a workforce skilled in science and technology, MCOM provides a wide range of master’s degrees and graduate certificates in emerging fields, such as biotechnology, bioinformatics, and metabolic and nutritional medicine. The mission of the University of South Florida School of Physical Therapy & Rehabilitation Sciences is to demonstrate excellence in movement sciences through inter-professional education and evidence-based clinical practice, research and service. This mission will be accomplished by preparing doctors of physical therapy, athletic trainers, researchers, and resident trained clinicians who have a strong foundation in basic and clinical sciences, and who demonstrate excellence in contemporary evidence-based patient care. The mission will be further supported through faculty scholarship and research, and through a clinical practice that enriches the program and serves the community. The University of South Florida School of Physical Therapy & Rehabilitation Sciences, through its collaborative initiatives, will be nationally recognized for its: Innovative, integrated, and inter-professional curriculum and faculty collaboration. Highly responsible, self-directed, capable, and caring graduates who advocate for and deliver patient-centered care throughout the lifespan. In all programs, the knowledge base and clinical application will be current, evidence-based, and rich in inter-professional collaboration. Faculty who advance knowledge in athletic training and physical therapy through scholarly activity and clinical, translational research. Faculty and doctoral students will apply advances in technology for the study of clients with movement dysfunction. Faculty and graduates who demonstrate leadership in athletic training and physical therapy and at the state, national, and global levels. Faculty who are dedicated to partnership in education, specifically helping undergraduate students experience excellent education that leads to a firm understanding of the career paths in the rehabilitation sciences. A Physical Therapy Clinical Center that is an integral component of the academic program in both didactic and clinical education. The Center will be recognized for contemporary, evidence-based clinical practice, expert clinicians with specialist certification, residency programs and research in movement dysfunctions. The Director will provide leadership that drives strong operational and financial performance for the department and its practice plan, solid research productivity as measured by federally funded research, educational achievement in both Athletic Training Board of Certification (BOC) and National Physical Therapy Exam (NPTE) outcomes, and collaboration and teamwork among department faculty. The position reports directly to the Dean of the Morsani College of Medicine and Executive Vice President for USF Health, and, for practice plan and service line development, to the Chief Clinical Officer of USF Health Care. This is an exciting opportunity for an education and research leader and strong mentor who will oversee the clinical, educational, and research areas of the school with a commitment to excellence in patient care and a passion for achieving ambitious goals by embracing change and leading transformation. Minimum Qualifications: Must be an athletic trainer or physical therapist who holds a current license to practice in any United States jurisdiction and is eligible for licensure in Florida. Must have an earned academic doctoral degree or meet CAATE/CAPTE requirements for exemption. Holds the rank of associate professor, professor, clinical associate professor, or clinical professor. Strong record of peer-reviewed publications and research funding. Demonstrated ability to lead and mentor academic and clinical faculty. Minimum of six years of full-time higher education experience, including at least three years of full-time experience in an accredited professional education program. Progressive experience in a complex academic health setting and relevant experience as a clinical leader and innovator. Preferred Qualifications: History of recent extramural research funding or recruitment of funded researchers. Documented experience and accomplishments in inter-professional research and academic endeavors. The Director will provide leadership that drives strong operational and financial performance for the department and its practice plan, solid research productivity as measured by federally funded research, educational achievement in both Athletic Training Board of Certification (BOC) and National Physical Therapy Exam (NPTE) outcomes, and collaboration and teamwork among department faculty. The position reports directly to the Dean of the Morsani College of Medicine and Executive Vice President for USF Health, and, for practice plan and service line development, to the Chief Clinical Officer of USF Health Care. This is an exciting opportunity for an education and research leader and strong mentor who will oversee the clinical, educational, and research areas of the school with a commitment to excellence in patient care and a passion for achieving ambitious goals by embracing change and leading transformation."
    }
  },
